{"parentUuid":"26d584ac-e91f-4818-aadf-e88b069b39ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md","content":"---\nname: never-use-pawan-dt-identity\ndescription: \"ABSOLUTE — never use the pawan-dt account/email for commits, gh, or pushes on faucet-stream; always PawanSikawat\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\n  modified: 2026-09-17T05:49:19.120Z\n---\n\n**Never use the `pawan-dt` GitHub account or its email (`pawan@drivetrain.ai`) on the faucet-stream repo — for anything.** Not commits, not `gh` commands, not pushes. The user stated this in the strongest possible terms (2026-09-17) after finding commits authored by `pawan-dt`.\n\nCorrect identity, always:\n- git author/committer: `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>` — pinned in the repo-local config (`git config user.name/user.email`), which beats the global `pawan-dt` default. **Verify before committing.**\n- `gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat` once, then **leave it there**. Never \"switch back\" — the old CLAUDE.md step 3 that said to revert to `pawan-dt` was exactly what caused the mis-attribution, and that instruction has been removed.\n\n**Why:** `pawan-dt` is a work identity that must not appear in this personal repo's history or API calls; it also 403s on `faucet-hq` and has authored zero commits on `main`.\n\n**How to apply:** if a commit is ever authored as `pawan-dt`, reauthor before the branch is pushed — `FILTER_BRANCH_SQUELCH_WARNING=1 git filter-branch -f --env-filter '<remap both AUTHOR and COMMITTER>' origin/main..HEAD`, verify the tree is unchanged (`git diff backup HEAD` empty), then `git push --force-with-lease` (force-push needs the user's explicit approval — the safety classifier blocks it).\n\nNote the GitHub account was **renamed to `pecsorabs`** (same numeric id `35492860`), so `gh auth status` and squash-merge commits may show either name — both are this account. See [[reference_gh_auth_and_git_add_gotchas]] and [[feedback_no_claude_coauthor_trailer]].\n\n**Squash-merge trailers are a second leak path.** GitHub composes the squash commit message from the PR's commits and appends `Co-authored-by:` for every distinct author, so a branch that ever held a commit from the work identity taints the merged commit body on `main` even after the branch is reauthored — and GitHub caches that suggested message when the merge box is first rendered, so a later reauthor does not clear it. This happened to #650 and #653. **Always merge with an explicit message** (`gh pr merge N --squash --subject \"<title>\" --body \"<text>\"`), never the auto-generated one, and verify after landing with `git log -1 --format='%B' origin/main | grep -i co-authored`.\n","numLines":24,"startLine":1,"totalLines":24}},"displayPath":"../../../../.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_never_use_pawan_dt_identity.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"db2ee859-a460-4bc1-9262-9a35fdc34d1e","timestamp":"2026-09-17T12:50:40.204Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.231","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
