{"parentUuid":"019c26da-c5ac-4ccb-9000-f6e65497ad24","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"1e50a2b8-f79b-4f2b-a79b-e532971b731e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018mxyMN97d1Thqu5Ghhm11p","type":"tool_result","content":"/// Extract an i32 partition. Errors on non-integer matches or out-of-range values.\npub fn partition_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<i32>, FaucetError> {\n    let Some(v) = first_match(record, path)? else {\n        return Ok(None);\n    };\n    match v.as_i64() {\n        Some(n) if n >= 0 && n <= i32::MAX as i64 => Ok(Some(n as i32)),\n        Some(n) => Err(FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"partition_path '{path}' resolved to out-of-range {n}\"\n        ))),\n        None => Err(FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"partition_path '{path}' did not resolve to an integer\"\n        ))),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Extract a headers map. The path must resolve to a JSON object;\n/// non-string values are stringified.\npub fn headers_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<Map<String, Value>>, FaucetError> {\n    let Some(v) = first_match(record, path)? else {\n        return Ok(None);\n    };\n    let obj = v.as_object().ok_or_else(|| {\n        FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"headers_path '{path}' did not resolve to a JSON object\"\n        ))\n    })?;\n    let mut out = Map::new();\n    for (k, val) in obj {\n        let s = match val {\n            Value::String(s) => s.clone(),\n            other => other.to_string(),\n        };\n        out.insert(k.clone(), Value::String(s));\n    }\n    Ok(Some(out))\n}\n\n/// Resolve a JSONPath against `record` and return the first matching JSON value.\npub fn value_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<Value>, FaucetError> {\n    first_match(record, path)","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"b2a68355-e70d-4362-8286-defaab6eedd4","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:05:21.051Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/// Extract an i32 partition. Errors on non-integer matches or out-of-range values.\npub fn partition_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<i32>, FaucetError> {\n    let Some(v) = first_match(record, path)? else {\n        return Ok(None);\n    };\n    match v.as_i64() {\n        Some(n) if n >= 0 && n <= i32::MAX as i64 => Ok(Some(n as i32)),\n        Some(n) => Err(FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"partition_path '{path}' resolved to out-of-range {n}\"\n        ))),\n        None => Err(FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"partition_path '{path}' did not resolve to an integer\"\n        ))),\n    }\n}\n\n/// Extract a headers map. The path must resolve to a JSON object;\n/// non-string values are stringified.\npub fn headers_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<Map<String, Value>>, FaucetError> {\n    let Some(v) = first_match(record, path)? else {\n        return Ok(None);\n    };\n    let obj = v.as_object().ok_or_else(|| {\n        FaucetError::Sink(format!(\n            \"headers_path '{path}' did not resolve to a JSON object\"\n        ))\n    })?;\n    let mut out = Map::new();\n    for (k, val) in obj {\n        let s = match val {\n            Value::String(s) => s.clone(),\n            other => other.to_string(),\n        };\n        out.insert(k.clone(), Value::String(s));\n    }\n    Ok(Some(out))\n}\n\n/// Resolve a JSONPath against `record` and return the first matching JSON value.\npub fn value_at(record: &Value, path: &str) -> Result<Option<Value>, FaucetError> {\n    first_match(record, path)","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"019c26da-c5ac-4ccb-9000-f6e65497ad24","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"b2a68355-e70d-4362-8286-defaab6eedd4","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_018mxyMN97d1Thqu5Ghhm11p","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":674},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c719cd14-702a-4846-a9c2-42fb0a64f070","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:05:21.051Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"c719cd14-702a-4846-a9c2-42fb0a64f070","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14926116 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"72d5f1ef-4bd7-4edb-818e-5c6581e0b1a5","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:05:21.065Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14926116 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"72d5f1ef-4bd7-4edb-818e-5c6581e0b1a5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf992CdMoBi3tmzVM5ScV","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01R8he3E8Nma76eZVM99tGwd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh issue create \\\n  --title \"bug(sink-kafka): \\`headers_path\\` is parsed and extracted but never attached to the produced message\" \\\n  --label bug --label tier-2 \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Summary\n\n`KafkaSinkConfig::headers_path` is accepted by the config, has a tested\nextraction helper (`extract::headers_at`), and is documented as producing Kafka\nmessage headers — but **the produce path never attaches the result to the\noutgoing message.** `rdkafka::message::OwnedHeaders` is never constructed\nanywhere in the crate, and `headers_at` has no caller outside its own tests:\n\n```\n$ grep -rn \"headers_path\\|OwnedHeaders\\|\\.headers(\" crates/sink/kafka/src/\ncrates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs:77:    pub headers_path: Option<String>,\ncrates/sink/kafka/src/extract.rs:54:  \"headers_path '{path}' did not resolve to a JSON object\"\n# (the other two hits are `headers_path: None` in test fixtures)\n```\n\nSo a user who sets `headers_path` gets a silently inert switch: validation\npasses, the run succeeds, and the headers they configured never reach the\nbroker. The field's doc comment has been amended to say so\n(`**Not yet applied:** …`) so the docs no longer overclaim, but the honest fix\nis to wire it up.\n\n## Motivation\n\nTies to the Primary Goal (reliability/correctness). A config field that is\naccepted and then ignored is the worst shape of configuration bug: there is no\nerror, no warning, and no metric — the operator discovers it downstream when a\nconsumer routing on a header sees none. Kafka headers are how consumers do\ntenant routing, trace propagation, schema hints, and dead-letter annotation, so\nthe silent gap is load-bearing for real deployments.\n\nIt is also a direct instance of PRINCIPLES §5 (no hidden state) and the\n\"config is an API\" principle: every accepted key must have an observable\neffect or be rejected.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nIn the per-record produce path in `crates/sink/kafka/src/sink.rs`, where the\nkey and partition are already resolved from `key_path` / `partition_path`:\n\n1. Call `extract::headers_at(record, path)` when `config.headers_path` is\n   `Some`.\n2. Convert the returned `Map<String, Value>` into `OwnedHeaders`, inserting\n   each entry with `rdkafka::message::Header { key, value: Some(&str) }`.\n   Every value is already stringified by `headers_at`.\n3. Attach with `FutureRecord::headers(owned)`.\n4. Do the same on the **exactly-once** path in\n   `crates/sink/kafka/src/idempotent.rs`, so a transactional produce carries\n   the same headers as a plain one. The commit-token record itself must NOT\n   carry record headers — it is faucet's own watermark, not user data.\n5. Decide and document the failure policy for a `headers_path` that does not\n   resolve to an object. `headers_at` already returns\n   `Err(FaucetError::Sink(..))`, which fails the batch; that is consistent\n   with `partition_path` and is the right default. A path that resolves to\n   *nothing* returns `Ok(None)` (no headers) — also correct, and it should\n   stay that way rather than growing an `on_headers_error` knob.\n\n### Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/sink.rs` — the plain produce path (attach headers).\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/idempotent.rs` — the transactional produce path.\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs` — drop the `**Not yet applied:**`\n  paragraph from the `headers_path` doc once it is wired.\n- `crates/sink/kafka/README.md` — the `headers_path` row, currently silent on\n  the gap.\n- `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` if it mentions Kafka headers.\n\n## Edge cases & failure modes\n\n- **Header value is `null`** — `headers_at` stringifies it to `\"null\"`. Kafka\n  headers permit a null value; decide whether `null` should mean \"absent\n  value\" (`Header { value: None }`) rather than the four-character string.\n  Preference: emit `value: None`, and pin it with a test.\n- **Empty object** at the path — attach no headers rather than an empty\n  `OwnedHeaders`.\n- **Duplicate keys** — impossible from a JSON object, so no ordering question.\n- **Non-UTF-8** — cannot arise; values come from JSON strings.\n- **Large headers** — headers count against `message.max.bytes`; a very large\n  extracted object can make an otherwise-fine record unproducible. The\n  resulting librdkafka error should surface as-is (it names the limit), so no\n  extra guard is needed, but it deserves a line in the README.\n- **Interaction with `value_format: confluent_*`** — headers are independent\n  of the value encoder; no interaction, worth one test to pin it.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [ ] A record produced with `headers_path` set carries exactly the extracted\n      entries as Kafka headers, asserted end-to-end in the existing\n      Docker-backed integration test (consume the message back and read its\n      headers).\n- [ ] Unit tests for the `Map` → `OwnedHeaders` conversion, including the\n      `null`-value decision and the empty-object case.\n- [ ] The exactly-once path attaches headers too, and the commit-token record\n      does not.\n- [ ] A `headers_path` resolving to a non-object fails the batch with a typed\n      `FaucetError::Sink` naming the path (already the helper's behaviour —\n      pin it from the sink's side).\n- [ ] The `**Not yet applied:**` doc paragraph is removed and the README\n      documents the behaviour.\n- [ ] ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- A `headers_map`-style literal/static header block (no extraction) — separate\n  feature if wanted.\n- Reading headers on the **source** side (`faucet-source-kafka` already\n  surfaces them).\n- An `on_headers_error` policy knob; fail-the-batch is the right default and\n  adding a knob for it is speculative.\n\n## References\n\n- Surfaced while auditing the repo against PRINCIPLES.md (#654) — this one is a\n  real behavioural bug rather than a principles violation, so it is filed\n  separately instead of being folded into that issue.\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/extract.rs::headers_at` — the existing, tested helper.\n- Roadmap epic #38.\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"File the kafka headers_path bug"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":883,"cache_read_input_tokens":278841,"output_tokens":2385,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":883,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2385,"cache_read_input_tokens":278841,"cache_creation_input_tokens":883,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":883},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01R8he3E8Nma76eZVM99tGwd":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh issue create \\\n  --title \"bug(sink-kafka): \\`headers_path\\` is parsed and extracted but never attached to the produced message\" \\\n  --label bug --label tier-2 \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\n## Summary\n\n`KafkaSinkConfig::headers_path` is accepted by the config, has a tested\nextraction helper (`extract::headers_at`), and is documented as producing Kafka\nmessage headers — but **the produce path never attaches the result to the\noutgoing message.** `rdkafka::message::OwnedHeaders` is never constructed\nanywhere in the crate, and `headers_at` has no caller outside its own tests:\n\n```\n$ grep -rn \"headers_path\\|OwnedHeaders\\|\\.headers(\" crates/sink/kafka/src/\ncrates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs:77:    pub headers_path: Option<String>,\ncrates/sink/kafka/src/extract.rs:54:  \"headers_path '{path}' did not resolve to a JSON object\"\n# (the other two hits are `headers_path: None` in test fixtures)\n```\n\nSo a user who sets `headers_path` gets a silently inert switch: validation\npasses, the run succeeds, and the headers they configured never reach the\nbroker. The field's doc comment has been amended to say so\n(`**Not yet applied:** …`) so the docs no longer overclaim, but the honest fix\nis to wire it up.\n\n## Motivation\n\nTies to the Primary Goal (reliability/correctness). A config field that is\naccepted and then ignored is the worst shape of configuration bug: there is no\nerror, no warning, and no metric — the operator discovers it downstream when a\nconsumer routing on a header sees none. Kafka headers are how consumers do\ntenant routing, trace propagation, schema hints, and dead-letter annotation, so\nthe silent gap is load-bearing for real deployments.\n\nIt is also a direct instance of PRINCIPLES §5 (no hidden state) and the\n\"config is an API\" principle: every accepted key must have an observable\neffect or be rejected.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nIn the per-record produce path in `crates/sink/kafka/src/sink.rs`, where the\nkey and partition are already resolved from `key_path` / `partition_path`:\n\n1. Call `extract::headers_at(record, path)` when `config.headers_path` is\n   `Some`.\n2. Convert the returned `Map<String, Value>` into `OwnedHeaders`, inserting\n   each entry with `rdkafka::message::Header { key, value: Some(&str) }`.\n   Every value is already stringified by `headers_at`.\n3. Attach with `FutureRecord::headers(owned)`.\n4. Do the same on the **exactly-once** path in\n   `crates/sink/kafka/src/idempotent.rs`, so a transactional produce carries\n   the same headers as a plain one. The commit-token record itself must NOT\n   carry record headers — it is faucet's own watermark, not user data.\n5. Decide and document the failure policy for a `headers_path` that does not\n   resolve to an object. `headers_at` already returns\n   `Err(FaucetError::Sink(..))`, which fails the batch; that is consistent\n   with `partition_path` and is the right default. A path that resolves to\n   *nothing* returns `Ok(None)` (no headers) — also correct, and it should\n   stay that way rather than growing an `on_headers_error` knob.\n\n### Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/sink.rs` — the plain produce path (attach headers).\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/idempotent.rs` — the transactional produce path.\n- `crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs` — drop the `**Not yet applied:**`\n  paragraph from the `headers_path` doc once it is wired.\n- `crates/sink/kafka/README.md` — the `headers_path` row, currently silent on\n  the gap.\n- `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` if it mentions Kafka headers.\n\n## Edge cases & failure modes\n\n- **Header value is `null`** — `headers_at` stringifies it to `\"null\"`. Kafka\n  headers permit a null value; decide whether `null` should mean \"absent\n  value\" (`Header { value: None }`) rather than the four-character string.\n  Preference: emit `value: None`, and pin it with a test.\n- **Empty object** at the path — attach no headers rather than an empty\n  `OwnedHeaders`.\n- **Duplicate keys** — impossible from a JSON object, so no ordering question.\n- **Non-UTF-8** — cannot arise; values come from JSON strings.\n- **Large headers** — headers count against `message.max.bytes`; a very large\n  extracted object can make an otherwise-fine record unproducible. The\n  resulting librdkafka error should surface as-is (it names the limit), so no\n  extra guard is needed, but it deserves a line in the README.\n- **Interaction with `value_format: confluent_*`** — headers are