{"parentUuid":"9e9b7ac1-b350-42d6-9d3a-e8361c380c64","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf99oqyfrAwgQGW6QeHnS","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01CRrGmDWWr7j5HEHYwtm4Ah","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngh pr merge 656 --disable-auto 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr merge 656 --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"fix: replace every message-grep classification with a typed one, and close the core retry gate (#656)\" \\\n  --body \"Closes the non-breaking half of the principles audit (#654).\n\nCore: with_retry_write! was gated on supports_idempotent_writes(), which only\npromises atomicity on the *idempotent* write path — eleven sinks advertise it\nwhile their plain write is a bare multi-row INSERT, so the macro retried\nexactly the writes its own comment forbids. Now gated on a defaulted\nSink::write_batch_is_replay_safe().\n\nTyped classification replaces string matching in nine places: delta\nmissing-table (a 403 read as 'no table' orphaned every data file), spanner\nexactly-once watermark, mssql transience (a UNIQUE-constraint name containing\n'connection' was called transient, so the poison row never reached the DLQ),\nthe scheduler's circuit-open cooldown, run-history backend transience, graphql\nrequest rejection, and the parquet arrow decoder.\n\nAlso: one jitter implementation across five retry sites (the websocket\nreconnect had no ceiling at all and redialled a dead endpoint forever);\nreserved names get one definition each; sql_literal is public with its ANSI\ncontract stated and ClickHouse documents why it must diverge; the XML decoder\nno longer panics on unbalanced network input; deny_unknown_fields on the five\nconfig blocks still missing it.\n\nAddresses #654\" 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"=== verify:\"; gh pr view 656 --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest | {headline: .commitHeadline, bodyStart: (.commitBody[0:60])}'","description":"Disable then re-arm auto-merge with the explicit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_read_input_tokens":300995,"output_tokens":1078,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":318},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":839,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1078,"cache_read_input_tokens":300995,"cache_creation_input_tokens":839,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":839},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01CRrGmDWWr7j5HEHYwtm4Ah":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngh pr merge 656 --disable-auto 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr merge 656 --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"fix: replace every message-grep classification with a typed one, and close the core retry gate (#656)\" \\\n  --body \"Closes the non-breaking half of the principles audit (#654).\n\nCore: with_retry_write! was gated on supports_idempotent_writes(), which only\npromises atomicity on the *idempotent* write path — eleven sinks advertise it\nwhile their plain write is a bare multi-row INSERT, so the macro retried\nexactly the writes its own comment forbids. Now gated on a defaulted\nSink::write_batch_is_replay_safe().\n\nTyped classification replaces string matching in nine places: delta\nmissing-table (a 403 read as 'no table' orphaned every data file), spanner\nexactly-once watermark, mssql transience (a UNIQUE-constraint name containing\n'connection' was called transient, so the poison row never reached the DLQ),\nthe scheduler's circuit-open cooldown, run-history backend transience, graphql\nrequest rejection, and the parquet arrow decoder.\n\nAlso: one jitter implementation across five retry sites (the websocket\nreconnect had no ceiling at all and redialled a dead endpoint forever);\nreserved names get one definition each; sql_literal is public with its ANSI\ncontract stated and ClickHouse documents why it must diverge; the XML decoder\nno longer panics on unbalanced network input; deny_unknown_fields on the five\nconfig blocks still missing it.\n\nAddresses #654\" 2>&1 | tail -2\necho \"=== verify:\"; gh pr view 656 --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest | {headline: .commitHeadline, bodyStart: (.commitBody[0:60])}'","description":"Disable then re-arm auto-merge with the explicit message"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf99oqDmgRmpyKr7cFVzL","type":"assistant","uuid":"9597f499-7bb9-48f4-a2fd-3a8cd99479ba","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:15:52.035Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
