{"parentUuid":"2d83a304-df21-4678-9a57-1d9193c8133b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9CsNho318iEEpe7qp4h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"CI still running. I'll hold this locally rather than push and restart the in-flight Coverage run — one follow-up commit can carry the extraction plus whatever CI flags:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":337854,"output_tokens":902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":214},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":337854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf9CsLh18r4Gr8oNJFpFY","type":"assistant","uuid":"459e7ab0-f4e3-4f5a-a88a-c9033a054d61","timestamp":"2026-09-17T14:55:54.024Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-correctness-paths","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"459e7ab0-f4e3-4f5a-a88a-c9033a054d61","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9CsNho318iEEpe7qp4h","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01SkrMsfWetjiiZ5U8XE7wmq","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -u && git commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nrefactor(graphql): lift the whole 200-with-errors decision out of the fetch path\n\n`classify_graphql_errors` was pure and fully tested, but the 17 lines that\n*used* it — deriving the sentinel page-size variable, composing the hint, and\npicking the `FaucetError` variant — sat inside the async fetch method, so every\none of those branches was reachable only through a live HTTP round-trip.\n\nExtracts two pure functions (`sentinel_page_size_variable`,\n`graphql_error_from_payload`) and leaves the fetch path a single call. Six unit\ntests now pin what previously needed wiremock: the transport/config split, the\nendpoint and joined message, hint-only-when-the-sentinel-is-live, a config code\ncomposing with the hint, offset pagination never yielding a sentinel variable,\nand an error payload carrying no `message` field at all.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged — this is the \"extract the pure logic rather than declare\nit untestable\" move the coverage policy asks for (PRINCIPLES §7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the graphql extraction locally","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_read_input_tokens":337854,"output_tokens":902,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":214},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":902,"cache_read_input_tokens":337854,"cache_creation_input_tokens":819,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":819},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01SkrMsfWetjiiZ5U8XE7wmq":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -u && git commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nrefactor(graphql): lift the whole 200-with-errors decision out of the fetch path\n\n`classify_graphql_errors` was pure and fully tested, but the 17 lines that\n*used* it — deriving the sentinel page-size variable, composing the hint, and\npicking the `FaucetError` variant — sat inside the async fetch method, so every\none of those branches was reachable only through a live HTTP round-trip.\n\nExtracts two pure functions (`sentinel_page_size_variable`,\n`graphql_error_from_payload`) and leaves the fetch path a single call. Six unit\ntests now pin what previously needed wiremock: the transport/config split, the\nendpoint and joined message, hint-only-when-the-sentinel-is-live, a config code\ncomposing with the hint, offset pagination never yielding a sentinel variable,\nand an error payload carrying no `message` field at all.\n\nBehaviour is unchanged — this is the \"extract the pure logic rather than declare\nit untestable\" move the coverage policy asks for (PRINCIPLES §7).\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the graphql extraction locally","timeout":300000}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011Cf9CsLh18r4Gr8oNJFpFY","type":"assistant","uuid":"6672c202-14a4-