{"parentUuid":"47464e81-bb07-4a55-996f-d985a4f558a6","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"7f18b2ae-41bd-4c93-ada1-530037b42da9","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VuVspceZsMSyVn3amjioQt","type":"tool_result","content":"24:/// Field the conformance battery uses to flag a record as a delete when\n25:/// exercising an upsert sink's delete path. Aliases the `cdc_unwrap` marker\n26:/// default rather than re-spelling it, so the battery can never assert against\n27:/// a field the real transform stopped stamping (#654 M17). A sink under test\n28:/// must be configured with a `delete_marker { field: \"__op\", values: [\"d\"] }`\n29:/// for the delete branch of\n30:/// [`assert_write_modes_truthful`](crate::assert_write_modes_truthful) to run.\n32:/// Value of [`DELETE_MARKER_FIELD`] that means \"this record is a delete\".\n35:/// A source that lazily emits `total` synthetic records (`{\"n\": i}`) in pages of\n36:/// its configured `batch` (or the `stream_pages` hint), **without** buffering\n37:/// the whole set — so it exercises the bounded-memory contract genuinely.\n38:///\n39:/// It also honours incremental resume: after `stream_pages` runs to completion\n40:/// it emits a `{\"n\": total}` bookmark; feeding that back via\n41:/// [`apply_start_bookmark`](Source::apply_start_bookmark) makes the next run\n42:/// start at that offset (so a fully-consumed source resumes to zero records).\n43:/// Construct with [`CountingSource::non_resumable`] to model a source that\n44:/// *ignores* the bookmark — used to prove the bookmark-roundtrip check fails.\n45:pub struct CountingSource {\n76:impl Source for CountingSource {\n138:/// A source whose read path always returns a typed [`FaucetError`] — models an\n139:/// unreachable endpoint / bad credentials. Used to prove the\n140:/// `errors-not-panics` check passes on a well-behaved failure.\n141:pub struct FailingSource;\n144:impl Source for FailingSource {\n159:/// A source whose read path **panics** — models a buggy connector that unwraps\n160:/// on unexpected input. Used to prove the `errors-not-panics` check *fails*\n161:/// (catches the unwind) rather than letting the panic escape silently.\n162:pub struct PanickingSource;\n165:impl Source for PanickingSource {\n178:/// A sink that records everything written, optionally deduplicating by a key\n179:/// field (upsert), optionally advertising the atomic-watermark idempotent path.\n180:///\n181:/// Modes:\n182:/// - [`TestSink::new`] — append-only, non-idempotent.\n183:/// - [`TestSink::keyed`] — dedups by key on `write_batch` (keyed-upsert /\n184:///   `dedups_by_key`), advertises `Upsert`/`Delete`.\n185:/// - [`TestSink::keyed_upsert`] — like `keyed`, but also honours a delete\n186:///   marker (`{\"__op\": \"d\"}`) so a delete-marked record genuinely *removes* the\n187:///   keyed row — used to exercise the delete path of\n188:///   [`assert_write_modes_truthful`](crate::assert_write_modes_truthful).\n189:/// - [`TestSink::idempotent`] — additionally advertises\n190:///   `supports_idempotent_writes` and stores a per-scope commit token, so the\n191:///   atomic-watermark path can be exercised.\n193:pub struct TestSink {\n275:impl Sink for TestSink {\n344:/// A sink that **claims** `supports_idempotent_writes` but does not actually\n345:/// store a commit token (it just appends). Used to prove the idempotent-replay\n346:/// and capabilities checks *fail* against a lying sink.\n348:pub struct LyingIdempotentSink {\n=== lines:\n    1033 crates/conformance/src/doubles.rs\n    1387 crates/conformance/src/lib.rs\n    2420 total","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"88013bbf-5729-47aa-89f4-db0359412c6b","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:20:41.790Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"24:/// Field the conformance battery uses to flag a record as a delete when\n25:/// exercising an upsert sink's delete path. Aliases the `cdc_unwrap` marker\n26:/// default rather than re-spelling it, so the battery can never assert against\n27:/// a field the real transform stopped stamping (#654 M17). A sink under test\n28:/// must be configured with a `delete_marker { field: \"__op\", values: [\"d\"] }`\n29:/// for the delete branch of\n30:/// [`assert_write_modes_truthful`](crate::assert_write_modes_truthful) to run.\n32:/// Value of [`DELETE_MARKER_FIELD`] that means \"this record is a delete\".\n35:/// A source that lazily emits `total` synthetic records (`{\"n\": i}`) in pages of\n36:/// its configured `batch` (or the `stream_pages` hint), **without** buffering\n37:/// the whole set — so it exercises the bounded-memory contract genuinely.\n38:///\n39:/// It also honours incremental resume: after `stream_pages` runs to completion\n40:/// it emits a `{\"n\": total}` bookmark; feeding that back via\n41:/// [`apply_start_bookmark`](Source::apply_start_bookmark) makes the next run\n42:/// start at that offset (so a fully-consumed source resumes to zero records).\n43:/// Construct with [`CountingSource::non_resumable`] to model a source that\n44:/// *ignores* the bookmark — used to prove the bookmark-roundtrip check fails.\n45:pub struct CountingSource {\n76:impl Source for CountingSource {\n138:/// A source whose read path always returns a typed [`FaucetError`] — models an\n139:/// unreachable endpoint / bad credentials. Used to prove the\n140:/// `errors-not-panics` check passes on a well-behaved failure.\n141:pub struct FailingSource;\n144:impl Source for FailingSource {\n159:/// A source whose read path **panics** — models a buggy connector that unwraps\n160:/// on unexpected input. Used to prove the `errors-not-panics` check *fails*\n161:/// (catches the unwind) rather than letting the panic escape silently.\n162:pub struct PanickingSource;\n165:impl Source for PanickingSource {\n178:/// A sink that records everything written, optionally deduplicating by a key\n179:/// field (upsert), optionally advertising the atomic-watermark idempotent path.\n180:///\n181:/// Modes:\n182:/// - [`TestSink::new`] — append-only, non-idempotent.\n183:/// - [`TestSink::keyed`] — dedups by key on `write_batch` (keyed-upsert /\n184:///   `dedups_by_key`), advertises `Upsert`/`Delete`.\n185:/// - [`TestSink::keyed_upsert`] — like `keyed`, but also honours a delete\n186:///   marker (`{\"__op\": \"d\"}`) so a delete-marked record genuinely *removes* the\n187:///   keyed row — used to exercise the delete path of\n188:///   [`assert_write_modes_truthful`](crate::assert_write_modes_truthful).\n189:/// - [`TestSink::idempotent`] — additionally advertises\n190:///   `supports_idempotent_writes` and stores a per-scope commit token, so the\n191:///   atomic-watermark path can be exercised.\n193:pub struct TestSink {\n275:impl Sink for TestSink {\n344:/// A sink that **claims** `supports_idempotent_writes` but does not actually\n345:/// store a commit token (it just appends). Used to prove the idempotent-replay\n346:/// and capabilities checks *fail* against a lying sink.\n348:pub struct LyingIdempotentSink {\n=== lines:\n    1033 crates/conformance/src/doubles.rs\n    1387 crates/conformance/src/lib.rs\n    2420 total","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"47464e81-bb07-4a55-996f-d985a4f558a6","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
