overwrite` succeeded.\n51\t    BeginOverwrite,\n52\t    /// `commit_overwrite` succeeded — the atomic swap actually happened.\n53\t    CommitOverwrite,\n54\t    /// `abort_overwrite` succeeded — the staged data was discarded.\n55\t    AbortOverwrite,\n56\t    /// `StateStore::put` succeeded for `key`, carrying the persisted value so a\n57\t    /// test can assert *which* bookmark was durable at that point.\n58\t    StatePut { key: String, value: Value },\n59\t    /// A `StateStore::put` was attempted and the script failed it.\n60\t    StatePutFailed { key: String },\n61\t    /// `cleanup_scope` ran with this many tracked keys.\n62\t    Cleanup(usize),\n63\t}\n64\t\n65\t/// The shared, ordered event log. Clone it to keep a handle after the doubles\n66\t/// are moved into the pipeline.\n67\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, Default)]\n68\tpub struct EventLog(Arc<Mutex<Vec<Event>>>);\n69\t\n70\timpl EventLog {\n71\t    /// A fresh, empty log.\n72\t    pub fn new() -> Self {\n73\t        Self::default()\n74\t    }\n75\t\n76\t    /// Append one event. Never blocks on a poisoned lock — a panicking test\n77\t    /// should fail on its own assertion, not on a secondary lock panic.\n78\t    pub fn push(&self, event: Event) {\n79\t        if let Ok(mut g) = self.0.lock() {\n80\t            g.push(event);\n81\t        }\n82\t    }\n83\t\n84\t    /// Every event, in order.\n85\t    pub fn events(&self) -> Vec<Event> {\n86\t        self.0.lock().map(|g| g.clone()).unwrap_or_default()\n87\t    }\n88\t\n89\t    /// Total records across successful writes of every kind.\n90\t    pub fn records_written(&self) -> usize {\n91\t        self.events()\n92\t            .iter()\n93\t            .map(|e| match e {\n94\t                Event::Write(n) | Event::IdempotentWrite { records: n, .. } => *n,\n95\t                _ => 0,\n96\t            })\n97\t            .sum()\n98\t    }\n99\t\n100\t    /// The values persisted by `StateStore::put`, in order.\n101\t    pub fn bookmarks(&self) -> Vec<Value> {\n102\t        self.events()\n103\t            .iter()\n104\t            .filter_map(|e| match e {\n105\t                Event::StatePut { value, .. } => Some(value.clone()),\n106\t                _ => None,\n107\t            })\n108\t            .collect()\n109\t    }\n110\t\n111\t    /// For each successful `StateStore::put`, how many records had been\n112\t    /// **confirmed written** before it.\n113\t    ///\n114\t    /// This is the shape the core durability guarantee is stated in: a bookmark\n115\t    /// must never be persisted covering data the sink has not confirmed. A test\n116\t    /// asserts the returned counts against the data each bookmark claims.\n117\t    pub fn writes_before_each_bookmark(&self) -> Vec<usize> {\n118\t        let mut confirmed = 0usize;\n119\t        let mut out = Vec::new();\n120\t        for e in self.events() {\n121\t            match e {\n122\t                Event::Write(n) | Event::IdempotentWrite { records: n, .. } => confirmed += n,\n123\t                Event::StatePut { .. } => out.push(confirmed),\n124\t                _ => {}\n125\t            }\n126\t        }\n127\t        out\n128\t    }\n129\t\n130\t    /// Whether `event` occurs anywhere in the log.\n131\t    pub fn contains(&self, event: &Event) -> bool {\n132\t        self.events().iter().any(|e| e == event)\n133\t    }\n134\t\n135\t    /// Whether any event matches `pred` — for variants carrying a payload a\n136\t    /// test does not want to spell out in full.\n137\t    pub fn any(&self, pred: impl Fn(&Event) -> bool) -> bool {\n138\t        self.events().iter().any(pred)\n139\t    }\n140\t\n141\t    /// Index of the first event matching `pred`, for order assertions.\n142\t    pub fn position(&self, pred: impl Fn(&Event) -> bool) -> Option<usize> {\n143\t        self.events().iter().position(pred)\n144\t    }\n145\t}\n146\t\n147\t/// The boundary a script fails at.\n148\t///\n149\t/// Every variant names a real transition the engine makes, and each one is a\n150\t/// place a naive implementation gets the ordering wrong.\n151\t#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq, Default)]\n152\tpub enum Boundary {\n153\t    /// Never fail — the control arm every failure test needs for comparison.\n154\t    #[default]\n155\t    Never,\n156\t    /// Fail the write of the (0-indexed) `nth` batch. Batches before and after\n157\t    /// it succeed, so the test observes a *partial* run rather than a total\n158\t    /// one.\n159\t    Write(usize),\n160\t    /// Fail `flush`. The writes themselves succeeded, so this is the case where\n161\t    /// the sink accepted rows it cannot guarantee are durable — the bookmark\n162\t    /// must not advance.\n163\t    Flush,\n164\t    /// Fail the (0-indexed) `nth` `StateStore::put`. Models a crash in the\n165\t    /// window between a confirmed sink write and a durable bookmark: on resume\n166\t    /// the pipeline must re-read, producing duplicates under at-least-once and\n167\t    /// none under exactly-once.\n168\t    StatePut(usize),\n169\t    /// Fail `commit_overwrite` — the atomic swap itself. The prior destination\n170\t    /// must survive.\n171\t    CommitOverwrite,\n172\t}\n173\t\n174\t/// Shared script state behind a [`ScriptedSink`] / [`ScriptedStateStore`].\n175\t#[derive(Debug)]\n176\tstruct Script {\n177\t    boundary: Boundary,\n178\t    writes: usize,\n179\t    state_puts: usize,\n180\t}\n181\t\n182\t/// A sink that logs every call into a shared [`EventLog`] and fails at exactly\n183\t/// one [`Boundary`].\n184\t///\n185\t/// Capability advertisement is configurable because several guarantees are\n186\t/// *about* the advertisement: the retry gate keys off\n187\t/// [`Sink::write_batch_is_replay_safe`], and the exactly-once path off\n188\t/// [`Sink::supports_idempotent_writes`]. A test that wants to prove the engine\n\n... [493 lines truncated] ...\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-