{"parentUuid":"24343e5f-8b88-45d3-ba1b-e10221b9fadc","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14902336 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9f7ef205-cbc6-446e-92e1-6943b43f3c61","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:32:57.365Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14902336 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/cover-pure-decisions","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"9f7ef205-cbc6-446e-92e1-6943b43f3c61","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9tJeUp75EDJVoLfMtv1","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01WzwrgzvcVwH8Y4muQKNy66","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(conformance): engine-level reliability harness + Category A suites\n\nFirst phase of the integration-test program (#651). Adds the two shared\nfoundations the program is built on, then the Category A suites that use them.\n\n`scripted` — boundary-precise failure injection. The engine's guarantees are\nall statements about the *order* in which it calls two collaborators\n(\"the bookmark is persisted only after the sink confirms\"), which no pure-logic\nunit test can observe. Every such test previously hand-rolled its own\n`FailingSink` that failed on *every* call, so the interesting case — fail on the\nthird write, succeed either side — went untested. Supplies one shared ordered\n`EventLog` plus a `ScriptedSink`/`ScriptedStateStore` pair that fail at exactly\none named `Boundary` and behave normally elsewhere, and a `PagedSource` that\nbookmarks every page so writes and bookmarks actually interleave.\n\n`fidelity` — the shared typed round-trip corpus (Category F groundwork). Owns\nthe hazard classes centrally (i64 past 2^53, -0.0, embedded quotes and\nbackslashes, empty strings, tz offsets, pre-epoch instants, nested JSON) so a\npair's test cannot quietly pick an easier corpus, and matches rows by key so a\nreordering destination is not penalised. `Tolerance` makes each allowance an\nexplicit statement about a destination limitation rather than a loose compare.\n\nCategory A suites (23 tests, all against the real `Pipeline::run`):\n\n- A1 bookmark ordering — every bookmark is backed by confirmed writes; a failed\n  write, a failed flush, and a failed state-put each leave the durable bookmark\n  behind the failure; resume re-reads exactly the unconfirmed tail with no gap\n  and at most one page of duplicates.\n- A2 exactly-once, both mechanisms — writes route through the idempotent path\n  with monotonic distinct tokens; a crash in the commit→state-put window\n  replays nothing; a re-run of a completed pipeline writes nothing; a failed\n  idempotent write leaves no token to skip on; the keyed mechanism converges\n  with no watermark at all. Includes a side-by-side control proving that under\n  the *identical* injected failure at-least-once does duplicate — without it\n  the exactly-once assertions would not be distinguishing the two modes.\n- A3 overwrite atomicity — begin precedes the first write and commit follows the\n  last; a failed write, a failed flush, and a cancel each abort without ever\n  swapping; a failing commit surfaces instead of reporting success; a suppressed\n  lifecycle leaves every phase to the caller (#552).\n- A8 cancel still flushes — a cancelled run flushes what it accepted and claims\n  no more than it flushed; an already-cancelled run writes and claims nothing.\n\nPer the issue's acceptance criteria, the durability guarantee is asserted\nthrough a shared helper that is itself proven capable of failing: three\n`#[should_panic]` tests feed it deliberately-wrong event logs (bookmark before\nwrite, bookmark overclaiming after a partial write).\n\nRefs #651\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'","description":"Commit phase 1"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_read_input_tokens":474661,"output_tokens":1245,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1245,"cache_read_input_tokens":474661,"cache_creation_input_tokens":388,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":388},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01WzwrgzvcVwH8Y4muQKNy66":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(conformance): engine-level reliability harness + Category A suites\n\nFirst phase of the integration-test program (#651). Adds the two shared\nfoundations the program is built on, then the Category A suites that use them.\n\n`scripted` — boundary-precise failure injection. The engine's guarantees are\nall statements about the *order* in which it calls two collaborators\n(\"the bookmark is persisted only after the sink confirms\"), which no pure-logic\nunit test can observe. Every such test previously hand-rolled its own\n`FailingSink` that failed on *every* call, so the interesting case — fail on the\nthird write, succeed either side — went untested. Supplies one shared ordered\n`EventLog` plus a `ScriptedSink`/`ScriptedStateStore` pair that fail at exactly\none named `Boundary` and behave normally elsewhere, and a `PagedSource` that\nbookmarks every page so writes and bookmarks actually interleave.\n\n`fidelity` — the shared typed round-trip corpus (Category F groundwork). Owns\nthe hazard classes centrally (i64 past 2^53, -0.0, embedded quotes and\nbackslashes, empty strings, tz offsets, pre-epoch instants, nested JSON) so a\npair's test cannot quietly pick an easier corpus, and matches rows by key so a\nreordering destination is not penalised. `Tolerance` makes each allowance an\nexplicit statement about a destination limitation rather than a loose compare.\n\nCategory A suites (23 tests, all against the real `Pipeline::run`):\n\n- A1 bookmark ordering — every bookmark is backed by confirmed writes; a failed\n  write, a failed flush, and a failed state-put each leave the durable bookmark\n  behind the failure; resume re-reads exactly the unconfirmed tail with no gap\n  and at most one page of duplicates.\n- A2 exactly-once, both mechanisms — writes route through the idempotent path\n  with monotonic distinct tokens; a crash in the commit→state-put window\n  replays nothing; a re-run of a completed pipeline writes nothing; a failed\n  idempotent write leaves no token to skip on; the keyed mechanism converges\n  with no watermark at all. Includes a side-by-side control proving that under\n  the *identical* injected failure at-least-once does duplicate — without it\n  the exactly-once assertions would not be distinguishing the two modes.\n- A3 overwrite atomicity — begin precedes the first write and commit follows the\n  last; a failed write, a failed flush, and a cancel each abort without ever\n  swapping; a failing commit surfaces instead of reporting success; a suppressed\n  lifecycle leaves every phase to the caller (#552).\n- A8 cancel still flushes — a cancelled run flushes what it accepted and claims\n  no more than it flushed; an already-cancelled run writes and claims nothing.\n\nPer the issue's acceptance criteria, the durability guarantee is asserted\nthrough a shared helper that is itself proven capable of failing: three\n`#[should_panic]` tests feed it deliberately-wrong event logs (bookmark before\nwrite, bookmark overclaiming after a partial write).\n\nRefs #651\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1; git log -1 --format='%an <%ae>'","description":"Commit phase 1"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9tJdwp5YVB8xUoxhnKB","type":"assistant","uuid":"793bb49c-6f49-4213-b726-462250b4d785","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:33:13.077Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoin