{"parentUuid":"f8f5638d-ca10-43e8-b31e-8e9158c13a9f","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14831098 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5098d93-0ea7-42cd-8a86-4620e64a838b","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:47:21.630Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14831098 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"c5098d93-0ea7-42cd-8a86-4620e64a838b","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9uQN5MwVqrLic5tQ4Bf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BUNo6qfoPJ2BXvD3CfbCzZ","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit add crates/conformance crates/sink/sqlite\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest: read-side fault injection (E1) and the first fidelity pair (F)\n\nThird phase of #651, closing the two categories the audit found genuinely\nuncovered — 0 test files each — while the rest of B/C/D turned out to be\nsubstantially covered already.\n\nCategory E1 — read-side faults and the \"never hangs\" property (8 tests).\nEverything in Category A injects a *write*-side failure; this injects the other\nside, via a new `PagedSource::failing_after(n)`: the read dies partway through,\nas a dropped connection or expired cursor would. A mid-stream read failure must\nfail the run rather than truncate it silently (the pages already read are kept —\ndiscarding them would turn a recoverable partial run into a full replay); the\ndurable bookmark stays consistent and resume leaves no gap across the failure;\na first-page failure claims nothing. It also covers the two destructive\ncombinations: a failed read must never publish an overwrite, and must never\nlicense a cleanup delete.\n\nEvery run in that suite executes under a hard 20s ceiling, because the property\nthat actually matters operationally is **termination**. A retry loop that never\ngives up is indistinguishable from a hang from outside, and an operator cannot\ntell a slow pipeline from a wedged one. The cancelled-slow-sink test asserts the\nrun stops within 5s of a cancel rather than draining a ~16s backlog.\n\nCategory F — the first fidelity pair (4 tests), on the SQLite sink because it\nneeds no container and so runs in the required tier. The corpus and comparison\nboth come from `faucet_conformance::fidelity`, so the file is just wiring, which\nis the point: a new pair should look like this and no longer.\n\nIt earned its place immediately. The JSON-document path is exactly lossless —\nevery hazard class round-trips bit-identically with no tolerance at all. The\nauto-mapped path is not, and the test now documents precisely why: SQLite has no\nboolean type, so `true`/`false` land as `1`/`0`, and negative zero loses its\nsign through a TEXT-affinity column. Those are real destination limitations, so\nthey are named via `Tolerance::skipping` with the reason — and the observed\nvalues are *also* pinned, so a future change that starts dropping those columns\nentirely cannot slip through the tolerance.\n\nBoth new suites carry a failing-first proof: the fidelity pair asserts a\ndeliberately corrupted read-back is caught, and the fault suite includes a\nhealthy control run, without which a bug that made every run fail early would\nleave the whole suite green.\n\nRefs #651\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit phase 3"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_read_input_tokens":545826,"output_tokens":1033,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1033,"cache_read_input_tokens":545826,"cache_creation_input_tokens":322,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":322},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BUNo6qfoPJ2BXvD3CfbCzZ":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit add crates/conformance crates/sink/sqlite\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest: read-side fault injection (E1) and the first fidelity pair (F)\n\nThird phase of #651, closing the two categories the audit found genuinely\nuncovered — 0 test files each — while the rest of B/C/D turned out to be\nsubstantially covered already.\n\nCategory E1 — read-side faults and the \"never hangs\" property (8 tests).\nEverything in Category A injects a *write*-side failure; this injects the other\nside, via a new `PagedSource::failing_after(n)`: the read dies partway through,\nas a dropped connection or expired cursor would. A mid-stream read failure must\nfail the run rather than truncate it silently (the pages already read are kept —\ndiscarding them would turn a recoverable partial run into a full replay); the\ndurable bookmark stays consistent and resume leaves no gap across the failure;\na first-page failure claims nothing. It also covers the two destructive\ncombinations: a failed read must never publish an overwrite, and must never\nlicense a cleanup delete.\n\nEvery run in that suite executes under a hard 20s ceiling, because the property\nthat actually matters operationally is **termination**. A retry loop that never\ngives up is indistinguishable from a hang from outside, and an operator cannot\ntell a slow pipeline from a wedged one. The cancelled-slow-sink test asserts the\nrun stops within 5s of a cancel rather than draining a ~16s backlog.\n\nCategory F — the first fidelity pair (4 tests), on the SQLite sink because it\nneeds no container and so runs in the required tier. The corpus and comparison\nboth come from `faucet_conformance::fidelity`, so the file is just wiring, which\nis the point: a new pair should look like this and no longer.\n\nIt earned its place immediately. The JSON-document path is exactly lossless —\nevery hazard class round-trips bit-identically with no tolerance at all. The\nauto-mapped path is not, and the test now documents precisely why: SQLite has no\nboolean type, so `true`/`false` land as `1`/`0`, and negative zero loses its\nsign through a TEXT-affinity column. Those are real destination limitations, so\nthey are named via `Tolerance::skipping` with the reason — and the observed\nvalues are *also* pinned, so a future change that starts dropping those columns\nentirely cannot slip through the tolerance.\n\nBoth new suites carry a failing-first proof: the fidelity pair asserts a\ndeliberately corrupted read-back is caught, and the fault suite includes a\nhealthy control run, without which a bug that made every run fail early would\nleave the whole suite green.\n\nRefs #651\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -3","description":"Commit phase 3"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9uQMPh63GYidpQGzdkn","type":"assistant","uuid":"8d150258-a7f5-4d4b-9a5c-a5c5bcf51190","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:47:37.252Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
