{"parentUuid":"77880659-602f-4445-a3ae-673ef8a40907","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9uYqzsZVnNfQqrgVi7H","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RLiVRapzEbj38uLzbLPoic","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr merge 660 --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"test: engine-level reliability program — guarantee suites, fidelity corpus, state-format gates (#660)\" \\\n  --body \"Implements the integration-test program in #651.\n\nAn audit first: the issue's premise that there is no systematic integration-test\nprogram was partly stale — 292 integration-test files already exist and much of\nCategories B/C/D is covered. This builds the foundations that were actually\nmissing, fills the genuinely uncovered categories (A1-A4/A8, E1, F, G1), and\nrecords the per-item audit on the issue.\n\nFoundations in faucet-conformance: 'scripted' gives boundary-precise failure\ninjection over one shared ordered EventLog, so tests assert the *sequence* a\nguarantee is stated in rather than a final row count; 'fidelity' owns the typed\nround-trip corpus centrally so a pair cannot pick easier data.\n\n51 new tests: bookmark ordering, exactly-once (both mechanisms, with a control\narm proving at-least-once duplicates under the identical failure), overwrite\natomicity, cleanup safety (including the cancelled case, which returns Ok by\ndesign and would slip past the obvious check), read-side fault injection under a\nhard termination ceiling, state-format compatibility against frozen fixtures,\nand the first fidelity pair.\n\nEach check is shown capable of failing, per the acceptance criteria.\n\nFound on the way: SQLite's auto-mapped path is not type-preserving (no boolean\ntype; negative zero loses its sign) — now documented and pinned rather than\nsmoothed over; and a whitespace-padded commit token parses deliberately, because\na CHAR(20) watermark column pads on read.\n\nNew required 'Reliability guarantees' CI job, Docker-free and seconds long, plus\nan operations/reliability-testing.md tier guide.\n\nAddresses #651\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr view 660 --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest.commitHeadline'","description":"Arm auto-merge with an explicit message"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3320,"cache_read_input_tokens":547707,"output_tokens":826,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3320,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":826,"cache_read_input_tokens":547707,"cache_creation_input_tokens":3320,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":3320},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RLiVRapzEbj38uLzbLPoic":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr merge 660 --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"test: engine-level reliability program — guarantee suites, fidelity corpus, state-format gates (#660)\" \\\n  --body \"Implements the integration-test program in #651.\n\nAn audit first: the issue's premise that there is no systematic integration-test\nprogram was partly stale — 292 integration-test files already exist and much of\nCategories B/C/D is covered. This builds the foundations that were actually\nmissing, fills the genuinely uncovered categories (A1-A4/A8, E1, F, G1), and\nrecords the per-item audit on the issue.\n\nFoundations in faucet-conformance: 'scripted' gives boundary-precise failure\ninjection over one shared ordered EventLog, so tests assert the *sequence* a\nguarantee is stated in rather than a final row count; 'fidelity' owns the typed\nround-trip corpus centrally so a pair cannot pick easier data.\n\n51 new tests: bookmark ordering, exactly-once (both mechanisms, with a control\narm proving at-least-once duplicates under the identical failure), overwrite\natomicity, cleanup safety (including the cancelled case, which returns Ok by\ndesign and would slip past the obvious check), read-side fault injection under a\nhard termination ceiling, state-format compatibility against frozen fixtures,\nand the first fidelity pair.\n\nEach check is shown capable of failing, per the acceptance criteria.\n\nFound on the way: SQLite's auto-mapped path is not type-preserving (no boolean\ntype; negative zero loses its sign) — now documented and pinned rather than\nsmoothed over; and a whitespace-padded commit token parses deliberately, because\na CHAR(20) watermark column pads on read.\n\nNew required 'Reliability guarantees' CI job, Docker-free and seconds long, plus\nan operations/reliability-testing.md tier guide.\n\nAddresses #651\" 2>&1 | tail -2\ngh pr view 660 --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest.commitHeadline'","description":"Arm auto-merge with an explicit message"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9uYqT89jYJZPWk2cmdt","type":"assistant","uuid":"4117d382-e0cb-44b7-85d7-b82fdcc5e055","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:49:28.870Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
