{"parentUuid":"37044df9-1520-4e4c-81a6-8f2ac054e662","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9ua1fJuqAEJTob43QqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Now the per-item audit on the issue — an explicit acceptance criterion (\"each category has a tracked checklist\"):"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":551027,"output_tokens":2737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2737,"cache_read_input_tokens":551027,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9uZzufrwWrxD4YWi4o9","type":"assistant","uuid":"643f2165-fae6-4797-b05e-0265e3efafc8","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:49:35.060Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"643f2165-fae6-4797-b05e-0265e3efafc8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9ua1fJuqAEJTob43QqR","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01JbZD25FGY9fQk2GDGimfsp","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad\ncat > $S/audit651.md <<'BODY'\n## Audit against the live tree, per sub-item\n\nBefore writing anything I checked each of the ~40 sub-items against the actual code, because the tracker lags reality and the matrix as written would have produced a lot of duplicates. **The issue's premise is partly stale**: there are already 292 integration-test files, and Categories B, C and D are substantially covered by them.\n\nLegend: ✅ covered (was already, or lands in #660) · 🆕 gap, closed in #660 · 🟡 partly covered, remainder is a container/nightly tier · ⬜ open.\n\n### Category A — correctness mechanisms\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Bookmark ordering / crash-safety | 🆕 `reliability_bookmark_ordering` (8) |\n| A2 | Exactly-once, both mechanisms | 🆕 `reliability_exactly_once` (6), incl. an at-least-once control arm |\n| A3 | Overwrite atomicity | 🆕 `reliability_lifecycle` (engine) + ✅ per-sink suites already existed (`sink/*/tests/overwrite.rs`) |\n| A4 | Scoped cleanup | 🆕 `reliability_cleanup_safety` (8) — the *gate* was untested; the pure parts already were |\n| A5 | DLQ routing | ✅ **already covered** — `faucet-core` has `dlq_routes_only_failed_rows_for_partial_success_sink`, `dlq_propagate_policy_bubbles_outer_err`, `dlq_dlq_all_policy_routes_every_row_on_outer_err`, the per-page and total budget matrix, and `dlq_bookmark_advances_only_after_both_flushes`. Not duplicated; now run by the new required job. |\n| A6 | Schema-drift policies | 🟡 18 unit tests in `core::drift` + the CLI gate; the live-container `evolve` DDL arm stays a container tier |\n| A7 | Quality/contract/masking ordering | ✅ **already covered** — `masking_runs_before_the_sink` and `masking_applies_before_the_dlq_envelope` in `faucet-core` |\n| A8 | Cooperative cancel = flush | 🆕 `reliability_lifecycle` (engine) + ✅ `assert_cancellation_flushes` already existed for sinks |\n\n### Category B — CDC end-to-end\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | postgres-cdc | ✅ `source/postgres-cdc/tests/integration.rs` (+2 more) |\n| B2 | mysql-cdc / mongodb-cdc | ✅ 4 files |\n| B3 | `replicate` snapshot→CDC handoff | ✅ 5 files incl. `cli/tests/replication.rs` |\n\nCovered. The engine-side invariant these rely on — a bookmark never advancing past a confirmed write — is now independently pinned by A1, which is the part a CDC test cannot isolate.\n\n### Category C — protocol simulation\n\nEvery item ✅: C1 pagination × termination (72 files use `MockServer`), C2 auth/single-flight (6), C3 `async_job` (3), C4 OData (2), C5 discovery recipe (23), C6 native byte-passthrough (2).\n\n### Category D — control plane\n\nEvery item ✅: D1 lifecycle, D2 idempotency (40), D3 cluster A+B (26), D4 schedule (9), D5 triggers, D6 templates, D7 backfill (4), D8 RBAC/audit (16) — `cli/tests/` already has `serve_lifecycle.rs`, `serve_cluster.rs`, `schedule.rs`, `serve_triggers.rs`, `templates_end_to_end.rs`, `backfill_end_to_end.rs`, `serve_rbac.rs`.\n\n### Category E — fault injection\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | Connection drop mid-page/upload; **never hangs** | 🆕 `reliability_fault_injection` (8) — was **0 files**. Engine-level, Docker-free, every run under a hard termination ceiling. The toxiproxy-fronted container version remains a nightly tier. |\n| E2 | 429/5xx storms, breaker opens | ✅ 7 files |\n| E3 | Poison row | ✅ 2 files |\n| E4 | Slow sink / bounded memory | ✅ 2 files + `assert_bounded_memory`; the cancelled-slow-sink arm is now also in E1 |\n\n### Category F — fidelity round-trip\n\n🆕 The shared corpus + `assert_round_trip` + `Tolerance` now exist (this was the explicitly-requested \"shared fixture so each pair is ~20 lines\"), with the **first pair** on the SQLite sink because it needs no container and so gates every PR. Remaining priority pairs (postgres→bigquery-emulator, mysql→postgres, parquet→sqlite, kafka→jsonl, mongo→postgres) are now ~20 lines each — tracked below.\n\n### Category G — compatibility gates\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G1 | State-format compatibility | 🆕 `compat_state_format` (11) + 5 frozen fixtures — was **0 files** |\n| G2 | Config compatibility | ✅ `cli/tests/examples_roundtrip.rs` + `cli_end_to_end.rs` + the committed JSON-schema gate |\n| G3 | Serve API shape | ✅ `serve_openapi.rs` two-way sync |\n\n---\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Each category has a tracked checklist (this comment) and lands as one or more PRs\n- [x] Every Category A/B guarantee has a failing-first test — the durability assertion has three `#[should_panic]` tests fed deliberately-wrong event logs; the fidelity comparison has a corrupted-read-back test; the fault suite has a healthy control arm\n- [x] A `docs/book` reliability-testing page documents what is covered and how to run each tier locally\n- [x] CI wiring — new **required** `Reliability guarantees` job, Docker-free, seconds of test time (well inside the <15 min budget)\n- [x] The conformance harness gains the shared fixture/assertion helpers so new connectors inherit round-trip tests by default\n\n## Remaining, deliberately not in #660\n\nEach is a container or nightly tier rather than a gap in the program's foundations, and each is now cheap because the harness exists:\n\n- **F, remaining priority pairs** — ~20 lines each against the shared corpus.\n- **E1, toxiproxy tier** — the container-fronted version of the read-fault suite.\n- **A6, live `evolve` DDL** — drift policies against a real Postgres, asserting the emitted DDL.\n- **Branch protection** — the new job must report on a commit before being added to the required set (per CLAUDE.md, never mark a context required until it is confirmed to actually post).\n\nI'd suggest keeping this issue open for those four and treating the foundations as done. Happy to file them as separate tier-2 issues instead if you'd rather this one close with #660.\nBODY\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh issue comment 651 --body-file $S/audit651.md 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Post the per-item audit on issue 651"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_read_input_tokens":551027,"output_tokens":2737,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2737,"cache_read_input_tokens":551027,"cache_creation_input_tokens":890,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":890},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01JbZD25FGY9fQk2GDGimfsp":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nS=/private/tmp/claude-502/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f/scratchpad\ncat > $S/audit651.md <<'BODY'\n## Audit against the live tree, per sub-item\n\nBefore writing anything I checked each of the ~40 sub-items against the actual code, because the tracker lags reality and the matrix as written would have produced a lot of duplicates. **The issue's premise is partly stale**: there are already 292 integration-test files, and Categories B, C and D are substantially covered by them.\n\nLegend: ✅ covered (was already, or lands in #660) · 🆕 gap, closed in #660 · 🟡 partly covered, remainder is a container/nightly tier · ⬜ open.\n\n### Category A — correctness mechanisms\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| A1 | Bookmark ordering / crash-safety | 🆕 `reliability_bookmark_ordering` (8) |\n| A2 | Exactly-once, both mechanisms | 🆕 `reliability_exactly_once` (6), incl. an at-least-once control arm |\n| A3 | Overwrite atomicity | 🆕 `reliability_lifecycle` (engine) + ✅ per-sink suites already existed (`sink/*/tests/overwrite.rs`) |\n| A4 | Scoped cleanup | 🆕 `reliability_cleanup_safety` (8) — the *gate* was untested; the pure parts already were |\n| A5 | DLQ routing | ✅ **already covered** — `faucet-core` has `dlq_routes_only_failed_rows_for_partial_success_sink`, `dlq_propagate_policy_bubbles_outer_err`, `dlq_dlq_all_policy_routes_every_row_on_outer_err`, the per-page and total budget matrix, and `dlq_bookmark_advances_only_after_both_flushes`. Not duplicated; now run by the new required job. |\n| A6 | Schema-drift policies | 🟡 18 unit tests in `core::drift` + the CLI gate; the live-container `evolve` DDL arm stays a container tier |\n| A7 | Quality/contract/masking ordering | ✅ **already covered** — `masking_runs_before_the_sink` and `masking_applies_before_the_dlq_envelope` in `faucet-core` |\n| A8 | Cooperative cancel = flush | 🆕 `reliability_lifecycle` (engine) + ✅ `assert_cancellation_flushes` already existed for sinks |\n\n### Category B — CDC end-to-end\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| B1 | postgres-cdc | ✅ `source/postgres-cdc/tests/integration.rs` (+2 more) |\n| B2 | mysql-cdc / mongodb-cdc | ✅ 4 files |\n| B3 | `replicate` snapshot→CDC handoff | ✅ 5 files incl. `cli/tests/replication.rs` |\n\nCovered. The engine-side invariant these rely on — a bookmark never advancing past a confirmed write — is now independently pinned by A1, which is the part a CDC test cannot isolate.\n\n### Category C — protocol simulation\n\nEvery item ✅: C1 pagination × termination (72 files use `MockServer`), C2 auth/single-flight (6), C3 `async_job` (3), C4 OData (2), C5 discovery recipe (23), C6 native byte-passthrough (2).\n\n### Category D — control plane\n\nEvery item ✅: D1 lifecycle, D2 idempotency (40), D3 cluster A+B (26), D4 schedule (9), D5 triggers, D6 templates, D7 backfill (4), D8 RBAC/audit (16) — `cli/tests/` already has `serve_lifecycle.rs`, `serve_cluster.rs`, `schedule.rs`, `serve_triggers.rs`, `templates_end_to_end.rs`, `backfill_end_to_end.rs`, `serve_rbac.rs`.\n\n### Category E — fault injection\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| E1 | Connection drop mid-page/upload; **never hangs** | 🆕 `reliability_fault_injection` (8) — was **0 files**. Engine-level, Docker-free, every run under a hard termination ceiling. The toxiproxy-fronted container version remains a nightly tier. |\n| E2 | 429/5xx storms, breaker opens | ✅ 7 files |\n| E3 | Poison row | ✅ 2 files |\n| E4 | Slow sink / bounded memory | ✅ 2 files + `assert_bounded_memory`; the cancelled-slow-sink arm is now also in E1 |\n\n### Category F — fidelity round-trip\n\n🆕 The shared corpus + `assert_round_trip` + `Tolerance` now exist (this was the explicitly-requested \"shared fixture so each pair is ~20 lines\"), with the **first pair** on the SQLite sink because it needs no container and so gates every PR. Remaining priority pairs (postgres→bigquery-emulator, mysql→postgres, parquet→sqlite, kafka→jsonl, mongo→postgres) are now ~20 lines each — tracked below.\n\n### Category G — compatibility gates\n\n| # | Item | Status |\n|---|---|---|\n| G1 | State-format compatibility | 🆕 `compat_state_format` (11) + 5 frozen fixtures — was **0 files** |\n| G2 | Config compatibility | ✅ `cli/tests/examples_roundtrip.rs` + `cli_end_to_end.rs` + the committed JSON-schema gate |\n| G3 | Serve API shape | ✅ `serve_openapi.rs` two-way sync |\n\n---\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- [x] Each category has a tracked checklist (this comment) and lands as one or more PRs\n- [x] Every Category A/B guarantee has a failing-first test — the durability assertion has three `#[should_panic]` tests fed deliberately-wrong event logs; the fidelity comparison has a corrupted-read-back test; the fault suite has a healthy control arm\n- [x] A `docs/book` reliability-testing page documents what is covered and how to run each tier locally\n- [x] CI wiring — new **required** `Reliability guarantees` job, Docker-free, seconds of test time (well inside the <15 min budget)\n- [x] The conformance harness gains the shared fixture/assertion helpers so new connectors inherit round-trip tests by default\n\n## Remaining, deliberately not in #660\n\nEach is a container or nightly tier rather than a gap in the program's foundations, and each is now cheap because the harness exists:\n\n- **F, remaining priority pairs** — ~20 lines each against the shared corpus.\n- **E1, toxiproxy tier** — the container-fronted version of the read-fault suite.\n- **A6, live `evolve` DDL** — drift policies against a real Postgres, asserting the emitted DDL.\n- **Branch protection** — the new job must report on a commit before being added to the required set (per CLAUDE.md, never mark a context required until it is confirmed to actually post).\n\nI'd suggest keeping this issue open for those four and treating the foundations as done. Happy to file them as separate tier-2 issues instead if you'd rather this one close with #660.\nBODY\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh issue comment 651 --body-file $S/audit651.md 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Post the per-item audit on issue 651"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011Cf9uZzufrwWrxD4YWi4o9","type":"assistant","uuid":"a56398b0-e7da-4a21-acb3-7b29aacda251","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:50:06.414Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":