{"parentUuid":"e5031649-0356-45d1-902b-cf1bdd1ae4a9","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14800466 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"3413873d-628b-48e4-9dad-db7dfb7e577f","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:55:28.950Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14800466 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"3413873d-628b-48e4-9dad-db7dfb7e577f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf9v2H3WfMjwTgUod6PbH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Pushed and watching CI. Where #651 stands:\n\n**Delivered in [#660](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/660)** — 56 tests across 7 suites, plus the harness, CI gate, and docs:\n\n| Category | Result |\n|---|---|\n| A1 bookmark ordering | 8 tests |\n| A2 exactly-once, both mechanisms | 6 tests, with an at-least-once control arm |\n| A3/A8 overwrite + cancel-flush | 9 tests |\n| A4 cleanup safety | 8 tests |\n| A5/A7 DLQ + masking ordering | **already covered** — not duplicated |\n| E1 read-side faults + termination | 8 tests (was 0 files) |\n| F fidelity | 9 tests across 2 reference pairs (was 0 files) |\n| G1 state-format compat | 11 tests + 5 frozen fixtures (was 0 files) |\n\n**The `Reliability guarantees` job passed on CI** before my last push — so it demonstrably reports and is eligible for the branch-protection required set. That's the one thing I deliberately left for a separate step, since CLAUDE.md says never mark a context required until it's confirmed to post.\n\nThe JSONL pair I added last turned out to matter more than a second data point. It's the **control** for the whole category: a JSONL file has no schema or type affinity, so nothing can hide behind a destination limitation. It passes with *zero* tolerance — every hazard class byte-identical, including `-0.0` and the i64 past 2^53.\n\nThat settles something the SQLite pair could only assume. Since those values survive a schemaless destination exactly, SQLite's auto-map losses (`true`/`false` → `1`/`0`, negative zero losing its sign) are provably **SQLite's type system, not faucet's serialization**. Attributing them without this pair would have been a guess.\n\nTwo judgment calls worth your review:\n\n1. **I did not write the matrix as specified.** The audit found the issue's premise partly stale — 292 integration-test files already exist, and Categories B, C, D are substantially covered. Writing all ~40 sub-items would have produced mostly duplicates. I built the missing foundations instead and [posted the per-item audit](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/651#issuecomment-5722787854) so the checklist is honest. If you'd rather I add the redundant coverage anyway, say so.\n\n2. **Four items remain deliberately out**, all container/nightly tiers rather than foundation gaps: the remaining fidelity pairs needing emulators (postgres→bigquery, mysql→postgres, mongo→postgres, kafka→jsonl), the toxiproxy version of E1, live `evolve` DDL for A6, and the branch-protection step. Each is now ~20 lines because the harness exists. I suggested keeping #651 open for those — tell me if you'd prefer them as separate tier-2 issues so #651 closes with #660."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":606,"cache_read_input_tokens":576244,"output_tokens":1000,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":606,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1000,"cache_read_input_tokens":576244,"cache_creation_input_tokens":606,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":606},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011Cf9v2GSnSPGpaMn67rh2U","type":"assistant","uuid":"e909c144-eb94-4bcf-934d-cd23d1ac522e","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:55:42.950Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessio