{"parentUuid":"cbd43bef-2d6d-4ac7-95f8-3da45af67ec1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01GkMffAPNCnUWq49NcYiB6X","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":235},"type":"attachment","uuid":"c5bf278b-7217-4df0-8489-dd2029a65266","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:58:37.121Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"c5bf278b-7217-4df0-8489-dd2029a65266","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"edited_text_file","filename":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/.claude/rules/maintenance.md","snippet":"43\t\n44\t| If you change… | Also update (same PR) |\n45\t|---|---|\n46\t| **Add / remove / rename a connector** | umbrella + CLI features; CI `feature-check` matrix (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`); root README connector table **and the counts** (hero \"20 sources / 16 sinks\", architecture \"46 crates — …\"); docs-site catalog `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` (capability matrix) + `reference/choosing.md`; a `cli/examples/<src>_to_<sink>.yaml`; `examples/README.md` mapping (+ `examples/docker-compose.yml` and `examples/infra/` if it needs new local infra); per-crate crates.io `keywords` + `[package.metadata.docs.rs]` + `#![cfg_attr(docsrs, feature(doc_cfg))]`; the crate table in this file; README \"Project Structure\" |\n47\t| **Change a connector's config fields / defaults / auth / pagination / behavior** | that crate's `README.md`; root README tables if user-facing; any docs-site page that mentions it (cookbook `auth`/`pagination`/`state`/`compression`, `reference/*`); affected `cli/examples/*.yaml`. (`faucet schema`/`init` are schema-driven — no manual update.) |\n48\t| **Change a connector's streaming / resumable / compression support** | the capability-matrix columns in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` (verify against the code — these were wrong once) |\n49\t| **Change CLI commands or the config-file grammar** | `docs/book/src/reference/cli.md` + `reference/config.md`; `cli/README.md`; root README quickstart |\n50\t| **Change `Source` / `Sink` / `Pipeline` / transform / `FaucetError` APIs** | the Architecture section here; docs-site `getting-started/concepts.md` + `tutorials/library.md`; affected crate READMEs |\n51\t| **Change an engine guarantee, or add a `Sink`/`Source` lifecycle hook (#651)** | the matching suite under `crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs` (and a new `Boundary`/`Event` in `crates/conformance/src/scripted.rs` if the failure point is new — plus a `#[should_panic]` proof that any reusable assertion can still fail); the tier table + \"what each suite asserts\" section in `docs/book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md`; the `reliability` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` if a new package needs covering; a frozen fixture under `crates/conformance/tests/fixtures/state/` when a new **state shape** ships (never edit an existing one to make a test pass) |\n52\t| **Add a dependency that introduces a new license** | `deny.toml` `allow` list (the `supply-chain` CI job enforces this; license rules differ by platform, so a Linux-only dep can fail CI even if local passes) |\n53\t| **Add / move / remove files or directories** | README \"Project Structure\" (see below) |\n54\t| **Change brand (logo / colors / wordmark)** | `.github/assets/` (logo.svg tile, logo-mark.svg transparent, logo-mono.svg single-color, wordmark.svg, favicon.svg/png, social-banner.png); re-render `social-banner.png` (1280×640) from its SVG source via headless Chrome; **re-upload to repo Settings → Social preview**; refresh the README header logo and the mdBook favicon when its override path is restored in mdBook 0.5+ |\n55\t| **File a feature / enhancement issue** | cross-link it to the roadmap epic (the open `epic`-labelled issue, currently #38) |\n56\t| **Change lineage config, transports, or column-lineage logic** | `docs/book/src/cookbook/lineage.md` (field table, column-lineage matrix, metrics); `docs/book/src/reference/config.md` (`## lineage` section); the Lineage subsection in this CLAUDE.md; affected connector READMEs if `dataset_uri()` shapes change |\n57\t| **Change exactly-once support (add/remove a capable source/sink)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`source_supports_exactly_once` / `sink_supports_idempotent_writes` allowlists); the Exactly-once column in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the \"Exactly-once delivery\" section in `docs/book/src/cookbook/state.md` (supported source/sink tables); the sink's `README.md` (add/remove the \"Exactly-once delivery\" section); override or remove `Sink::supports_idempotent_writes` / `write_batch_idempotent` / `last_committed_token` on the sink, and `Source::supports_exactly_once` on the source |\n58\t| **Change upsert support (add/remove a capable sink)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`sink_supported_write_modes` allowlist); the sink's `Sink::supported_write_modes()` override; the Upsert capability column in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the supported-sink table in `docs/book/src/cookbook/upsert.md`; the sink's `README.md` (write-mode / `key` / `delete_marker` section); the `write_mode × sink` gate in `cli/src/expand.rs` |\n59\t| **Change overwrite support (add/remove a capable sink, #492)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`OVERWRITE_SINK_KINDS` + `sink_supports_overwrite` + `sink_supported_write_modes`); the sink's `Sink::supported_write_modes()` (must list `Overwrite`) + its `is_overwrite`/`begin_overwrite`/`commit_overwrite`/`abort_overwrite` lifecycle; the Overwrite note in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the Overwrite section in `docs/book/src/cookbook/upsert.md`; the sink's `README.md` (Overwrite subsection); the overwrite gates in `cli/src/expand.rs` (exactly-once / schema-evolve / cleanup incompatibilities); the \"Write modes / upsert\" + `write_mode.rs` notes in `.claude/rules/{connectors,architecture}.md` |"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d0ffe063-23b3-451f-838a-df930d343b3c","timestamp":"2026-09-17T23:58:37.474Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream/.claude/rules/maintenance.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n43\t\n44\t| If you change… | Also update (same PR) |\n45\t|---|---|\n46\t| **Add / remove / rename a connector** | umbrella + CLI features; CI `feature-check` matrix (`.github/workflows/ci.yml`); root README connector table **and the counts** (hero \"20 sources / 16 sinks\", architecture \"46 crates — …\"); docs-site catalog `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` (capability matrix) + `reference/choosing.md`; a `cli/examples/<src>_to_<sink>.yaml`; `examples/README.md` mapping (+ `examples/docker-compose.yml` and `examples/infra/` if it needs new local infra); per-crate crates.io `keywords` + `[package.metadata.docs.rs]` + `#![cfg_attr(docsrs, feature(doc_cfg))]`; the crate table in this file; README \"Project Structure\" |\n47\t| **Change a connector's config fields / defaults / auth / pagination / behavior** | that crate's `README.md`; root README tables if user-facing; any docs-site page that mentions it (cookbook `auth`/`pagination`/`state`/`compression`, `reference/*`); affected `cli/examples/*.yaml`. (`faucet schema`/`init` are schema-driven — no manual update.) |\n48\t| **Change a connector's streaming / resumable / compression support** | the capability-matrix columns in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md` (verify against the code — these were wrong once) |\n49\t| **Change CLI commands or the config-file grammar** | `docs/book/src/reference/cli.md` + `reference/config.md`; `cli/README.md`; root README quickstart |\n50\t| **Change `Source` / `Sink` / `Pipeline` / transform / `FaucetError` APIs** | the Architecture section here; docs-site `getting-started/concepts.md` + `tutorials/library.md`; affected crate READMEs |\n51\t| **Change an engine guarantee, or add a `Sink`/`Source` lifecycle hook (#651)** | the matching suite under `crates/conformance/tests/reliability_*.rs` (and a new `Boundary`/`Event` in `crates/conformance/src/scripted.rs` if the failure point is new — plus a `#[should_panic]` proof that any reusable assertion can still fail); the tier table + \"what each suite asserts\" section in `docs/book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md`; the `reliability` job in `.github/workflows/ci.yml` if a new package needs covering; a frozen fixture under `crates/conformance/tests/fixtures/state/` when a new **state shape** ships (never edit an existing one to make a test pass) |\n52\t| **Add a dependency that introduces a new license** | `deny.toml` `allow` list (the `supply-chain` CI job enforces this; license rules differ by platform, so a Linux-only dep can fail CI even if local passes) |\n53\t| **Add / move / remove files or directories** | README \"Project Structure\" (see below) |\n54\t| **Change brand (logo / colors / wordmark)** | `.github/assets/` (logo.svg tile, logo-mark.svg transparent, logo-mono.svg single-color, wordmark.svg, favicon.svg/png, social-banner.png); re-render `social-banner.png` (1280×640) from its SVG source via headless Chrome; **re-upload to repo Settings → Social preview**; refresh the README header logo and the mdBook favicon when its override path is restored in mdBook 0.5+ |\n55\t| **File a feature / enhancement issue** | cross-link it to the roadmap epic (the open `epic`-labelled issue, currently #38) |\n56\t| **Change lineage config, transports, or column-lineage logic** | `docs/book/src/cookbook/lineage.md` (field table, column-lineage matrix, metrics); `docs/book/src/reference/config.md` (`## lineage` section); the Lineage subsection in this CLAUDE.md; affected connector READMEs if `dataset_uri()` shapes change |\n57\t| **Change exactly-once support (add/remove a capable source/sink)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`source_supports_exactly_once` / `sink_supports_idempotent_writes` allowlists); the Exactly-once column in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the \"Exactly-once delivery\" section in `docs/book/src/cookbook/state.md` (supported source/sink tables); the sink's `README.md` (add/remove the \"Exactly-once delivery\" section); override or remove `Sink::supports_idempotent_writes` / `write_batch_idempotent` / `last_committed_token` on the sink, and `Source::supports_exactly_once` on the source |\n58\t| **Change upsert support (add/remove a capable sink)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`sink_supported_write_modes` allowlist); the sink's `Sink::supported_write_modes()` override; the Upsert capability column in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the supported-sink table in `docs/book/src/cookbook/upsert.md`; the sink's `README.md` (write-mode / `key` / `delete_marker` section); the `write_mode × sink` gate in `cli/src/expand.rs` |\n59\t| **Change overwrite support (add/remove a capable sink, #492)** | `cli/src/registry.rs` (`OVERWRITE_SINK_KINDS` + `sink_supports_overwrite` + `sink_supported_write_modes`); the sink's `Sink::supported_write_modes()` (must list `Overwrite`) + its `is_overwrite`/`begin_overwrite`/`commit_overwrite`/`abort_overwrite` lifecycle; the Overwrite note in `docs/book/src/reference/connectors.md`; the Overwrite section in `docs/book/src/cookbook/upsert.md`; the sink's `README.md` (Overwrite subsection); the overwrite gates in `cli/src/expand.rs` (exactly-once / schema-evolve / cleanup incompatibilities); the \"Write modes / upsert\" + `write_mode.rs` notes in `.claude/rules/{connectors,architecture}.md` |\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
