{"parentUuid":"1141dec8-1636-4133-b317-c692d19af25c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfA2BCDjyLkTwkZFb1RJn","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01NBesKViuKoReU4Bht62Rat","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream \\\n  --base main --head fix/reliability-job-always-runs \\\n  --title \"ci: make the reliability gate always report so it can be required\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\nPrerequisite for adding `Reliability guarantees` (#660) to the branch-protection required set. Found before it could affect anyone.\n\n## The problem\n\nThe job I added in #660 carried a **job-level** `if` gate, copied from `test`:\n\n```yaml\nif: ${{ github.event_name != 'pull_request' || needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' }}\n```\n\nBut `test` is deliberately *not* a required check, and this one is meant to be. None of the actually-required jobs has a job-level gate, and `clippy` spells out why in its own comment:\n\n> `# Required check → job always runs (stays green), but the heavy step is gated`\n\nWith the job-level gate, a docs-only PR (`code == false`) skips the whole job. A **skipped** required check can leave a PR sitting on *\"Expected — waiting for status\"* indefinitely — which is exactly the reason `codecov/patch` is kept out of the required set (documented in CLAUDE.md). So marking this context required as-is would have blocked every docs-only PR from merging.\n\n## The fix\n\nMove the condition to the four expensive steps, matching the established pattern, and state the reasoning inline so it does not get reintroduced.\n\n- **Docs-only PR** → job runs, all steps skip, reports green in seconds without even installing a toolchain.\n- **Code PR** → suites run exactly as before: **53s**, against `Test`'s 1h13m and `Coverage`'s 1h7m. That gap is the entire point of splitting this out.\n\n## After this lands\n\nI'll add the context with the granular endpoint, preserving the existing eight:\n\n```bash\ngh api --method PATCH repos/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/branches/main/protection/required_status_checks \\\n  -f 'contexts[]=…'   # the current 8, plus \"Reliability guarantees\"\n```\n\nNot a full `PUT .../protection`, which would clobber the rest of the protection config.\n\nRefs #651\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Open the CI fix PR"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":602261,"output_tokens":878,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":878,"cache_read_input_tokens":602261,"cache_creation_input_tokens":878,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":878},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01NBesKViuKoReU4Bht62Rat":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && gh pr create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream \\\n  --base main --head fix/reliability-job-always-runs \\\n  --title \"ci: make the reliability gate always report so it can be required\" \\\n  --body \"$(cat <<'BODY'\nPrerequisite for adding `Reliability guarantees` (#660) to the branch-protection required set. Found before it could affect anyone.\n\n## The problem\n\nThe job I added in #660 carried a **job-level** `if` gate, copied from `test`:\n\n```yaml\nif: ${{ github.event_name != 'pull_request' || needs.changes.outputs.code == 'true' }}\n```\n\nBut `test` is deliberately *not* a required check, and this one is meant to be. None of the actually-required jobs has a job-level gate, and `clippy` spells out why in its own comment:\n\n> `# Required check → job always runs (stays green), but the heavy step is gated`\n\nWith the job-level gate, a docs-only PR (`code == false`) skips the whole job. A **skipped** required check can leave a PR sitting on *\"Expected — waiting for status\"* indefinitely — which is exactly the reason `codecov/patch` is kept out of the required set (documented in CLAUDE.md). So marking this context required as-is would have blocked every docs-only PR from merging.\n\n## The fix\n\nMove the condition to the four expensive steps, matching the established pattern, and state the reasoning inline so it does not get reintroduced.\n\n- **Docs-only PR** → job runs, all steps skip, reports green in seconds without even installing a toolchain.\n- **Code PR** → suites run exactly as before: **53s**, against `Test`'s 1h13m and `Coverage`'s 1h7m. That gap is the entire point of splitting this out.\n\n## After this lands\n\nI'll add the context with the granular endpoint, preserving the existing eight:\n\n```bash\ngh api --method PATCH repos/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/branches/main/protection/required_status_checks \\\n  -f 'contexts[]=…'   # the current 8, plus \"Reliability guarantees\"\n```\n\nNot a full `PUT .../protection`, which would clobber the rest of the protection config.\n\nRefs #651\nBODY\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Open the CI fix PR"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfA2BBMPwSSpcUcUBKYRt","type":"assistant","uuid":"77a275a6-8ec6-4276-8195-5c2139320aff","timestamp":"2026-09-18T01:16:22.355Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/reliability-job-always-runs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
