{"parentUuid":"c3aa83c0-fa3e-49c4-a33d-90c6239cfe07","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAQZE81xmoYmqBDRGm6R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Swapped the noisy monitor for a single waiter that fires once — on merge, or on a real failure. No more per-check chatter.\n\nSummary of where #651 landed:\n\n| PR | Content | State |\n|---|---|---|\n| #660 | Harness (`scripted`, `fidelity`), Categories A/E1-engine/G1, required CI job, docs | **merged** |\n| #661 | Made the gate always report so it could be required | **merged** |\n| #663 | A6 drift matrix, 4 fidelity pairs, container fault injection | awaiting `Coverage` |\n\nPlus branch protection updated (9 required contexts) and three issues filed from findings along the way: [#657](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/657) (kafka `headers_path` inert), [#658](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/658) (`NodeReport.error` untyped), [#662](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/662) (SQL sources mistyping runtime failures as `Config`).\n\nTotal: 74 tests across 9 suites, every guarantee with a proof it can fail.\n\nTwo things still open for your call, neither blocking:\n- The decimal-typing improvement I offered to file — the one genuine weakness the BSON question surfaced.\n- Whether you want the B/C/D duplicate coverage; my audit still says it exists across the 292 files already there."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":707673,"output_tokens":477,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":636,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":477,"cache_read_input_tokens":707673,"cac