ink\\|validate_connector\\|source_schema\" crates/../cli/src/templates/store.rs | head -6\necho\necho \"=== 620: delta target_file_size used?\"\ngrep -rn \"target_file_size\" crates/sink/delta/src/*.rs crates/common/delta/src/*.rs 2>/dev/null | head -5\necho\necho \"=== 623: async_job page buffering — does it stream?\"\ngrep -n \"fn stream\\|collect()\\|Vec::new()\\|extend(\" crates/source/rest/src/async_job.rs | head -8\necho\necho \"=== 640: read the complaint\"\ngh issue view 640 --json body --jq .body | head -14","description":"Check 609, 620, 623, 640"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfAXWCdT62fd4FPXuDxMR","type":"assistant","uuid":"39cdee36-3b01-4850-8b6b-ff8ea439d093","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:40:55.914Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"39cdee36-3b01-4850-8b6b-ff8ea439d093","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01HabuJmrQw9emzj7DUfuDRx","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":71},"type":"attachment","uuid":"94d1b0c4-f313-419f-9ec2-27aaf718c20a","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:40:56.002Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"39cdee36-3b01-4850-8b6b-ff8ea439d093","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e0f7f418-adf2-4227-9df5-4e6afef6b88f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HabuJmrQw9emzj7DUfuDRx","type":"tool_result","content":"=== 609: does template register validate connector config?\n\n=== 620: delta target_file_size used?\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:59:    pub target_file_size: Option<usize>,\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:75:            target_file_size: None,\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:87:        if matches!(self.target_file_size, Some(0)) {\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:89:                \"delta sink: `target_file_size` must be greater than 0 when set\".to_string(),\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:127:    fn rejects_zero_target_file_size() {\n\n=== 623: async_job page buffering — does it stream?\n\n=== 640: read the complaint\n## Summary\n\nQuery-based sources collapse **many logical datasets into one catalog/lineage entry** because `dataset_uri()` returns only the connection endpoint, not the object/table the query targets. Observed: a 21-object Salesforce → BigQuery matrix shows **1 source dataset** (`https://example.my.salesforce.com/`, \"20 runs\", a single conflated row count) but **21 sink datasets** (distinct `table_id`s). Each matrix row should be its own source dataset with its own row count and its own `source → sink` lineage edge.\n\n## Motivation\n\nCatalog (#279) + lineage correctness. The whole point of the Data Movement Catalog is per-dataset identity, schema timeline, volume, and lineage. When N objects share one endpoint, the catalog reports one source touched by \"N runs\" with a meaningless merged row count, and the lineage graph shows a single node fanning out to N sinks instead of N clean edges — losing per-object volume/freshness/lineage. This is wrong for every query-based source used in a matrix: REST `async_job` (SObject in SOQL), GraphQL (operation/type), and SQL sources (postgres/mysql/mssql/sqlite/…: table in the query).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`dataset_uri()` identifies the dataset, and the catalog keys on it (`cli/src/catalog/model.rs::canonicalize_uri`). The REST source returns `base_url + path` (`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs`), which is identical across matrix rows whose only difference is the query body (`async_job.submit.json.query` = \"… FROM Account\" vs \"… FROM Contact\"). Sinks don't collapse because each row sets a distinct `table_id`.\n\n## Proposed design","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"3b0b2578-f1a2-4679-b41c-cc7901223088","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:40:59.868Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== 609: does template register validate connector config?\n\n=== 620: delta target_file_size used?\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:59:    pub target_file_size: Option<usize>,\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:75:            target_file_size: None,\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:87:        if matches!(self.target_file_size, Some(0)) {\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:89:                \"delta sink: `target_file_size` must be greater than 0 when set\".to_string(),\ncrates/sink/delta/src/config.rs:127:    fn rejects_zero_target_file_size() {\n\n=== 623: async_job page buffering — does it stream?\n\n=== 640: read the complaint\n## Summary\n\nQuery-based sources collapse **many logical datasets into one catalog/lineage entry** because `dataset_uri()` returns only the connection endpoint, not the object/table the query targets. Observed: a 21-object Salesforce → BigQuery matrix shows **1 source dataset** (`https://example.my.salesforce.com/`, \"20 runs\", a single conflated row count) but **21 sink datasets** (distinct `table_id`s). Each matrix row should be its own source dataset with its own row count and its own `source → sink` lineage edge.\n\n## Motivation\n\nCatalog (#279) + lineage correctness. The whole point of the Data Movement Catalog is per-dataset identity, schema timeline, volume, and lineage. When N objects share one endpoint, the catalog reports one source touched by \"N runs\" with a meaningless merged row count, and the lineage graph shows a single node fanning out to N sinks instead of N clean edges — losing per-object volume/freshness/lineage. This is wrong for every query-based source used in a matrix: REST `async_job` (SObject in SOQL), GraphQL (operation/type), and SQL sources (postgres/mysql/mssql/sqlite/…: table in the query).\n\n## Root cause\n\n`dataset_uri()` identifies the dataset, and the catalog keys on it (`cli/src/catalog/model.rs::canonicalize_uri`). The REST source returns `base_url + path` (`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs`), which is identical across matrix rows whose only difference is the query body (`async_job.submit.json.query` = \"… FROM Account\" vs \"… FROM Contact\"). Sinks don't collapse because each row sets a distinct `table_id`.\n\n## Proposed design","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"39cdee36-3b01-4850-8b6b-ff8ea439d093","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
