{"parentUuid":"56a585c7-bc38-4db1-9c04-81ac5a8325ff","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01LSGYnxjjr6R85iswXyKhxt","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":60},"type":"attachment","uuid":"607bcfab-6bbf-4cc2-8dff-8513646b669d","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:42:30.401Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"56a585c7-bc38-4db1-9c04-81ac5a8325ff","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"e0f7f418-adf2-4227-9df5-4e6afef6b88f","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01LSGYnxjjr6R85iswXyKhxt","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\n\nIn the `Value` write path, a page that carries a bookmark is checkpointed inside `run_stream` (flush → `StateStore::put`, ADR 0002) **before** `Pipeline::run` decides the overwrite outcome. Under `write_mode: overwrite` with a staged lifecycle, that means the bookmark can be durably advanced while `commit_overwrite` subsequently **fails or is skipped** (abort path): the destination is left unchanged (staging discarded — correct), but the state store now claims the run's data was delivered.\n\nOn the next incremental run the source resumes from the advanced bookmark, so the records between the old and new bookmark are never re-fetched — the refreshed destination is **permanently missing rows**, silently, with green runs thereafter.\n\n## Motivation\n\nSilent downstream incorrectness is the worst bug class (CLAUDE.md Primary Goal). The native byte-passthrough path fixed this ordering for its own loop in #650 (bookmarks are held until the single terminal flush under overwrite); the `Value` path predates that work and still persists per-page.\n\n## Reproduction sketch\n\n1. Config: incremental-capable source emitting a final-page bookmark + a staged-overwrite sink (`write_mode: overwrite`) + a durable `state:` block.\n2. Run once; make `commit_overwrite` fail (e.g. drop the staging table concurrently, or kill the process between `run_stream` returning and the commit).\n3. Destination unchanged (correct), state store bookmark advanced (wrong).\n4. Run again: the source applies the advanced bookmark; the \"full refresh\" now excludes the skipped window.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nMirror the native path's rule in `run_stream` / `Pipeline::run`: when the sink `is_overwrite()`, defer every bookmark (hold the last one seen) and persist it **only after `commit_overwrite` succeeds**. On abort/failure/cancel, persist nothing. Alternatively (smaller): reject `replication_method`-driven bookmarks + `write_mode: overwrite` at expand time — a full refresh arguably has no meaningful resume position — but the deferred-persist fix keeps the (bookmark-carrying source → periodic full refresh) pattern working.\n\n## Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/core/src/pipeline.rs` — `run_stream` checkpoint block; `Pipeline::run` overwrite commit/abort block (the native runner already implements the target semantics — see `run_stream_native`'s `pending_bookmark`).\n- Tests: a mock overwrite sink whose `commit_overwrite` fails once + a `MemoryStateStore` assertion that the bookmark did not advance.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Cancelled overwrite runs (terminal flush is already skipped since #650) must also not persist.\n- Exactly-once mode is unaffected (overwrite × exactly-once is already rejected at expand time).\n- Topology sink nodes share `run_stream`, so the fix must apply per sink node.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A failed/aborted/cancelled overwrite never advances the state-store bookmark (unit-tested).\n- A successful overwrite persists the final bookmark exactly once, after commit.\n- Non-overwrite checkpoint semantics unchanged (ADR 0002 ordering intact).\n\n## Out of scope","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"629ad8d3-109b-44ba-89f7-cffdcacd1071","timestamp":"2026-09-18T07:42:31.384Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Summary\n\nIn the `Value` write path, a page that carries a bookmark is checkpointed inside `run_stream` (flush → `StateStore::put`, ADR 0002) **before** `Pipeline::run` decides the overwrite outcome. Under `write_mode: overwrite` with a staged lifecycle, that means the bookmark can be durably advanced while `commit_overwrite` subsequently **fails or is skipped** (abort path): the destination is left unchanged (staging discarded — correct), but the state store now claims the run's data was delivered.\n\nOn the next incremental run the source resumes from the advanced bookmark, so the records between the old and new bookmark are never re-fetched — the refreshed destination is **permanently missing rows**, silently, with green runs thereafter.\n\n## Motivation\n\nSilent downstream incorrectness is the worst bug class (CLAUDE.md Primary Goal). The native byte-passthrough path fixed this ordering for its own loop in #650 (bookmarks are held until the single terminal flush under overwrite); the `Value` path predates that work and still persists per-page.\n\n## Reproduction sketch\n\n1. Config: incremental-capable source emitting a final-page bookmark + a staged-overwrite sink (`write_mode: overwrite`) + a durable `state:` block.\n2. Run once; make `commit_overwrite` fail (e.g. drop the staging table concurrently, or kill the process between `run_stream` returning and the commit).\n3. Destination unchanged (correct), state store bookmark advanced (wrong).\n4. Run again: the source applies the advanced bookmark; the \"full refresh\" now excludes the skipped window.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nMirror the native path's rule in `run_stream` / `Pipeline::run`: when the sink `is_overwrite()`, defer every bookmark (hold the last one seen) and persist it **only after `commit_overwrite` succeeds**. On abort/failure/cancel, persist nothing. Alternatively (smaller): reject `replication_method`-driven bookmarks + `write_mode: overwrite` at expand time — a full refresh arguably has no meaningful resume position — but the deferred-persist fix keeps the (bookmark-carrying source → periodic full refresh) pattern working.\n\n## Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/core/src/pipeline.rs` — `run_stream` checkpoint block; `Pipeline::run` overwrite commit/abort block (the native runner already implements the target semantics — see `run_stream_native`'s `pending_bookmark`).\n- Tests: a mock overwrite sink whose `commit_overwrite` fails once + a `MemoryStateStore` assertion that the bookmark did not advance.\n\n## Edge cases\n\n- Cancelled overwrite runs (terminal flush is already skipped since #650) must also not persist.\n- Exactly-once mode is unaffected (overwrite × exactly-once is already rejected at expand time).\n- Topology sink nodes share `run_stream`, so the fix must apply per sink node.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A failed/aborted/cancelled overwrite never advances the state-store bookmark (unit-tested).\n- A successful overwrite persists the final bookmark exactly once, after commit.\n- Non-overwrite checkpoint semantics unchanged (ADR 0002 ordering intact).\n\n## Out of scope","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"56a585c7-bc38-4db1-9c04-81ac5a8325ff","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"test/reliability-program-phase2","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
