{"parentUuid":"d9b10240-1922-44f9-a8d2-5acbcd11edf8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAb278VFmwu65o5DhGSr","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HCxQnk8Wz4EDpbnEBMKoGG","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngh issue comment 662 --body \"**Scope correction before fixing:** I claimed nine sources when filing this. Checking each one, only **three** had query-time misclassification:\n\n| Crate | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| postgres, mysql, sqlite | 2 query-time sites each — **real**, now fixed |\n| duckdb | \\`duckdb config: {e}\\` / \\`DuckDB open failed ({path})\\` — genuine config/open failures, correctly \\`Config\\` |\n| spanner | 3 sites: a non-scalar parameter, a parameter overflowing INT64, and a NUMERIC cursor column — all genuinely config errors, correctly classified |\n| bigquery, redshift, mssql, mssql-cdc | no \\`Config(format!(..))\\` query sites at all |\n\nSo the fix is 6 sites across 3 crates, not ~18 across 9. Sorry for the overstatement — I grepped for the crates that *mention* a query-failure string rather than verifying each classification.\n\nConnect-time sites stay \\`Config\\` deliberately, and now say why inline: they run in \\`new()\\` at registry-build time before any data moves, which is what lets \\`validate\\`/\\`doctor\\` surface an unreachable destination as a config problem. A mid-query failure is categorically different.\n\nSQLSTATE preservation and the retriability change that depends on it are **not** in this fix — they need their own failure-injection tests, and #656 already has the pattern to reuse (\\`pg_err\\` / \\`sqlstate_of\\`). I'll file that separately rather than leave this issue open for it.\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Correct the scope claim on 662"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_read_input_tokens":803830,"output_tokens":716,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":716,"cache_read_input_tokens":803830,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1001},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HCxQnk8Wz4EDpbnEBMKoGG":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngh issue comment 662 --body \"**Scope correction before fixing:** I claimed nine sources when filing this. Checking each one, only **three** had query-time misclassification:\n\n| Crate | Verdict |\n|---|---|\n| postgres, mysql, sqlite | 2 query-time sites each — **real**, now fixed |\n| duckdb | \\`duckdb config: {e}\\` / \\`DuckDB open failed ({path})\\` — genuine config/open failures, correctly \\`Config\\` |\n| spanner | 3 sites: a non-scalar parameter, a parameter overflowing INT64, and a NUMERIC cursor column — all genuinely config errors, correctly classified |\n| bigquery, redshift, mssql, mssql-cdc | no \\`Config(format!(..))\\` query sites at all |\n\nSo the fix is 6 sites across 3 crates, not ~18 across 9. Sorry for the overstatement — I grepped for the crates that *mention* a query-failure string rather than verifying each classification.\n\nConnect-time sites stay \\`Config\\` deliberately, and now say why inline: they run in \\`new()\\` at registry-build time before any data moves, which is what lets \\`validate\\`/\\`doctor\\` surface an unreachable destination as a config problem. A mid-query failure is categor