{"parentUuid":"649979ec-1f07-4314-a88a-d2f5a2ef8589","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01XrpmmtrPkijLBZJ4ugGGrs","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":308},"type":"attachment","uuid":"4444267f-73b5-40ce-91c6-9f07454416e1","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:28:27.210Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"4444267f-73b5-40ce-91c6-9f07454416e1","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14901068 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ad5994d4-4d46-4e34-ada0-b45753f41ab9","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:28:27.222Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14901068 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"ad5994d4-4d46-4e34-ada0-b45753f41ab9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAb95KJ3jggU2Eb7WfSN","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**[#664](https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/664) is up** with three fixes, auto-merge armed. Here's the audit result you asked for:\n\n## Already fixed — closed with evidence\n\nAll four had landed in **#650** but used no closing keyword, so they stayed open:\n\n| Issue | | Evidence |\n|---|---|---|\n| **#611** | BigQuery `selectedFields` | both `tables.get` sites pass `None` |\n| **#613** | `TransformingSource` re-chunking | `max(batch_size, page_len)` |\n| **#627** | TokenEndpoint form-encoding | `TokenBodyEncoding::Form` + a wiremock header test |\n| **#640** | dataset_uri collapse | code cites `(#640)` and derives per-object URIs |\n\nTwo of those were `launch-blocker`. Your instinct was right — the tracker just lagged the code.\n\n## Not fixed — now fixed\n\n**#652** was the important one for a reliability release: a genuine **silent data-loss path**. A failed `commit_overwrite` left the destination untouched but the bookmark advanced, so the next run resumed past the gap — permanently missing rows, green runs forever. I proved the tests catch it by reverting the fix; the event log says it plainly:\n\n```\n[BeginOverwrite, Write(3), Flush, StatePut{page:0}, …]   ← no CommitOverwrite, yet page 3 durable\n```\n\n**#657** and **#662** are the same class: config accepted and silently ignored, and a runtime failure wearing a config label.\n\nTwo things worth flagging honestly:\n\n- **I corrected my own issue.** #662 claimed nine sources; verifying each, only three had real misclassification. duckdb's were genuine config errors, spanner's three were correctly typed. I'd grepped for crates *mentioning* query failures rather than checking each classification.\n- **The Kafka tests cost me three wrong hypotheses** before I stopped guessing and baselined the existing Kafka test in the same environment. It passed, which told me the broker was fine and my test was wrong. The two real causes (`StreamConsumer` needs a multi-thread runtime; the first `recv()` pays for group rebalance) are now comments in the code so the next person doesn't repeat it.\n\n## Still open\n\n| Issue | Why not now |\n|---|---|\n| **#619** | Object-store `concurrency` no-op on the streaming path — confirmed real (zero `buffer_unordered` in `stream_pages`). Performance, not correctness. |\n| **#620** | Delta `target_file_size` dead knob — confirmed real (declared and validated, never used). |\n| **#609** | Template register skips connector-config validation — real, and documented as deliberate in the code. |\n| **#623** | async_job whole-result buffering — real; a larger change. |\n| **#654** | Deferred set needs your decisions (all break YAML or API). |\n\nWant me to keep going through #619, #620, #609 and #623 in a follow-up PR while #664 is in CI? #619 and #620 are both \"knob accepted and ignored\", same class as the two I just fixed, and I'd guess a few hours each."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":725,"cache_read_input_tokens":808533,"output_tokens":1056,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":725,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1056,"cache_read_input_tokens":808533,"cache_creation_input_tokens":725,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":725},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAb94dsE612bbUeMYaku","type":"assistant","uuid":"d8fe086f-5461-4915-8dc5-6fc36c8796f8","timestamp":"2026-09-1