semver contract](feedback_additive_api_minor_bump_policy.md) — never major-bump for additive fields; extend the cargo-semver-checks lints block instead; compat wrappers for real signature changes.\n51\t- [No employer/use-case keywords in issues](feedback_no_employer_or_usecase_keywords_in_issues.md) — never \"Drivetrain\"/tenant ids/customer orgs/internal repos in public repo artifacts; generic industry framing; keep this rule OUT of tracked files.\n52\t- [Stop asking, just execute](feedback_stop_asking_just_execute.md) — when a task lists N items, fix all N and report once; don't ask \"shall I continue?\" mid-list."},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0fdef4ee-7e1a-44fe-ae6a-f987941562be","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:38:09.684Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\nNote: /Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/MEMORY.md changed on disk since you last read it. That's usually deliberate, so take it as the current state rather than reverting it; if the change looks wrong, say so rather than undoing it yourself — otherwise no need to call it out. Here are the relevant changes (shown with line numbers):\n44\t- [Pre-push gate checklist](reference_pre_push_gate_checklist.md) — the exact command set (touch changed files FIRST so clippy re-analyses, --all-targets, semver-checks, doc -D warnings, the 3 slim builds); running a subset cost CI iterations on #457/#463.\n45\t- [Adding a `use` can trip redundant_explicit_links](reference_adding_import_activates_redundant_link_lint.md) — importing an item makes a pre-existing explicit-target doc link redundant → fails Docs gate; grep+shorten after adding imports. docsrs doc-check needs nightly.\n46\t- [Validate infallible new() at the registry](feedback_validate_infallible_new_at_registry.md) — don't change a `new() -> Self` to Result (semver break); add config.validate() + call it in registry build_source for infallible sources, in new() for fallible ones.\n47\t- [Repo moved