{"parentUuid":"d0c35bd5-3e88-4704-9337-30b679d86e71","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAdMoFzSv8cqwawM2jtW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Found the real bug** — and it's in the code, not the examples:\n\n```rust\n#[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"HashMap::is_empty\")]   // ← belongs to `headers`\npub headers: HashMap<String, String>,\npub query_params: HashMap<String, String>,                      // ← NO attributes at all\n```\n\n`query_params` is missing `#[serde(default)]`, so it's **required** — while `headers` and `query_params_multi` both have it. Any rest config omitting it fails to deserialize, meaning `faucet run` fails on those examples today:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":876969,"output_tokens":1396,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":710},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1396,"cache_read_input_tokens":876969,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfAdMmzbTTHX4JCkgP4Te","type":"assistant","uuid":"f56d656a-686f-440a-a124-cff85554253d","timestamp":"2026-09-18T08:57:47.202Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"f56d656a-686f-440a-a124-cff85554253d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAdMoFzSv8cqwawM2jtW","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Ddv4KfgJAfopP4moxAoAkN","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nsed -n '71,82p' crates/source/rest/src/config.rs\necho \"=== which other rest fields lack a default? (declared without a preceding serde/doc attr)\"\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport re\ns=open(\"crates/source/rest/src/config.rs\").read()\ni=s.index(\"pub struct RestStreamConfig {\")\nj=s.index(\"\\n}\", i)\nbody=s[i:j]\nlines=body.split(\"\\n\")\nmissing=[]\nfor k,l in enumerate(lines):\n    m=re.match(r'\\s*pub (\\w+):', l)\n    if not m: continue\n    # walk back over doc comments/attrs to find whether a serde default exists\n    has=False\n    p=k-1\n    while p>=0 and (lines[p].strip().startswith(\"///\") or lines[p].strip().startswith(\"#[\") or lines[p].strip()==\"\"):\n        if \"serde(\" in lines[p] and \"default\" in lines[p]: has=True\n        if re.match(r'\\s*pub \\w+:', lines[p]): break\n        p-=1\n    if not has: missing.append(m.group(1))\nprint(\"no serde default:\", missing)\nPY","description":"Audit which rest fields lack a serde default"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_read_input_tokens":876969,"output_tokens":1396,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":710},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1396,"cache_read_input_tokens":876969,"cache_creation_input_tokens":0,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"type":"messa