{"parentUuid":"6ca8e410-eea1-46f8-9029-bc28ac905a69","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"PostToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_013HmNzYmZUFuR9vZbbya4aJ","hookEvent":"PostToolUse","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"tool_complete\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"tool_name\\\":\\\"Bash\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-post-tool-use.sh","durationMs":293},"type":"attachment","uuid":"45fd9b6c-95ff-4457-9331-c350b82795aa","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:37:10.676Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"45fd9b6c-95ff-4457-9331-c350b82795aa","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14875781 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"d5554ee4-8a00-493d-9ab4-903d629a470d","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:37:10.693Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14875781 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"d5554ee4-8a00-493d-9ab4-903d629a470d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAgP4ApMofWK6xjfLYUt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01VUwtfpRoqZfz1UXyRprw5z","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(cli): deserialize connector configs at validate/register time\n\n`faucet validate` and `faucet template register` never deserialized a\nconnector's `config` — it stayed an opaque `serde_json::Value` until\n`build_source`/`build_sink` ran at execution time. So a structurally wrong\nconnector block passed validation, registered, launched, and only failed on the\nfirst triggered run (#609).\n\nAdds `registry::validate_{source,sink}_config`: deserialize into the\nconnector's typed config and, for the 37 types that expose one, call\n`validate()`. No credentials are resolved, no pool is built, no connection is\nopened — live reachability stays `faucet doctor`'s job. Discovery rows are\nskipped, since `NodeRole::Discovery` has no sink.\n\nCalling `validate()` is the load-bearing half, not a nicety. The reported repro\n— `MssqlConnectionConfig` is `#[serde(flatten)]`, so nesting it under a\n`connection:` key — **deserializes cleanly** into a config with no connection\nstring at all; only `validate()` notices. It is passed as a closure because\n`validate()` is an inherent method on each config type, not a trait one.\n\n## What turning it on found\n\nThe gate immediately failed against our own tree, which is the point of it.\n\n**Two missing serde defaults.** `RestStreamConfig::query_params` and\n`XmlStreamConfig::query_params` had **no `#[serde(default)]`** while their\nsiblings `headers` and `query_params_multi` both did — so they were *required*,\nand any config omitting them could not deserialize. Several shipped examples\nomitted them and therefore could not run at all.\n\n**`RestStreamConfig` required 22 fields.** A config had to spell out\n`max_retries`, `retry_backoff`, `tolerated_http_errors`, `primary_keys`,\n`partitions`, `schema_sample_size` and more before it would deserialize — which\nis why the examples are so verbose, and why several still missed one field. Each\nnow defaults to the value the existing `Default` impl already specified. Done\nper-field rather than with a container-level `#[serde(default)]`: the container\nform also empties the JSON Schema's `required` array, which silently broke\n`faucet init` (every field got commented out, so the generated `config:` was\nempty). `base_url` stays required in both serde and the schema, and\n`validate()` now reports it with a message naming the knob instead of serde's\nbare \"missing field\". Same treatment for `S3SourceConfig`, where only `bucket`\nis genuinely required.\n\n**11 examples used the wrong form for `column_mapping`.** postgres/mysql/sqlite\ntag that enum *externally*, so `type: jsonb` is not a thing — `jsonb: {column: x}`\nis. mssql is `#[serde(tag = \"type\")]`, so its examples were already correct and\nare untouched.\n\n**8 examples mis-spelled internally-tagged enum variants** — `{type: none}`,\n`{type: incremental}`, and one bare `pagination: none` — against PascalCase\nvariants (`None`, `Incremental`). Some examples already had it right, so this\nwas inconsistency rather than a convention.\n\n**4 more had outright invalid fields**: `url:` (never a REST field),\n`endpoint:`, PageNumber's fields nested under `config:`, and an S3\n`file_format` wrapped in `{type: …}`.\n\nAll 115 shipped examples now validate; before this, 16 of them could not run.\nTwo test fixtures used `url: http://x` and are corrected; two template-store\nassertions moved from `config.url` to `config.base_url`/`path` (their subject is\nparam binding, not field naming).\n\n`cargo semver-checks`: no semver update required for rest, s3 or xml — making a\nrequired field optional is additive.\n\nCloses #609\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the 609 fix and all its findings"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_read_input_tokens":934376,"output_tokens":1441,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1441,"cache_read_input_tokens":934376,"cache_creation_input_tokens":787,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":787},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01VUwtfpRoqZfz1UXyRprw5z":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(cli): deserialize connector configs at validate/register time\n\n`faucet validate` and `faucet template register` never deserialized a\nconnector's `config` — it stayed an opaque `serde_json::Value` until\n`build_source`/`build_sink` ran at execution time. So a structurally wrong\nconnector block passed validation, registered, launched, and only failed on the\nfirst triggered run (#609).\n\nAdds `registry::validate_{source,sink}_config`: deserialize into the\nconnector's typed config and, for the 37 types that expose one, call\n`validate()`. No credentials are resolved, no pool is built, no connection is\nopened — live reachability stays `faucet doctor`'s job. Discovery rows are\nskipped, since `NodeRole::Discovery` has no sink.\n\nCalling `validate()` is the load-bearing half, not a nicety. The reported repro\n— `MssqlConnectionConfig` is `#[serde(flatten)]`, so nesting it under a\n`connection:` key — **deserializes cleanly** into a config with no connection\nstring at all; only `validate()` notices. It is passed as a closure because\n`validate()` is an inherent method on each config type, not a trait one.\n\n## What turning it on found\n\nThe gate immediately failed against our own tree, which is the point of it.\n\n**Two missing serde defaults.** `RestStreamConfig::query_params` and\n`XmlStreamConfig::query_params` had **no `#[serde(default)]`** while their\nsiblings `headers` and `query_params_multi` both did — so they were *required*,\nand any config omitting them could not deserialize. Several shipped examples\nomitted them and therefore could not run at all.\n\n**`RestStreamConfig` required 22 fields.** A config had to spell out\n`max_retries`, `retry_backoff`, `tolerated_http_errors`, `primary_keys`,\n`partitions`, `schema_sample_size` and more before it would deserialize — which\nis why the examples are so verbose, and why several still missed one field. Each\nnow defaults to the value the existing `Default` impl already specified. Done\nper-field rather than with a container-level `#[serde(default)]`: the container\nform also empties the JSON Schema's `required` array, which silently broke\n`faucet init` (every field got commented out, so the generated `config:` was\nempty). `base_url` stays required in both serde and the schema, and\n`validate()` now reports it with a message naming the knob instead of serde's\nbare \"missing field\". Same treatment for `S3SourceConfig`, where only `bucket`\nis genuinely required.\n\n**11 examples used the wrong form for `column_mapping`.** postgres/mysql/sqlite\ntag that enum *externally*, so `type: jsonb` is not a thing — `jsonb: {column: x}`\nis. mssql is `#[serde(tag = \"type\")]`, so its examples were already correct and\nare untouched.\n\n**8 examples mis-spelled internally-tagged enum variants** — `{type: none}`,\n`{type: incremental}`, and one bare `pagination: none` — against PascalCase\nvariants (`None`, `Incremental`). Some examples already had it right, so this\nwas inconsistency rather than a convention.\n\n**4 more had outright invalid fields**: `url:` (never a REST field),\n`endpoint:`, PageNumber's fields nested under `config:`, and an S3\n`file_format` wrapped in `{type: …}`.\n\nAll 115 shipped examples now validate; before this, 16 of them could not run.\nTwo test fixtures used `url: http://x` and are corrected; two template-store\nassertions moved from `config.url` to `config.base_url`/`path` (their subject is\nparam binding, not field naming).\n\n`cargo semver-checks`: no semver update required for rest, s3 or xml — making a\nrequired field optional is additive.\n\nCloses #609\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the 609 fix and all its findings"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAgP2gGMjRi5JWd3kcrD","type":"assistant","uuid":"00221291-73b3-4df5-84cb-405a4fb717b9","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:37:30.535Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
