{"parentUuid":"2e2397c0-e8b0-4112-bb48-1f10baaa5d56","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAgZ2xAdjEEffF6tWNcT","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Fy35nQ8V2ZnLy494PAWDak","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngh issue comment 623 --body \"Already fixed — landed in #650 (\\`fd32cf08\\`) without a closing keyword, so this stayed open. The implementation cites this issue number in its own comment.\n\n\\`stream_pages_inner\\`'s async-job branch now streams one \\`StreamPage\\` per locator page instead of accumulating:\n\n\\`\\`\\`rust\n// crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:718\n// Async-job lifecycle (#514/#623): submit → poll → resolve the fetch\n// URL once, then stream one \\`StreamPage\\` per locator-paged result set\n// (#557) instead of buffering the entire extract into a single page.\n…\n// Stream this locator page immediately — peak memory is\n// O(one page), not O(whole extract). Per-page bookmark stays\n// \\`None\\`; the incremental bookmark is emitted once at the end.\nyield faucet_core::StreamPage { records, bookmark: None };\n\\`\\`\\`\n\nThe \\`all_records.extend(...)\\` accumulator this issue pointed at is gone from that path; the one that remains (\\`fetch_partition\\`, line ~1083) is the **eager batch** API that returns a \\`Vec\\` by contract, not the streaming path a real run drives.\n\nIt also matches the proposed design on the loop guard: the next locator is only adopted when it differs, so a repeating locator terminates rather than spinning.\n\nIncremental bookmarking behaves as the issue's 'carry a resumable bookmark' point asked, via #630: the bookmark is captured *before* submit and emitted once at the end, so the pipeline persists it only after the sink confirms.\" >/dev/null && gh issue close 623 --reason completed >/dev/null && echo \"closed #623\"","descripti