{"parentUuid":"ba0858ef-6214-4369-b778-f77934f2feeb","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01VFEFV6TgHMy7PMFTZhqGRT","type":"tool_result","content":"=== stale iceberg 0.9.1 refs the issue flagged:\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/schema.rs:7://! iceberg-rust 0.9.1). The pipeline still hands the sink `serde_json::Value`\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/sink.rs:17://! iceberg-rust 0.9.1 already handles benign races: on a retryable conflict it\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/sink.rs:373:    /// `Transaction::commit` in iceberg-rust 0.9.1 already includes an internal\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/writer.rs:90:        // Arrow `SchemaRef`. The iceberg 0.9.1 API uses the table's current\n.claude/rules/architecture.md:41:| `faucet-sink-iceberg` | `crates/sink/iceberg/` | Apache Iceberg sink — append snapshots via REST/Glue/SQL/HMS catalogs; local + cloud (S3/GCS via `storage-opendal`) warehouses; Parquet data files, `fast_append` transactions. Commit-conflict retry/metadata-refresh is handled by iceberg-rust 0.9.1 internally (tunable via `commit.retry.*` table props); opt-in `cleanup_orphans_on_failure` deletes uploaded data files on a *definitive* commit loss (`CatalogCommitConflicts`/`DataInvalid`), never on an ambiguous one (#193) |\n.claude/rules/architecture.md:115:- `traits.rs` — `Source` (primary: `fetch_with_context()`, convenience: `fetch_all()`, plus `state_key()` / `apply_start_bookmark()` for resumable runs, `supports_exactly_once()` + the derived typed `replay_guarantee()` (#292), and `capture_resume_position()` — capture the source's current replication position as a bookmark `Value` without consuming changes; default `None`, overridden by postgres-cdc/mysql-cdc/mongodb-cdc and used by `faucet replicate` to anchor CDC before a bulk snapshot, #189) and `Sink` async traits. Both expose `config_schema(&self) -> Value`, `connector_name(&self) -> &'static str` (default returns stripped `type_name`; built-in connectors override with friendly labels like `\"rest\"`, `\"jsonl\"`), and `check(&self, &CheckContext) -> Result<CheckReport, _>` (preflight probe for `faucet doctor`, #126), plus `supports_discover()` / `discover() -> Vec<DatasetDescriptor>` (live catalog introspection for `faucet discover`, #211 — default: typed unsupported error; overridden by the 11 catalog-backed sources: postgres, mysql, mssql, sqlite, mongodb, elasticsearch, bigquery, snowflake, spanner, s3, gcs). `Source::check` defaults to pulling one page via `stream_pages` (generic real-read-path probe; overridden by webhook/websocket/postgres-cdc/kafka where a page-pull would block or have side effects); `Sink::check` defaults to `not_implemented` and each built-in sink overrides it with a non-mutating connect/auth/metadata probe. `Sink` also exposes three defaulted, object-safe schema-drift methods (#194): `current_schema() -> Option<Value>` (the sink's live destination schema as an `infer_schema`-shaped object; default `None` = schemaless / drift-inert), `supports_schema_evolution() -> bool` (default `false`), and `evolve_schema(&SchemaEvolution)` (default = typed \"unsupported\" error). Seven sinks override all three (postgres/mysql/mssql/sqlite/bigquery/elasticsearch/spanner); iceberg overrides only `current_schema` (evolve blocked on iceberg-rust 0.9.1, #255). Object-safe — no associated types, no generics on trait methods.\n=== actual version:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c84b6edc-d8e4-4d99-9eb7-6de5f49b09bd","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:43:58.828Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"=== stale iceberg 0.9.1 refs the issue flagged:\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/schema.rs:7://! iceberg-rust 0.9.1). The pipeline still hands the sink `serde_json::Value`\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/sink.rs:17://! iceberg-rust 0.9.1 already handles benign races: on a retryable conflict it\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/sink.rs:373:    /// `Transaction::commit` in iceberg-rust 0.9.1 already includes an internal\ncrates/sink/iceberg/src/writer.rs:90:        // Arrow `SchemaRef`. The iceberg 0.9.1 API uses the table's current\n.claude/rules/architecture.md:41:| `faucet-sink-iceberg` | `crates/sink/iceberg/` | Apache Iceberg sink — append snapshots via REST/Glue/SQL/HMS catalogs; local + cloud (S3/GCS via `storage-opendal`) warehouses; Parquet data files, `fast_append` transactions. Commit-conflict retry/metadata-refresh is handled by iceberg-rust 0.9.1 internally (tunable via `commit.retry.*` table props); opt-in `cleanup_orphans_on_failure` deletes uploaded data files on a *definitive* commit loss (`CatalogCommitConflicts`/`DataInvalid`), never on an ambiguous one (#193) |\n.claude/rules/architecture.md:115:- `traits.rs` — `Source` (primary: `fetch_with_context()`, convenience: `fetch_all()`, plus `state_key()` / `apply_start_bookmark()` for resumable runs, `supports_exactly_once()` + the derived typed `replay_guarantee()` (#292), and `capture_resume_position()` — capture the source's current replication position as a bookmark `Value` without consuming changes; default `None`, overridden by postgres-cdc/mysql-cdc/mongodb-cdc and used by `faucet replicate` to anchor CDC before a bulk snapshot, #189) and `Sink` async traits. Both expose `config_schema(&self) -> Value`, `connector_name(&self) -> &'static str` (default returns stripped `type_name`; built-in connectors override with friendly labels like `\"rest\"`, `\"jsonl\"`), and `check(&self, &CheckContext) -> Result<CheckReport, _>` (preflight probe for `faucet doctor`, #126), plus `supports_discover()` / `discover() -> Vec<DatasetDescriptor>` (live catalog introspection for `faucet discover`, #211 — default: typed unsupported error; overridden by the 11 catalog-backed sources: postgres, mysql, mssql, sqlite, mongodb, elasticsearch, bigquery, snowflake, spanner, s3, gcs). `Source::check` defaults to pulling one page via `stream_pages` (generic real-read-path probe; overridden by webhook/websocket/postgres-cdc/kafka where a page-pull would block or have side effects); `Sink::check` defaults to `not_implemented` and each built-in sink overrides it with a non-mutating connect/auth/metadata probe. `Sink` also exposes three defaulted, object-safe schema-drift methods (#194): `current_schema() -> Option<Value>` (the sink's live destination schema as an `infer_schema`-shaped object; default `None` = schemaless / drift-inert), `supports_schema_evolution() -> bool` (default `false`), and `evolve_schema(&SchemaEvolution)` (default = typed \"unsupported\" error). Seven sinks override all three (postgres/mysql/mssql/sqlite/bigquery/elasticsearch/spanner); iceberg overrides only `current_schema` (evolve blocked on iceberg-rust 0.9.1, #255). Object-safe — no associated types, no generics on trait methods.\n=== actual version:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"ba0858ef-6214-4369-b778-f77934f2feeb","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
