{"parentUuid":"9b24cd39-af46-487f-94c8-ceb1b83b56cd","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14847871 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"8471868d-ba39-47cd-aba0-1aa46ecd5e67","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:47:05.573Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14847871 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"8471868d-ba39-47cd-aba0-1aa46ecd5e67","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAh8w1BXVKAb6HqAKgSh","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01L7poaRXicrYbPnYAj8sUFS","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0\ncargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-sink-delta --baseline-rev origin/main 2>&1 | grep -Ei \"summary|required|no semver\" | head -2\ngit add crates/sink/delta crates/sink/iceberg\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(sink-delta): make target_file_size real, bounding peak memory\n\n`target_file_size` was declared in the config and validated (a zero was\nrejected) and then **never read** (#620). `RecordBatchWriter::for_table` was\nbuilt with no sizing, and the only `flush_and_commit` came at end-of-run —\nso a bulk load, which emits no bookmarks and therefore triggers no intermediate\nflush, buffered the **entire dataset** as in-memory parquet. A large table\ncould OOM, and the documented knob did nothing.\n\ndelta-rs offers no target-size parameter: `RecordBatchWriter` writes exactly\none data file per commit, so file size is governed entirely by flush cadence.\nWiring the knob and bounding memory are therefore the same change. The sink now\nchecks `writer.buffer_len()` after each chunk and commits early once it reaches\n`target_file_size`, on both the `Value` and the columnar path. The existing\ncommit logic is factored into `commit_buffered` so `flush` and the size-roll\nare the same operation, differing only in when they fire.\n\nUnset stays unbounded — one commit per run, exactly as before — so nobody\nrelying on the current behaviour is surprised. The cost when set is a few\ncommits per run instead of one, which is the trade the knob exists to offer.\n\nFive tests, asserting through the observable consequence (the number of parquet\ndata files the table ends up with) rather than by inspecting internals: a small\ntarget rolls into several files *and* preserves every row with no gaps or\nduplicates; an unset target still produces exactly one file; a target larger\nthan the data produces one file (it is a ceiling, not a mandate to split);\nrolling across multiple `write_batch` calls stays exact; and a zero target is\nstill rejected.\n\nThe first test needed `batch_size` set to chunk within one `write_batch` —\nwithout it a single 2000-row chunk buffers the whole page before the first size\ncheck, which is precisely the O(whole dataset) behaviour being capped. Worth\nnoting in case someone later wonders why the test sets it.\n\nAlso corrects the stale `iceberg-rust 0.9.1` references this issue flagged —\nthe workspace pins `iceberg 0.10.0` (four sites in `crates/sink/iceberg/` plus\nthe architecture reference).\n\nCommit coalescing across CDC transactions (the issue's second half) is **not**\nhere: it changes the flush/bookmark cadence in `crates/core/src/pipeline.rs`\nand has to reconcile with per-transaction durability and the exactly-once token\nmodel, so it needs its own design and failure-injection tests rather than\nriding along with a sink fix.\n\nAddresses #620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the delta fix","timeout":900000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":947,"cache_read_input_tokens":961732,"output_tokens":1247,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":947,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1247,"cache_read_input_tokens":961732,"cache_creation_input_tokens":947,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":947},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01L7poaRXicrYbPnYAj8sUFS":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nTOOL=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin\nexport PATH=$TOOL:$PATH RUSTC=$TOOL/rustc CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0\ncargo semver-checks check-release -p faucet-sink-delta --baseline-rev origin/main 2>&1 | grep -Ei \"summary|required|no semver\" | head -2\ngit add crates/sink/delta crates/sink/iceberg\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(sink-delta): make target_file_size real, bounding peak memory\n\n`target_file_size` was declared in the config and validated (a zero was\nrejected) and then **never read** (#620). `RecordBatchWriter::for_table` was\nbuilt with no sizing, and the only `flush_and_commit` came at end-of-run —\nso a bulk load, which emits no bookmarks and therefore triggers no intermediate\nflush, buffered the **entire dataset** as in-memory parquet. A large table\ncould OOM, and the documented knob did nothing.\n\ndelta-rs offers no target-size parameter: `RecordBatchWriter` writes exactly\none data file per commit, so file size is governed entirely by flush cadence.\nWiring the knob and bounding memory are therefore the same change. The sink now\nchecks `writer.buffer_len()` after each chunk and commits early once it reaches\n`target_file_size`, on both the `Value` and the columnar path. The existing\ncommit logic is factored into `commit_buffered` so `flush` and the size-roll\nare the same operation, differing only in when they fire.\n\nUnset stays unbounded — one commit per run, exactly as before — so nobody\nrelying on the current behaviour is surprised. The cost when set is a few\ncommits per run instead of one, which is the trade the knob exists to offer.\n\nFive tests, asserting through the observable consequence (the number of parquet\ndata files the table ends up with) rather than by inspecting internals: a small\ntarget rolls into several files *and* preserves every row with no gaps or\nduplicates; an unset target still produces exactly one file; a target larger\nthan the data produces one file (it is a ceiling, not a mandate to split);\nrolling across multiple `write_batch` calls stays exact; and a zero target is\nstill rejected.\n\nThe first test needed `batch_size` set to chunk within one `write_batch` —\nwithout it a single 2000-row chunk buffers the whole page before the first size\ncheck, which is precisely the O(whole dataset) behaviour being capped. Worth\nnoting in case someone later wonders why the test sets it.\n\nAlso corrects the stale `iceberg-rust 0.9.1` references this issue flagged —\nthe workspace pins `iceberg 0.10.0` (four sites in `crates/sink/iceberg/` plus\nthe architecture reference).\n\nCommit coalescing across CDC transactions (the issue's second half) is **not**\nhere: it changes the flush/bookmark cadence in `crates/core/src/pipeline.rs`\nand has to reconcile with per-transaction durability and the exactly-once token\nmodel, so it needs its own design and failure-injection tests rather than\nriding along with a sink fix.\n\nAddresses #620\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the delta fix","timeout":900000}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAh8uBnq5zDQQa4aXGgh","type":"assistant","uuid":"70a6173d-d835-490e-b003-cf96c78b6543","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:47:21.635Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
