{"parentUuid":"0fd99a19-463f-4eaf-b87c-758b348fbc3c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\n\nThe conversation spans several explicit user requests, in order:\n\n1. **(Continuation)** Finish PR #656 — the remaining principles-audit (#654) fixes, all in one PR.\n2. **\"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/651 — Let's solve this now completely.\"** Implement the tier-1 integration-test program (Categories A–G).\n3. **\"do all of it since we picked it already\"** — complete every remaining #651 item, no deferrals.\n4. **\"dont leave anything else on the table\"** (sent mid-turn).\n5. **BSON question:** \"MongoDB uses BB as Bison. Is this a very good format for representing our current data as well for all the transfers and everything? What do you think? Maybe between source and sync, we can use Bison, or will it be challenging and may cause incompatibility at certain places?\" — an architecture opinion request.\n6. **Bug-issue audit:** \"There are some GitHub issues created which are marked as bugs. I think some of them are solved already. Can you please check if some of them are already solved and we just forgot to link them to the PR? In case those are not solved, please pick them up and solve them right now. I'm going to make a release which is going to ensure the reliability of the existing features that we have. That is the main part of the release.\"\n7. **\"Yes, please fix all of those together. Why are you asking me again and again, man? Please just fix all of those together.\"** — explicit instruction to stop asking permission and execute the full list (#619, #620, #609, #623).\n\n**Security/constraint instructions that MUST remain in force (verbatim intent):**\n- **\"Don't ever use the Pawan-DT git account on this repo... It should always use the other ID.\"** Applies to commits, `gh` commands, and pushes. Correct identity: `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>`; GitHub account renamed to `pecsorabs` (id 35492860). `pawan-dt` / `pawan@drivetrain.ai` must never appear.\n- Never use employer/customer/tenant identifiers (e.g. \"Drivetrain\") in public repo artifacts; that rule lives in local memory only, never in tracked files.\n- \"Adding an API should not bump the version\" — never bump a major unilaterally.\n- ≥95% patch coverage is a hard floor.\n- Always merge with an explicit `--subject`/`--body`; never accept GitHub's auto-generated squash message (it injects `Co-authored-by` trailers from branch commit authors — it tainted #650 and #653).\n- Harness attribution (supersedes earlier guidance): commits end with `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>`; PR bodies end with `🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)`. This conflicts with the user's standing \"no Claude co-author trailer in this repo\" rule; I flagged it and asked whether to strip it — **still unanswered**.\n\n## 2. Key Technical Concepts\n\n- PRINCIPLES.md P1–P10 (notably §2 correctness-lives-once-in-core, §5 no-hidden-state/magic-strings, §6 typed-errors-never-message-grep, §7 pure-core+tested, §10 docs-move-with-code)\n- Declared semver contract via `[package.metadata.cargo-semver-checks.lints]`; additive API = minor\n- Boundary-precise failure injection: shared ordered `EventLog`, `Boundary` enum, `ScriptedSink`/`ScriptedStateStore`/`PagedSource`\n- Fidelity corpus + `Tolerance` (externally-stated destination limitations)\n- ADR 0002 checkpoint ordering (write → flush → persist bookmark); ADR 0011 cooperative cancellation\n- Exactly-once: atomic-watermark (commit token) vs keyed-upsert mechanisms\n- serde tagging: **externally tagged** (`rename_all` only) vs **internally tagged** (`tag = \"type\"`) vs **adjacently tagged** (`{type, config}`) — the root of 19 example bugs\n- Container-level `#[serde(default)]` empties the JSON Schema's `required` array → breaks `faucet init`\n- `rdkafka` `StreamConsumer` needs a multi-thread runtime; first `recv()` pays JoinGroup/SyncGroup rebalance\n- delta-rs `RecordBatchWriter` writes one file per commit → file size governed by flush cadence; `buffer_len()` is the observable\n- Toolchain pinning: `RUSTC=~/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/rustc` + that dir's cargo\n- `DOCKER_HOST=unix://$HOME/.colima/default/docker.sock` for testcontainers; SQL Server image is x86-only\n\n## 3. Files and Code Sections\n\n**`crates/conformance/src/scripted.rs` (new, ~900 lines)** — the reliability harness foundation. `Event`, `EventLog` (with `writes_before_each_bookmark`), `Boundary { Never, Write(n), Flush, StatePut(n), CommitOverwrite }`, `ScriptedSink` (independently-advertised capabilities incl. `.idempotent()`, `.replay_safe()`, `.keyed()`, `.overwrite()`, `.cleanup()`, `.with_write_delay()`, `.rearm()`), `ScriptedStateStore`, `PagedSource` (per-page bookmarks, `failing_after(n)`), and the reusable guarantee assertion:\n```rust\npub fn assert_bookmarks_backed_by_writes(log: &EventLog, records_claimed: impl Fn(&Value) -> usize) {\n    let mut confirmed = 0usize;\n    for (i, event) in log.events().into_iter().enumerate() {\n        match event {\n            Event::Write(n) | Event::IdempotentWrite { records: n, .. } => confirmed += n,\n            Event::StatePut { ref value, .. } => {\n                let claimed = records_claimed(value);\n                assert!(claimed <= confirmed, \"durability violated at event {i}: ...\");\n            }\n            _ => {}\n        }\n    }\n}\n```\n\n**`crates/conformance/src/fidelity.rs` (new)** — `ROW_KEY = \"__fidelity_id\"`, `corpus()` (6 hazard classes), `flat_corpus()`, `Tolerance` (`skipping`, `float_epsilon`, `empty_string_becomes_null`, `lenient_scalar_kind`), `Mismatch`, `diff_round_trip`, `assert_round_trip`. Explicitly checks `-0.0` sign bit since `json!(-0.0) == json!(0.0)`.\n\n**`crates/core/src/pipeline.rs`** — the #652 fix. Added in `run_stream`:\n```rust\nlet defer_bookmarks = sink.is_overwrite();\n```\nguarding two `store.put` sites with `if !defer_bookmarks && let (Some(store), Some(key)) = ...`; and in `Pipeline::run`'s overwrite finalize:\n```rust\nOk(_) if !cancelled => {\n    wrapped_sink.commit_overwrite().await?;\n    if let (Some(store), Some(key), Ok(res)) = (\n        wrapped_state_store.as_ref(), state_key.as_ref(), &run_result,\n    ) && let Some(bm) = res.bookmark.as_ref() { store.put(key, bm).await?; }\n}\n```\n(`state_key` needed `.clone()` at the `opts.with_state` site.)\n\n**`crates/sink/kafka/src/sink.rs`** — the #657 fix. New `RecordRouting { key, partition, headers }` struct, `owned_headers()` (JSON `null` → valueless header), headers extracted per record and attached on both produce paths; commit-token record explicitly gets `RecordRouting { key: Some(scope), ..Default::default() }`.\n\n**`crates/sink/kafka/src/extract.rs`** — `headers_at` now preserves `Value::Null` instead of stringifying to `\"null\"`.\n\n**`crates/source/{postgres,mysql,sqlite}/src/stream.rs`** — the #662 fix: 6 query-time sites `FaucetError::Config` → `FaucetError::Source`; connect-time sites kept as `Config` with an inline rationale.\n\n**`cli/src/registry.rs`** — the #609 fix. `check` / `check_with` helpers plus generated `validate_source_config` / `validate_sink_config` dispatchers (37 arms upgraded to `check_with::<T, _, _>(\"kind\", name, config, |c| c.validate())`).\n\n**`cli/src/commands/validate.rs`** — `check_connector_configs(&nodes)` called after `check_transforms`, skipping `NodeRole::Discovery` rows.\n\n**`cli/src/templates/store.rs`** — same validation in `register`; fixtures corrected from `url:` to `base_url:`/`path:`; two assertions moved off `config.url`.\n\n**`crates/source/rest/src/config.rs`** — per-field `#[serde(default)]`/`#[serde(default = \"…\")]` on ~20 fields with 9 new default fns (`default_method` → GET, `default_max_pages` → Some(100), `default_timeout`, `default_max_retries` → 3, `default_retry_backoff`, `default_replication_method` → FullTable, `default_schema_sample_size` → 100, `default_pagination` → None, `default_auth`); `query_params` gained its missing default; `validate()` gained a `base_url` non-empty guard.\n\n**`crates/source/xml/src/config.rs`** — `query_params` gained `#[serde(default)]`.\n\n**`crates/source/s3/src/config.rs`** — `#[serde(default)]` on prefix/region/endpoint_url/file_format/max_objects, `#[serde(default = \"default_concurrency\")]` on concurrency.\n\n**`crates/sink/delta/src/sink.rs`** — the #620 fix: extracted `commit_buffered(&self, state)` and added\n```rust\nasync fn roll_if_over_target(&self, state: &mut SinkState) -> Result<(), FaucetError> {\n    let Some(target) = self.config.target_file_size else { return Ok(()) };\n    let buffered = match state.writer.as_ref() { Some(w) => w.buffer_len(), None => return Ok(()) };\n    if buffered >= target { self.commit_buffered(state).await?; }\n    Ok(())\n}\n```\ncalled after each write on both `Value` and columnar paths.\n\n**19 `cli/examples/*.yaml`** — corrected `column_mapping` external tagging (11), enum variant casing (8), and invalid fields (`url:`, `endpoint:`, nested PageNumber `config:`, s3 `file_format: {type: …}`).\n\n**`.github/workflows/ci.yml`** — new required `reliability` job (always runs, heavy steps gated at step level).\n\n**`docs/book/src/operations/reliability-testing.md`** (new) + SUMMARY.md + `docs/contributing/testing.md` cross-link.\n\n## 4. Errors and Fixes\n\n- **Orphaned `ObjectVerifySpec`**: a workstream added it plus a `#[serde(flatten)]` on 3 object-store configs (a major semver break I'd already reverted), leaving the type exported-but-unused with docs describing a nonexistent design, plus a broken intra-doc link `Self::verify`. Deleted the type, re-export, tests and 3 README links; fixed the link.\n- **Exactly-once control arm**: forgot `.failing_at(Boundary::StatePut(1))`, so the \"control\" ran clean and the assertion fired on a healthy run. Added the injection and made it a true side-by-side.\n- **`faucet_core::tokio_util::sync::CancellationToken`** doesn't exist → `faucet_core::CancellationToken`.\n- **`unwrap_state` returns `(Option<Value>, u64)`** not an Option → used `.0`.\n- **clippy `loop counter`** on `emitted_here` → `.enumerate()`.\n- **`NodeReport` is `#[non_exhaustive]`** so tests couldn't construct one → changed `build_summary` to take `(&HashMap<String,usize>, &[(&str,&str)])`.\n- **Kafka header tests returned 0 messages — three wrong hypotheses** (missing broker env vars; current-thread runtime; both partially relevant). Stopped guessing and **baselined the existing `integration.rs` Kafka test, which passed** — proving the broker was fine. Real cause: my 5s per-`recv()` timeout gave up during the consumer-group rebalance; the working test uses 30s. Both real causes are now code comments.\n- **`headers_at` stringified `null` to `\"null\"`** making my valueless-header arm unreachable. Verified no existing test asserted the old behaviour, then changed it to preserve `Value::Null`.\n- **clippy 8-argument limit** on `enqueue_in_txn` → introduced `RecordRouting` rather than an `allow`.\n- **Container-level `#[serde(default)]` on `RestStreamConfig` broke `faucet init`** (emptied the schema's `required`, so init commented out every field and emitted `config:` = Null). Reverted to per-field defaults, keeping `base_url` required in serde *and* schema.\n- **Duplicate serde attributes** on `request_delay`/`timeout` from my bulk insertion → folded into the existing attrs.\n- **Unused `default_response_format`** (field already had `#[serde(default)]`) → removed.\n- **Template fixtures used `url: http://x`** (never a REST field) and validation ran on discovery-row sinks → fixed fixtures; skipped `NodeRole::Discovery`.\n- **Delta rolling test saw 1 file**: a single 2000-row chunk buffers everything then rolls once. Set `batch_size = 200` so the roll is checked *within* one `write_batch` — the actual memory-bounding property.\n- **My own #662 issue overstated scope** (claimed 9 sources; only 3 had query-time sites). Posted a correction comment.\n- **User feedback — repeated permission-asking**: *\"Why are you asking me again and again, man?\"* Recorded as memory `feedback_stop_asking_just_execute.md` and stopped asking; now fix all enumerated items and report once.\n\n## 5. Problem Solving\n\n**Completed:** #656 merged clean (first merge on this repo to avoid the `pawan-dt` trailer injection, via explicit `--subject`/`--body`); #659 merged; #651 fully closed across #660/#661/#663 with 74 tests, harness, required CI gate, docs and a per-item audit; branch protection updated to 9 required contexts.\n\n**Bug audit results:** 5 already-fixed bugs closed with commit evidence (#611, #613, #627, #640, #623 — all landed in #650 `fd32cf08` without closing keywords). 3 fixed in PR #664 (#652, #657, #662). 2 fixed and committed locally (#609 `40a43a2a`, #620 `f94cc6e9`). #619 in progress.\n\n**Notable findings reported:** Postgres `DOUBLE PRECISION` preserves `-0.0` but JSONB normalises it via `numeric` (so \"Postgres loses negative zero\" is false in general, true for the document path); MongoDB BSON is fully faithful; `query_params` was accidentally required in two sources; `RestStreamConfig` required 22 fields; 16 shipped examples could not run.\n\n**BSON recommendation:** advised against — no source→sink serialization exists (in-memory `Vec<Value>`), `serde_json::Number` already preserves i64 exactly (proven by zero-tolerance JSONL/BSON tests), decimals already travel as exact strings (`postgres/stream.rs:111` + `pg_bind_text`), and Arrow (`faucet_core::columnar`) already is the binary columnar path. Offered to file a typed-decimal improvement — **unanswered**.\n\n## 6. All User Messages\n\n- \"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context…\" (continuation preamble with prior summary)\n- \"continue\" (twice, via `/autocompact` and `/compact` local-command output)\n- \"try now?\"\n- \"Continue from where you left off.\"\n- \"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/issues/651 \\n\\nLet's solve this now completely.\"\n- \"Yes, please fix all of those together.\" *(note: this appears as part of message 7 below)*\n- \"do all of it since we picked it already\"\n- \"dont leave anything else on the table\"\n- \"MongoDB uses BB as Bison. Is this a very good format for representing our current data as well for all the transfers and everything? What do you think? Maybe between source and sync, we can use Bison, or will it be challenging and may cause incompatibility at certain places?\"\n- \"There are some GitHub issues created which are marked as bugs. I think some of them are solved already. Can you please check if some of them are already solved and we just forgot to link them to the PR? In case those are not solved, please pick them up and solve them right now. I'm going to make a release which is going to ensure the reliability of the existing features that we have. That is the main part of the release.\"\n- \"Yes, please fix all of those together. Why are you asking me again and again, man? Please just fix all of those together.\"\n- (A `/model` command output switching to Opus 5 with \"continue\".)\n\n## 7. Pending Tasks\n\n- **#619** — Object-store sources: make `concurrency` real on the streaming path (`stream_pages`/`stream_batches` in s3/gcs/azure-blob read serially; `buffer_unordered(concurrency)` is only in the deprecated eager `fetch_with_context`); stop whole-object Parquet buffering on S3/GCS (use async `ParquetObjectReader`); add a `concurrency` field to the sftp source.\n- Push the local commits (`e12e99db`, `bd57d312`, `152af81c`, `40a43a2a`, `f94cc6e9`) to PR #664 / open PRs for #609 and #620; PR #664 is OPEN with auto-merge armed.\n- **#654** — deferred set (H9 `deny_unknown_fields` on 62 configs, H10 semver lints across 89 crates, M20–M24) still needs user decisions; all break YAML or API.\n- **Awaiting user answers:** (a) whether to strip the `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5` trailer (conflicts with their standing repo rule); (b) whether to rewrite published `main` history to remove `Co-authored-by: pawan-dt` from `6433e74b`/`fd32cf08`; (c) whether to file the typed-decimal improvement from the BSON discussion; (d) whether to add the redundant Category B/C/D coverage (my audit says it already exists).\n- Iceberg CDC commit coalescing (#620's second half) deliberately deferred — needs core `pipeline.rs` flush/bookmark cadence design.\n\n## 8. Current Work\n\nImmediately before the summary request I was starting **#619**, having just committed #620 as `f94cc6e9`. I had confirmed the bug is real: `buffer_unordered(concurrency)` appears only in `crates/source/s3/src/stream.rs:340` inside `fetch_with_context` (line 310), and a grep of the entire `stream_pages` body (lines 375–580) found **zero** occurrences of `concurrency` or `buffer_unordered`.\n\nI was reading `crates/source/s3/src/stream.rs` to understand the per-format structure inside the serial `for key in &keys` loop. Lines 396–470 showed:\n- `S3FileFormat::JsonLines` — streams line-by-line via `self.open_object_reader(key)` + `lines.next_line()`, yielding pages at `batch_size` (memory O(batch), good)\n- `S3FileFormat::RawText` — `self.read_object_text(key)` buffers the whole body, one record per object\n- `S3FileFormat::Parquet` (arrow feature, line ~468) — was about to be read\n\nI had identified the design tension: concurrency requires N objects in flight, while the JSONL path deliberately streams one object's lines to keep memory at O(batch). My working plan was to fetch bodies concurrently with a bounded look-ahead for the whole-object formats (JsonArray/RawText/Parquet) while keeping JSONL's line streaming, and to document the distinction.\n\n## 9. Optional Next Step\n\nContinue #619: implement bounded-concurrency object reads on the streaming path for s3, then gcs and azure-blob, and add the missing `concurrency` field to the sftp source.\n\nDirect quotes anchoring this task, from my most recent messages:\n\n> \"Confirmed **#619 is still real** — `buffer_unordered(concurrency)` is only in `fetch_with_context` (the batch path), not in `stream_pages` (what a real run uses)\"\n\n> \"Zero concurrency in the entire `stream_pages` body — #619 is real.\"\n\n> \"Now #619 — making `concurrency` real on the streaming path:\"\n\nAnd the user's governing instruction for this batch:\n\n> \"Yes, please fix all of those together. Why are you asking me again and again, man? Please just fix all of those together.\"\n\nPer that instruction I should complete #619 and then report once on all four (#609, #620, #623, #619) rather than checking in mid-list.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."},"isVisibleInTranscriptOnly":true,"isCompactSummary":true,"uuid":"c6220e9a-e037-44f8-b3d3-ac2b532468b2","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09:50:57.991Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"c6220e9a-e037-44f8-b3d3-ac2b532468b2","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"file","filename":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_stop_asking_just_execute.md","content":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_stop_asking_just_execute.md","content":"---\nname: stop-asking-just-execute\ndescription: \"Don't ask permission to continue work already scoped; execute the whole list, then report\"\nmetadata: \n  node_type: memory\n  type: feedback\n  originSessionId: 55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\n  modified: 2026-09-18T08:37:58.172Z\n---\n\n**Stop asking whether to continue work that is already in scope.** The user\ncalled this out directly (2026-09-18): *\"Why are you asking me again and again,\nman? Please just fix all of those together.\"*\n\nPattern that annoyed them: after finishing part of a task I listed the\nremaining items and asked \"want me to keep going?\" — repeatedly, across several\nturns. They had already said \"do all of it\" and \"don't leave anything on the\ntable\".\n\n**How to apply:** when a task enumerates N items (open bugs, audit findings, a\ncategory matrix), fix all N and report once at the end. Reserve questions for\ngenuine forks where proceeding either way would be wrong — a breaking API change\nthey must sign off on, or a destructive operation. Offering a choice I could\nhave made myself reads as stalling, not diligence.\n\nRelated: [[feedback_autonomous_push_pr_merge]],\n[[feedback_merge_green_prs_autonomously]],\n[[feedback_complete_features_no_deferring]].\n","numLines":29,"startLine":1,"totalLines":29}},"displayPath":"../../../../.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/feedback_stop_asking_just_execute.md"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"0ebcb9ce-c2ac-4e7a-91d7-bcdb379c937e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T09