{"parentUuid":"b643b12c-9805-4885-82ab-09bb8a494f50","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01PVfdYVqMi2Jk7GAouV6HgJ","type":"tool_result","content":"19:| `host` | string | — | Server hostname or IP. |\n20:| `port` | integer | `22` | Server port. |\n21:| `username` | string | — | SSH username. |\n22:| `type` / `config` | auth | — | `password` or `private_key` (see `faucet-common-sftp`). |\n23:| `known_hosts` | policy | `{ mode: accept_new }` | Host-key verification policy. |\n24:| `path` | string | — | Remote directory to list, or a single file. |\n25:| `glob` | string | none | Filename glob (`*` / `?`) applied to basenames when `path` is a directory. |\n26:| `format` | enum | `jsonl` | `jsonl` \\| `json_array` \\| `raw_text`. |\n27:| `batch_size` | integer | `1000` | Records per page; `0` = one page per file. |\n52:      batch_size: 1000\n--- highlights\n# faucet-source-sftp\n\nSFTP source connector for the [faucet-stream](https://crates.io/crates/faucet-stream)\necosystem.\n\nLists a remote directory (or reads a single file) over SFTP and streams the\nfiles as JSON Lines, JSON arrays, or raw text. JSON Lines and raw text are\ndecoded incrementally, so memory stays bounded regardless of file size; JSON\narrays are buffered per file (the closing `]` is needed to validate the\nstructure) and then chunked.\n\nConnection, authentication, and host-key verification come from\n[`faucet-common-sftp`](https://crates.io/crates/faucet-common-sftp).\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `host` | string | — | Server hostname or IP. |\n| `port` | integer | `22` | Server port. |\n| `username` | string | — | SSH username. |\n| `type` / `config` | auth | — | `password` or `private_key` (see `faucet-common-sftp`). |\n| `known_hosts` | policy | `{ mode: accept_new }` | Host-key verification policy. |\n| `path` | string | — | Remote directory to list, or a single file. |\n| `glob` | string | none | Filename glob (`*` / `?`) applied to basenames when `path` is a directory. |\n| `format` | enum | `jsonl` | `jsonl` \\| `json_array` \\| `raw_text`. |\n| `batch_size` | integer | `1000` | Records per page; `0` = one page per file. |\n\n`raw_text` emits one record per file: `{ \"path\": <remote path>, \"content\": <file text> }`.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"6bc23469-b195-4027-a526-d2dbf2985c28","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:08:10.746Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"19:| `host` | string | — | Server hostname or IP. |\n20:| `port` | integer | `22` | Server port. |\n21:| `username` | string | — | SSH username. |\n22:| `type` / `config` | auth | — | `password` or `private_key` (see `faucet-common-sftp`). |\n23:| `known_hosts` | policy | `{ mode: accept_new }` | Host-key verification policy. |\n24:| `path` | string | — | Remote directory to list, or a single file. |\n25:| `glob` | string | none | Filename glob (`*` / `?`) applied to basenames when `path` is a directory. |\n26:| `format` | enum | `jsonl` | `jsonl` \\| `json_array` \\| `raw_text`. |\n27:| `batch_size` | integer | `1000` | Records per page; `0` = one page per file. |\n52:      batch_size: 1000\n--- highlights\n# faucet-source-sftp\n\nSFTP source connector for the [faucet-stream](https://crates.io/crates/faucet-stream)\necosystem.\n\nLists a remote directory (or reads a single file) over SFTP and streams the\nfiles as JSON Lines, JSON arrays, or raw text. JSON Lines and raw text are\ndecoded incrementally, so memory stays bounded regardless of file size; JSON\narrays are buffered per file (the closing `]` is needed to validate the\nstructure) and then chunked.\n\nConnection, authentication, and host-key verification come from\n[`faucet-common-sftp`](https://crates.io/crates/faucet-common-sftp).\n\n## Configuration\n\n| Field | Type | Default | Description |\n|-------|------|---------|-------------|\n| `host` | string | — | Server hostname or IP. |\n| `port` | integer | `22` | Server port. |\n| `username` | string | — | SSH username. |\n| `type` / `config` | auth | — | `password` or `private_key` (see `faucet-common-sftp`). |\n| `known_hosts` | policy | `{ mode: accept_new }` | Host-key verification policy. |\n| `path` | string | — | Remote directory to list, or a single file. |\n| `glob` | string | none | Filename glob (`*` / `?`) applied to basenames when `path` is a directory. |\n| `format` | enum | `jsonl` | `jsonl` \\| `json_array` \\| `raw_text`. |\n| `batch_size` | integer | `1000` | Records per page; `0` = one page per file. |\n\n`raw_text` emits one record per file: `{ \"path\": <remote path>, \"content\": <file text> }`.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"b643b12c-9805-4885-82ab-09bb8a494f50","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/overwrite-bookmark-ordering","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
