{"parentUuid":"cab54e69-f4d7-483c-980a-69612cbf3d5e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAmFCbRq7YDtTmBdWiP4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The branch is on `faucet-hq` (the old remote URL redirects). Creating the PR with a same-repo head:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":295233,"output_tokens":2211,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2211,"cache_read_input_tokens":295233,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAmFBq3KYivTvW3oWXaT","type":"assistant","uuid":"564a007a-5e08-4b8d-859b-22651d3598a9","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:41:00.736Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"564a007a-5e08-4b8d-859b-22651d3598a9","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAmFCbRq7YDtTmBdWiP4","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BB9vReRcxd95uxFWi8MZKu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ncat > /tmp/pr619.md <<'BODY'\nThree more open bugs for the reliability release. All three share a shape: a\nconfig field that was declared, documented, and in two cases *validated* — and\nthen never acted on. A knob that silently does nothing is worse than a missing\none, because the operator believes the guarantee it advertises.\n\n## #609 — connector configs were never deserialized at validate time\n\n`faucet validate` (and `faucet template register`) checked an entry's *shape*\nbut never parsed it into the connector's own config type, so a misspelled or\nmalformed connector field passed validation and failed on the first page of a\nreal run — after the pipeline had been scheduled, or a template released.\n\n`registry.rs` gains `check` / `check_with` helpers plus generated\n`validate_source_config` / `validate_sink_config` dispatchers (37 kinds), and\neach entry's `validate()` now runs too. Wired into `commands/validate.rs` (after\n`check_transforms`, skipping `NodeRole::Discovery` rows, whose configs are\ncompleted at run time from parent records) and into `templates/store.rs::register`.\n\nTurning it on immediately caught real defects, which are fixed here:\n\n- **`RestStreamConfig` required 22 fields.** Only `base_url` is genuinely\n  required; the rest now carry per-field `#[serde(default)]` /\n  `#[serde(default = \"…\")]`. Deliberately *per-field* rather than a container\n  `#[serde(default)]` — the container form empties the JSON Schema's `required`\n  array, which breaks `faucet init` (it comments out every field and emits a\n  null `config:`).\n- **`query_params` was accidentally required** on the rest and xml sources.\n- **16 shipped examples could not run**: `column_mapping` written as internally\n  rather than externally tagged (11), wrong enum-variant casing (8), and fields\n  that never existed (`url:`, `endpoint:`, a nested `PageNumber` `config:`, an\n  s3 `file_format: {type: …}`).\n- Template fixtures used `url:` for the rest source, which is not a field.\n\n## #620 — `sink-delta`'s `target_file_size` was validated, then ignored\n\nThe value was rejected when zero and otherwise never read: the writer was built\nwith no sizing and the only `flush_and_commit` ran at end-of-run. A bulk source\nemits no bookmarks, so that meant **one commit per run and a parquet buffer\nholding the whole dataset** — an OOM on a large table.\n\ndelta-rs offers no target-size parameter (`RecordBatchWriter` writes exactly one\nfile per commit), so file size is governed by flush cadence and wiring the knob\n*is* the memory fix. `commit_buffered` is extracted and `roll_if_over_target`\nruns after each write on both the `Value` and columnar paths, keyed on the\nwriter's own `buffer_len()`. The tests assert it through the observable\nconsequence — the number of Delta versions and parquet files — with\n`batch_size` set below the row count so the roll is exercised *within* a single\n`write_batch`, which is the property that actually bounds memory.\n\n## #619 — `concurrency` did nothing on the object-store streaming path\n\n`buffer_unordered(concurrency)` only ever existed in the eager\n`fetch_with_context` batch path. `stream_pages` — what every real run drives —\nread objects strictly one at a time, so s3 / gcs / azure-blob accepted a\ndocumented knob and ignored it; the sftp source had no such field at all.\n\nEach source now prefetches through an **ordered** `buffered(concurrency)`\nlook-ahead:\n\n- reads overlap — a 60-object scan is >2× faster at concurrency 15, asserted\n  against MinIO with warm-up excluded so the comparison measures overlap rather\n  than client setup;\n- pages still arrive in listing order and a failing object is still blamed at\n  its own position, so concurrency changes throughput and nothing an operator\n  can observe;\n- `concurrency: 0` is clamped to 1 rather than producing a `buffered(0)` stream\n  that yields nothing forever — pinned by a test so the clamp cannot be\n  refactored into a hang.\n\nWhat the look-ahead holds differs by format, and that difference is the memory\ncontract: `json_lines` prefetches only open body readers (opening an object does\nnot download it), so peak memory stays `O(batch_size)`; `json_array` /\n`raw_text` / `parquet` hold up to `concurrency` whole bodies — the bound the\nknob already advertised. Documented per source.\n\nsftp gains `concurrency`, defaulting to **4** rather than 10: every read shares\none SSH channel and servers commonly cap concurrent handles.\n`faucet-common-sftp` re-exports the open-file handle as `SftpFile` so the source\ncan name it without depending on `russh-sftp` directly.\n\n## Scope notes\n\n- Additive only: new config fields with defaults, a new re-export, new\n  dispatcher functions. No signature changes, so this is a minor bump per the\n  declared semver contract.\n- The GCS concurrency test is `#[ignore]`d for the same reason as the rest of\n  that file — `fake-gcs-server` speaks REST while the connector uses the gRPC\n  data plane. The s3 (MinIO) and azure-blob (Azurite) suites run unignored.\n- Iceberg CDC commit coalescing, the second half of #620's original report, is\n  **not** here: it needs a `pipeline.rs` flush/bookmark cadence design rather\n  than a sink-local change. #620 is closed on the `target_file_size` defect it\n  was filed for.\n\nCloses #609\nCloses #619\nCloses #620\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\nBODY\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh pr create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --head fix/inert-config-knobs --base main \\\n --title \"fix: three inert config knobs — connector config validation, delta target_file_size, object-store concurrency\" \\\n --body-file /tmp/pr619.md 2>&1 | tail -3","description":"Create the PR","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_read_input_tokens":295233,"output_tokens":2211,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2211,"cache_read_input_tokens":295233,"cache_creation_input_tokens":495,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":495},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BB9vReRcxd95uxFWi8MZKu":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ncat > /tmp/pr619.md <<'BODY'\nThree more open bugs for the reliability release. All three share a shape: a\nconfig field that was declared, documented, and in two cases *validated* — and\nthen never acted on. A knob that silently does nothing is worse than a missing\none, because the operator believes the guarantee it advertises.\n\n## #609 — connector configs were never deserialized at validate time\n\n`faucet validate` (and `faucet template register`) checked an entry's *shape*\nbut never parsed it into the connector's own config type, so a misspelled or\nmalformed connector field passed validation and failed on the first page of a\nreal run — after the pipeline had been scheduled, or a template released.\n\n`registry.rs` gains `check` / `check_with` helpers plus generated\n`validate_source_config` / `validate_sink_config` dispatchers (37 kinds), and\neach entry's `validate()` now runs too. Wired into `commands/validate.rs` (after\n`check_transforms`, skipping `NodeRole::Discovery` r