{"parentUuid":"bcbae028-a06c-4cac-bc7c-f919150c863b","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01We34VsQ66FzsXn4PGXL7JR","type":"tool_result","content":"diff --git a/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs b/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\nindex 0289ece9..8f643028 100644\n--- a/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\n+++ b/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\n@@ -69,10 +69,16 @@ pub struct KafkaSinkConfig {\n     /// JSONPath to a flat JSON object whose entries become Kafka message\n     /// headers (values are stringified). Unset by default.\n     ///\n-    /// **Not yet applied:** the extraction helper exists and is tested, but\n-    /// the produce path does not attach the headers to the outgoing message,\n-    /// so setting this currently has no effect on what reaches the broker.\n-    /// Carry the values inside the record body until it is wired up.\n+    /// Applied on both the at-least-once and the transactional (exactly-once)\n+    /// produce paths. A JSON `null` becomes a **valueless** header rather than\n+    /// the string `\"null\"`, which is what Kafka's header model actually\n+    /// expresses. The commit-token record on the side-topic never carries these\n+    /// — it is faucet's own watermark, not a user record.\n+    ///\n+    /// A path that resolves to nothing yields no headers; one that resolves to\n+    /// a non-object fails the batch, matching [`Self::partition_path`]'s\n+    /// strictness: a header map the operator asked for and did not get is not\n+    /// something to paper over.\n     #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub headers_path: Option<String>,\n     /// What to do when [`Self::key_path`] resolves to nothing for a record:","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"944d98d4-926e-4860-97ab-355a314fdb0e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:45:02.759Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"diff --git a/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs b/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\nindex 0289ece9..8f643028 100644\n--- a/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\n+++ b/crates/sink/kafka/src/config.rs\n@@ -69,10 +69,16 @@ pub struct KafkaSinkConfig {\n     /// JSONPath to a flat JSON object whose entries become Kafka message\n     /// headers (values are stringified). Unset by default.\n     ///\n-    /// **Not yet applied:** the extraction helper exists and is tested, but\n-    /// the produce path does not attach the headers to the outgoing message,\n-    /// so setting this currently has no effect on what reaches the broker.\n-    /// Carry the values inside the record body until it is wired up.\n+    /// Applied on both the at-least-once and the transactional (exactly-once)\n+    /// produce paths. A JSON `null` becomes a **valueless** header rather than\n+    /// the string `\"null\"`, which is what Kafka's header model actually\n+    /// expresses. The commit-token record on the side-topic never carries these\n+    /// — it is faucet's own watermark, not a user record.\n+    ///\n+    /// A path that resolves to nothing yields no headers; one that resolves to\n+    /// a non-object fails the batch, matching [`Self::partition_path`]'s\n+    /// strictness: a header map the operator asked for and did not get is not\n+    /// something to paper over.\n     #[serde(default, skip_serializing_if = \"Option::is_none\")]\n     pub headers_path: Option<String>,\n     /// What to do when [`Self::key_path`] resolves to nothing for a record:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"bcbae028-a06c-4cac-bc7c-f919150c863b","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
