{"parentUuid":"5b819461-e93f-49bf-a224-869191c6e0ae","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Ri12Jrb1f2c2p7S5BGKB81","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink.md:15:iceberg-rust 0.9.1 is pre-1.0 and its writer/catalog/transaction APIs churn; **docs.rs and the GitHub `main` branch may differ from 0.9.1**. For every iceberg call, resolve the exact signature against the real 0.9.1 crate: `cargo doc -p iceberg -p iceberg-catalog-rest --no-deps` then read, or inspect `~/.cargo/registry/src/*/iceberg-0.9.1*/src/`. Trust the compiler over this plan. When a signature differs, adapt while preserving behavior. If a needed capability is genuinely absent in 0.9.1, report BLOCKED with the specific type/method.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:15:The design spec listed **Iceberg** among the evolvable sinks. Planning revealed `iceberg-rust 0.9.1`\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:1955:- Add a code comment citing the iceberg-rust 0.9.1 blocker (parallel to the existing #179/#190 comments at\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:1963:git commit -m \"feat(sink-iceberg): current_schema (evolve blocked on iceberg-rust 0.9.1)\"\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:2082:/// intentionally excluded — iceberg-rust 0.9.1 exposes no schema-evolution API.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:2306:  iceberg-rust 0.9.1 blocker.\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-10-unified-write-mode-upsert-design.md:23:- **Iceberg upsert** — needs an equality-delete writer that `iceberg-rust 0.9.1` (the pinned version) does not expose. Version-gated; relates to #179 (Iceberg overwrite). Iceberg keeps `supported_write_modes() == [Append]`.\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink-design.md:14:- **Append-only v1.** iceberg-rust 0.9.1's `Transaction` exposes only\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink-design.md:33:## Verified iceberg-rust 0.9.1 API (shape — implementer resolves exact signatures)\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-07-iceberg-cloud-warehouse-storage-design.md:49:## Background: how iceberg-rust 0.9.1 wires storage\n--- also fix the local rules file (gitignored, for future sessions)\n103:**Capable sinks** (each overrides `Sink::supported_write_modes()` to return `[Append, Upsert, Delete]`; the trait default is `[Append]`): **postgres, sqlite, mysql, mssql** (require column-mapping mode — `auto_map` for postgres/mysql/sqlite, `auto_columns` for mssql — plus a UNIQUE/PK on `key`), **mongodb, elasticsearch** (schemaless; `key` → match filter / `_id`), and **bigquery** (in-place `MERGE … USING (SELECT … FROM UNNEST(JSON_QUERY_ARRAY(@payload)))` — no staging table; `key` must be real table columns; the target table must already exist with a defined schema), and **spanner** (`InsertOrUpdate`/`Delete` mutations; `key` must set-equal the table PK — mutations always address the primary key). Native primitives: postgres/sqlite `INSERT … ON CONFLICT … DO UPDATE`, mysql `ON DUPLICATE KEY UPDATE`, mssql `MERGE`, mongodb `replace_one(upsert)`/`delete_one`, elasticsearch `_bulk` `index`/`delete`, bigquery in-place `MERGE` / keyed semi-join `DELETE`. **Iceberg is append-only** for `write_mode` (overrides `supported_write_modes` to `[Append]` with a comment — equality-delete upsert is version-gated on `iceberg-rust`, #225). Note this is independent of exactly-once *delivery*: BigQuery supports both `delivery: exactly_once` (#215) and `write_mode: upsert` (#224), and they compose.\n342:`quarantine`/`fail` work), but `evolve` is blocked on `iceberg-rust` 0.10.0 (issue #255) and is","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1e4ef3f6-84d8-46e3-a894-10112a47971a","timestamp":"2026-09-18T10:53:24.616Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"docs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink.md:15:iceberg-rust 0.9.1 is pre-1.0 and its writer/catalog/transaction APIs churn; **docs.rs and the GitHub `main` branch may differ from 0.9.1**. For every iceberg call, resolve the exact signature against the real 0.9.1 crate: `cargo doc -p iceberg -p iceberg-catalog-rest --no-deps` then read, or inspect `~/.cargo/registry/src/*/iceberg-0.9.1*/src/`. Trust the compiler over this plan. When a signature differs, adapt while preserving behavior. If a needed capability is genuinely absent in 0.9.1, report BLOCKED with the specific type/method.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:15:The design spec listed **Iceberg** among the evolvable sinks. Planning revealed `iceberg-rust 0.9.1`\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:1955:- Add a code comment citing the iceberg-rust 0.9.1 blocker (parallel to the existing #179/#190 comments at\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:1963:git commit -m \"feat(sink-iceberg): current_schema (evolve blocked on iceberg-rust 0.9.1)\"\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:2082:/// intentionally excluded — iceberg-rust 0.9.1 exposes no schema-evolution API.\ndocs/superpowers/plans/2026-06-18-schema-drift-handling.md:2306:  iceberg-rust 0.9.1 blocker.\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-10-unified-write-mode-upsert-design.md:23:- **Iceberg upsert** — needs an equality-delete writer that `iceberg-rust 0.9.1` (the pinned version) does not expose. Version-gated; relates to #179 (Iceberg overwrite). Iceberg keeps `supported_write_modes() == [Append]`.\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink-design.md:14:- **Append-only v1.** iceberg-rust 0.9.1's `Transaction` exposes only\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-06-iceberg-sink-design.md:33:## Verified iceberg-rust 0.9.1 API (shape — implementer resolves exact signatures)\ndocs/superpowers/specs/2026-06-07-iceberg-cloud-warehouse-storage-design.md:49:## Background: how iceberg-rust 0.9.1 wires storage\n--- also fix the local rules file (gitignored, for future sessions)\n