{"parentUuid":"09284328-b266-4467-aa7d-126fb2d897a7","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"0b270ed8-79ad-458f-b783-66e7a379786e","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01HSKSqKFbbSiiKaLMxMg2xS","type":"tool_result","content":"726:impl<T> ParquetRecordBatchStream<T> {\n727-    /// Returns the projected [`SchemaRef`] for reading the parquet file.\n728-    ///\n729-    /// Note that the schema metadata will be stripped here. See\n730-    /// [`ParquetRecordBatchStreamBuilder::schema`] if the metadata is desired.\n731-    pub fn schema(&self) -> &SchemaRef {\n732-        &self.schema\n733-    }\n734-}\n735-\n736:impl<T> ParquetRecordBatchStream<T>\n737-where\n738-    T: AsyncFileReader + Unpin + Send + 'static,\n739-{\n740-    /// Fetches the next row group from the stream.\n741-    ///\n742-    /// Users can continue to call this function to get row groups and decode them concurrently.\n743-    ///\n744-    /// ## Notes\n745-    ///\n746-    /// ParquetRecordBatchStream should be used either as a `Stream` or with `next_row_group`; they should not be used simultaneously.\n747-    ///\n748-    /// ## Returns\n749-    ///\n750-    /// - `Ok(None)` if the stream has ended.\n=== s3 compression handling\n151:    /// so length/checksum verification (and any configured decompression)\n276:        // (below any decompression), then `BufReader` so `.lines()` is usable\n280:        #[cfg(feature = \"compression\")]\n282:            let codec = self.config.compression.resolve(key);\n283:            faucet_core::compression::warn_mismatch(key, codec);\n284:            Ok(faucet_core::compression::wrap_async_reader(buffered, codec))\n286:        #[cfg(not(feature = \"compression\"))]\n954:    #[cfg(feature = \"compression\")]\n956:    fn compression_default_is_auto() {\n958:        assert_eq!(cfg.compression, faucet_core::CompressionConfig::Auto);","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"7394553f-e1b2-4609-b854-0744ab731305","timestamp":"2026-09-18T11:01:20.455Z","too