{"parentUuid":"734b554b-9e4f-456c-9f04-9506eed467e8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfArMG62kMsySL3qkhWqY","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Rn2k5XTKgnKK7GCjtPAtfR","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(sources): make the ranged-read failure paths pure and covered\n\nThe range adapters' only non-trivial logic is arithmetic and diagnostics —\nan off-by-one in the HTTP range header reads the wrong bytes rather than\nfailing, and a short read handed to the Parquet decoder becomes a\nwrong-value bug rather than an error. Both were buried in the I/O call.\n\nExtracted as `range_header` / `failed` / `short` and unit-tested directly,\nleaving the request itself a thin shim. That matters most for gcs, whose\nemulator suite is `#[ignore]`d (`fake-gcs-server` speaks REST, the\nconnector uses the gRPC data plane), so these are the only automated\ncover that adapter gets.\n\nDropped the one test that drove a real request at a closed port: the\nclient's retry backoff made it take 282 seconds, which is not a unit test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit -c credential.helper= \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.helper=' \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.helper=!/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth git-credential' \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.username=PawanSikawat' \\\n    push 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"Commit and push the test refactor","timeout":600000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":646,"cache_read_input_tokens":447976,"output_tokens":636,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":646,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":636,"cache_read_input_tokens":447976,"cache_creation_input_tokens":646,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":646},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01Rn2k5XTKgnKK7GCjtPAtfR":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\ntest(sources): make the ranged-read failure paths pure and covered\n\nThe range adapters' only non-trivial logic is arithmetic and diagnostics —\nan off-by-one in the HTTP range header reads the wrong bytes rather than\nfailing, and a short read handed to the Parquet decoder becomes a\nwrong-value bug rather than an error. Both were buried in the I/O call.\n\nExtracted as `range_header` / `failed` / `short` and unit-tested directly,\nleaving the request itself a thin shim. That matters most for gcs, whose\nemulator suite is `#[ignore]`d (`fake-gcs-server` speaks REST, the\nconnector uses the gRPC data plane), so these are the only automated\ncover that adapter gets.\n\nDropped the one test that drove a real request at a closed port: the\nclient's retry backoff made it take 282 seconds, which is not a unit test.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\ngit -c credential.helper= \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.helper=' \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.helper=!/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth git-credential' \\\n    -c 'credential.https://github.com.username=PawanSikawat' \\\n    push 2>&1 | tail -2","timeout":600000,"description":"Commit and push the test refactor"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfArMFTKcXpp5k7oXvzry","type":"assistant","uuid":"