{"parentUuid":"82426b7f-14e2-4e15-974b-a2aecc47b186","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfArV843wNwheDnFiAspA","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01HETPysiH7pAEQGkLz41u8u","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\".claude/rules/connectors.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"- **Parallel I/O** — S3 source/sink uses `buffer_unordered()` for concurrent object reads/writes.\"\nnew = \"\"\"- **Parallel I/O** — S3 source/sink uses `buffer_unordered()` for concurrent object reads/writes. On the **streaming** path (`stream_pages`/`stream_batches`) s3/gcs/azure-blob/sftp use an **ordered** `buffered(concurrency)` prefetch instead (#619): listing order and per-object error attribution must not change, and `concurrency: 0` is clamped to 1 (a `buffered(0)` stream yields nothing forever). What the look-ahead holds differs by format — `json_lines` only open body readers and `parquet` only footer metadata (peak memory stays `O(batch_size)`), `json_array`/`raw_text` up to `concurrency` whole bodies.\n- **Parquet on s3/gcs streams row groups** (#619) via a crate-local `parquet_range` adapter implementing `AsyncFileReader` over ranged reads (`GetObject` + `Range` header / `read_object` + `ReadRange::segment`), with the Arrow batch size capped at `batch_size`. `object_store`'s `ParquetObjectReader` is deliberately not used: those crates authenticate through the vendor SDKs. **Two configs fall back to whole-object buffering** — `verify_checksum` (the checksum covers the whole object) and a resolved `compression` codec (not randomly addressable). `verify_length` needs no exception: a short range is an error.\"\"\"\nassert old in s\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nprint(\"rules updated\")\nPY","description":"Record the new invariants in the local rules file"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":409,"cache_read_input_tokens":449988,"output_tokens":1695,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":947},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":409,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1695,"cache_read_input_tokens":449988,"cache_creation_input_tokens":409,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":409},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01HETPysiH7pAEQGkLz41u8u":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\".claude/rules/connectors.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"- **Parallel I/O** — S3 source/sink uses `buffer_unordered()` for concurrent object reads/writes.\"\nnew = \"\"\"- **Parallel I/O** — S3 source/sink uses `buffer_unordered()` for concurrent object reads/writes. On the **streaming** path (`stream_pages`/`stream_batches`) s3/gcs/azure-blob/sftp use an **ordered** `buffered(concurrency)` prefetch instead (#619): listing order and per-object error attribution must not change, and `concurrency: 0` is clamped to 1 (a `buffered(0)` stream yields nothing forever). What the look-ahead holds differs by format — `json_lines` only open body readers and `parquet` only footer metadata (peak memory stays `O(batch_size)`), `json_array`/`raw_text` up to `concurrency` whole bodies.\n- **Parquet on s3/gcs streams row groups** (#619) via a crate-local `parquet_range` adapter implementing `AsyncFileReader` over ranged reads (`GetObject` + `Range` header / `read_object` + `ReadRange::segment`), with the Arrow batch size capped at `batch_size`. `object_store`'s `ParquetObjectReader` is deliberately not used: those crates authenticate through the vendor SDKs. **Two configs fall back to whole-object buffering** — `verify_checksum` (the checksum covers the whole object) and a resolved `compression` codec (not randomly addressable). `verify_length` needs no exception: a short range is an error.\"\"\"\nassert old in s\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1))\nprint(\"rules updated\")\nPY","description":"Record the new invariants in the local rules file"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfArV6xKhScHXnCzQTgnp","type":"assistant","uuid":"4c3d562b-9e6c-4b7d-a865-5a1dd1e88fdf","timestamp":"2026-09-18T11:50:03.603Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
