{"parentUuid":"4ef0ab8c-afd9-409f-befb-d015c7b00ede","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfArea6xeAAFnBUabA1tk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"","signature":""}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_read_input_tokens":456920,"output_tokens":1658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":147},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1658,"cache_read_input_tokens":456920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAreZMp9HUH6rjGyVteC","type":"assistant","uuid":"69394cc9-f90a-4346-8126-4cf3fd2ab49e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T11:51:54.980Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"69394cc9-f90a-4346-8126-4cf3fd2ab49e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfArea6xeAAFnBUabA1tk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Everything is implemented, verified locally, and pushed. Here's where the bug batch stands.\n\n## What landed in this batch\n\n**PR #664** — `#652` overwrite bookmark ordering, `#657` kafka `headers_path`, `#662` source error typing. It was **red** when I picked it back up: `Test` and `Coverage` both failed on `committed_schema_covers_current_build`. Cause was mine from the earlier session — the kafka doc rewrite changed a field's rustdoc, which is part of the committed `schemas/faucet.schema.json`, and the schema update had landed on the *other* branch. Spliced the one description back (verified against a real `--all-features faucet schema config`: zero drift) and pushed. Now green except `Test`/`Coverage` still running.\n\n**PR #665** (new) — the three you named that weren't fixed yet, all one shape: *a config knob that was declared, documented, and in two cases validated, then never acted on.*\n\n- **#609** — `faucet validate` / `template register` never deserialized a connector config into its own type. 37 dispatcher arms now do, plus each config's `validate()`. Turning it on caught real defects, all fixed: `RestStreamConfig` required 22 fields (per-field defaults, *not* a container default — that empties the schema's `required` and breaks `faucet init`), `query_params` accidentally required on rest and xml, and **16 shipped examples could not run**.\n- **#620** — delta's `target_file_size` was rejected when zero and otherwise never read, so a bulk source made one commit per run with a parquet buffer holding the whole dataset. Wired via `roll_if_over_target` on both write paths; tests assert it through Delta versions/file counts with `batch_size` below the row count, so the roll is exercised *inside* one `write_batch` — the property that actually bounds memory.\n- **#619** — both halves. `concurrency` was inert on the streaming path (`buffer_unordered` only ever existed in the eager batch path): s3/gcs/azure-blob/sftp now prefetch through an **ordered** `buffered(concurrency)` look-ahead — 60 objects read >2× faster at concurrency 15 against MinIO, listing order and per-object error attribution unchanged, `0` clamped to 1. And Parquet objects were buffered whole; each source now reads them **row group at a time** through an `AsyncFileReader` over ranged reads, batch size capped at `batch_size`.\n\nTwo things I deliberately did not paper over:\n\n- `verify_checksum` and `compression` keep the whole-object Parquet path — a whole-object checksum can't be verified from ranges, and a compressed member isn't randomly addressable. Each guarantee is worth more than the memory saving; `verify_length` needs no exception because a short range is an error.\n- **The sftp concurrency path has no end-to-end test** — neither sftp crate has a container harness. It's covered by config unit tests and the shared design, and the default is 4 (not 10) because every read shares one SSH channel. Noted in the PR; an `atmoz/sftp` suite would close it if you want it.\n\n`#623` was already fixed and is closed.\n\n## Two things worth your attention\n\n1. **Local disk hit 100%** mid-session (`target/` was 143 GB). I deleted the regenerable caches — `incremental/`, `semver-checks/`, and `llvm-cov-target/` (42 GB). The next coverage run will rebuild instrumented artifacts from scratch.\n2. **`gh` drifted back to `pawan-dt`** partway through and one API call was refused under it. No commit, push, or merge ran under that identity — the refused call was a PR-body edit, which I redid after re-switching. Every commit is authored `PawanSikawat <pawansikawat1998@gmail.com>`.\n\nStill unanswered from earlier, and I've stopped asking — just flagging once so they're not lost: the harness now instructs a `Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5` trailer, which contradicts your standing no-Claude-trailer rule for this repo (I've been following the harness); whether to rewrite published `main` history to strip `Co-authored-by: pawan-dt` from `6433e74b`/`fd32cf08`; and whether to file the typed-decimal improvement from the BSON discussion.\n\nBoth PRs have auto-merge armed with explicit `--subject`/`--body`, so nothing can pick up an injected trailer. CI is mid-run with **no failing checks** on either; I'm watching and will fix anything that goes red."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_read_input_tokens":456920,"output_tokens":1658,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":147},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1658,"cache_read_input_tokens":456920,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1813,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1813},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfAreZMp9HUH6rjGyVteC","type":"assistant","uuid":"0df359f6-a3dc-48fd-9b58-b0c3408f7d96","timestamp":"2026-09-18T11:52:15.272Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"0df359f6-a3dc-48fd-9b58-b0c3408f7d96","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_success","hookName":"Stop","toolUseID":"c53aa76b-b38e-4092-b8d5-b8433b3a08e0","hookEvent":"Stop","content":"","stdout":"{\"terminalSequence\":\"\\u001b]777;notify;warp://cli-agent;{\\\"v\\\":1,\\\"agent\\\":\\\"claude\\\",\\\"event\\\":\\\"stop\\\",\\\"session_id\\\":\\\"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f\\\",\\\"cwd\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\\\",\\\"project\\\":\\\"faucet-stream\\\",\\\"query\\\":\\\"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\\\\n\\\\nSummary:\\\\n## 1. Primary Request and Intent\\\\n\\\\nT...\\\",\\\"response\\\":\\\"Everything is implemented, verified locally, and pushed. Here's where the bug batch stands.\\\\n\\\\n## What landed in this batch\\\\n\\\\n**PR #664** — `#652` overwrite bookmark ordering, `#657` kafka `headers_pa...\\\",\\\"transcript_path\\\":\\\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f.jsonl\\\"}\\u0007\"}\n","stderr":"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/plugins/cache/claude-code-warp/warp/2.2.0/scripts/emit-terminal-sequence.sh: line 82: /dev/tty: Device not configured\n","exitCode":0,"command":"${CLAUDE_PLUGIN_ROOT}/scripts/on-stop.sh","durationMs":3824},"type":"attachment","uuid":"ab52529c-8143-444e-8c40-61f929cc7a67","timestamp":"2026-09-18T11:52:19.150Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
