{"parentUuid":"032ca67c-40b5-4559-b00b-5c33d056624c","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAtPEmSvG6e9TPPv5hrU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#664 is merged** — `#652` (overwrite bookmark ordering), `#657` (kafka headers), and `#662` (source error typing) are now on `main`.\n\nBecause that PR touched the same `schemas/faucet.schema.json` line my branch reverted, I test-merged the new `main` into #665 locally before letting auto-merge land it. It merges cleanly and the merged state is right — the kafka description keeps #664's \"applied\" wording while my sftp `concurrency` splice survives with the correct widened `[\"integer\",\"string\"]` type — and all five schema tests pass on it. So #665 won't regress `main`.\n\n#665 is still open with auto-merge armed. Its only red mark is the crates.io download timeout; the background watcher will re-run that job as soon as the current workflow finishes. Disk filled a third time mid-verification (the incremental cache regrows fast at this workspace size) — cleared again, and I ran the check with `CARGO_INCREMENTAL=0` to stop it rebuilding."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_read_input_tokens":553083,"output_tokens":502,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":169},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":327,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":502,"cache_read_input_tokens":553083,"cache_creation_input_tokens":327,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":327},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfAtPE4X8M1jvGE54DPbv","type":"assistant","uuid":"3caf