{"parentUuid":"69237de4-b3e2-4677-a06d-c14ea8dddad3","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAzK5ko42o4vh2yg8WWi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"`Coverage` was a real failure, not a flake — **88.20%** of changed lines (755/856) against the 95% floor. Every gap was genuine; all are now closed with tests that assert something real:\n\n- **`registry.rs` — 28 uncovered dispatcher arms.** The new tests are driven off `source_descriptions()`/`sink_descriptions()` rather than a hand-written list, so a connector added *without* a validation arm now fails the test instead of silently accepting any config until its first triggered run — exactly the defect #609 was filed for.\n- **`sftp/stream.rs` — the entire streaming path.** I wrote the `atmoz/sftp` integration suite after all; six tests now run against a real SSH server and **confirm the concurrent-read path works** (no drops, no duplicates, listing order held, per-file error attribution intact under prefetch, `concurrency: 0` clamped). That also closes the test gap I'd flagged in the PR description as unverified — so that caveat is gone.\n- **`rest/config.rs`** — the nine new `default_*` fns; serde only calls them when a field is absent and no test deserialized the minimum. The new test is the regression test for the 22-required-fields defect, and it pins that the defaulted auth is the inert one.\n- **`templates/store.rs`** — a structurally invalid *sink* config at register time (the source half was already covered).\n- **`s3/config.rs`** — the fields that gained defaults.\n\nTwo judgement calls, both stated in the commit and PR rather than hidden:\n\n1. **`gcs/src/parquet_range.rs` added to the three coverage ignore lists** (ci.yml, codecov.yml, patch-coverage.py — the comment says keep them in sync). This is the established exception its sibling `gcs/src/stream.rs` already has and for the identical reason: the GCS SDK speaks a gRPC data plane no emulator implements, so that suite is `#[ignore]`d (#220). Every non-helper line in the file issues a `read_object`; the arithmetic and failure messages are unit-tested in the file itself.\n2. **Two lines stay uncovered deliberately** — the `writer: None` guards in delta's `commit_buffered`/`roll_if_over_target`. Both write paths return early on an empty batch, so neither is reachable through the public API.\n\nPushed; fmt, workspace clippy (`--all-targets --all-features -D warnings`), and all affected tests pass locally (1,673 CLI lib tests green). CI is recomputing the patch number now."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_read_input_tokens":606491,"output_tokens":842,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1569,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":842,"cache_read_input_tokens":606491,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1569,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1569},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfAzK3zNnVENCuK64ULzA","type":"assistant","uuid":"37a4ddc6-1341-4096-987b-759a033eb95e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:32:30.894Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
