{"parentUuid":"87b5ae98-8cdb-4f5f-ac5c-7a65dc83ac94","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAzYn1LUu44hC1rXviYU","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_0113GmRwLZbnMJBE5P8V4Nkd","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > \"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run.md\" <<'MD'\n---\nname: reference-never-rerun-superseded-ci-run\ndescription: \"Re-running an older CI run after a new push cancels the new run — CI's concurrency group has cancel-in-progress\"\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nOn faucet-hq/faucet-stream the CI workflow uses a per-branch concurrency\ngroup with `cancel-in-progress`. A `gh run rerun <old-run> --failed`\ncounts as a **new** run for that group, so it **cancels the run for the\ncommit you just pushed** — every check shows `COMPLETED / CANCELLED` on\nthe new head and nothing is actually testing your code.\n\nHit 2026-09-18 on PR #665: a background watcher re-ran a transient\ncrates.io-timeout job from the previous commit's run moments after a new\npush; the fresh run was cancelled and the PR sat with an empty rollup.\n\n**How to apply:** only re-run a run whose SHA is still the PR head. After\nany push, drop queued reruns for older SHAs. To recover: `gh run cancel\n<stale-run>` to free the concurrency slot, then `gh run rerun <cancelled\nrun for the current head>` (or push again). A transient failure in a\n**non-required** job is not worth a rerun at all if another push is\ncoming — see [[feedback_enable_auto_merge_default]].\nMD\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/MEMORY.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nline = \"- [Never re-run a superseded CI run](reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run.md) — `gh run rerun` on an older SHA cancels the run for the commit you just pushed (concurrency group has cancel-in-progress); cancel the stale run to recover.\\n\"\nif \"reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run\" not in s:\n    p.write_text(s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + line)\nprint(\"index updated\")\nPY","description":"Save the CI concurrency lesson to memory"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_read_input_tokens":613208,"output_tokens":1127,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":234},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1127,"cache_read_input_tokens":613208,"cache_creation_input_tokens":450,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":450},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_0113GmRwLZbnMJBE5P8V4Nkd":{"command":"cat > \"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run.md\" <<'MD'\n---\nname: reference-never-rerun-superseded-ci-run\ndescription: \"Re-running an older CI run after a new push cancels the new run — CI's concurrency group has cancel-in-progress\"\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\nOn faucet-hq/faucet-stream the CI workflow uses a per-branch concurrency\ngroup with `cancel-in-progress`. A `gh run rerun <old-run> --failed`\ncounts as a **new** run for that group, so it **cancels the run for the\ncommit you just pushed** — every check shows `COMPLETED / CANCELLED` on\nthe new head and nothing is actually testing your code.\n\nHit 2026-09-18 on PR #665: a background watcher re-ran a transient\ncrates.io-timeout job from the previous commit's run moments after a new\npush; the fresh run was cancelled and the PR sat with an empty rollup.\n\n**How to apply:** only re-run a run whose SHA is still the PR head. After\nany push, drop queued reruns for older SHAs. To recover: `gh run cancel\n<stale-run>` to free the concurrency slot, then `gh run rerun <cancelled\nrun for the current head>` (or push again). A transient failure in a\n**non-required** job is not worth a rerun at all if another push is\ncoming — see [[feedback_enable_auto_merge_default]].\nMD\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/MEMORY.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nline = \"- [Never re-run a superseded CI run](reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run.md) — `gh run rerun` on an older SHA cancels the run for the commit you just pushed (concurrency group has cancel-in-progress); cancel the stale run to recover.\\n\"\nif \"reference_never_rerun_superseded_ci_run\" not in s:\n    p.write_text(s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + line)\nprint(\"index updated\")\nPY","description":"Save the CI concurrency lesson to memory"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfAzYk9UQVoGG1nD9wWza","type":"assistant","uuid":"e9487d3b-4753-479a-9317-8eef132b986e","timestamp":"2026-09-18T13:35:40.563Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
