{"parentUuid":"09d19859-8249-40b4-8ab5-073a1ff8ce9f","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfAza9tFu2dxWrDJ6h11R","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"That empty check list was my own doing, not CI: the re-run I'd queued for the *previous* commit's transient failure fired right after my push, and CI's per-branch concurrency group has `cancel-in-progress` — so the re-run of the stale run cancelled the run for the commit that actually mattered. Every check on `a6296b8a` read `CANCELLED` because nothing was testing it.\n\nRecovered by cancelling the stale run to free the concurrency slot; CI is now queued against the correct head. I've saved the lesson to memory so I don't arm that kind of watcher again — a transient failure in a non-required job isn't worth a re-run when another push is coming.\n\nWhere #665 stands: the coverage work is pushed (registry table tests, the `atmoz/sftp` suite, rest/s3 config defaults, the store sink-validation test, plus the documented GCS adapter exclusion), everything passes locally, and CI is re-running to recompute the patch number. The persistent watch is still armed, so I'll report when it merges or if something real goes red."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cache_read_input_tokens":613658,"output_tokens":343,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1159,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":343,"cache_read_input_tokens":613658,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1159,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1159},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,