{"parentUuid":"a82b5b1e-2a0d-453d-b21d-2aa425e8a930","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14983475 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b784a14-c869-4f35-95e9-491730472b1e","timestamp":"2026-09-19T09:10:16.694Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14983475 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"9b784a14-c869-4f35-95e9-491730472b1e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCY8yVxWFVBUmQ1cpFML","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01FWXkzQ5H9gFEMpMfoqruzs","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ncat > /tmp/issue_flake.md <<'BODY'\n## Summary\n\n`template_register` against a **SQLite** run-history backend can fail with\n`database is locked` (SQLITE_BUSY) under concurrent callers. The backend\nalready classifies the error as `Transient`, but the register path does not\nretry that class — it retries only PK conflicts — so the error reaches the\ncaller. On `faucet serve` with `--history sqlite:…` that is a spurious 500 on\na concurrent template register; in CI it makes the **required** `Coverage` and\n`Test` jobs flaky.\n\nObserved on an unrelated PR's CI run (PR #665, run 35350804257, attempt 1 —\nthe same test passed on a later attempt, which is what makes it a flake rather\nthan a break):\n\n```\nthread 'templates::concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write'\npanicked at cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs:911:86:\ncalled `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` value: BackendClassified {\n    message: \"error returned from database: (code: 5) database is locked\",\n    transience: Transient,\n}\n```\n\n## Why this matters\n\n[Primary Goal — reliability.] Two separate costs:\n\n1. **Product.** A concurrent register is a normal thing for a deploy pipeline\n   to do (several templates registered in parallel by CI). Today one of them\n   can fail with a lock error that the layer below already knows is retryable.\n2. **CI signal.** A flaky *required* check trains everyone to re-run rather\n   than read a red gate — the failure mode a reliability release should not\n   ship with.\n\n## Where it is\n\n- `cli/src/serve/history/sql.rs` — `impl_sql_history!`, the `template_register`\n  / `template_launch` read-max-then-insert transactions. They carry a bounded\n  **PK-conflict** retry (added so a concurrent write is never lost); a\n  `Transient` backend error takes a different path and is returned.\n- `cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs::concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write`\n  — spawns 6 concurrent registers and `unwrap()`s each.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nPrefer fixing the backend over relaxing the test — the test is asserting the\nright thing.\n\n1. **Set a busy timeout on the SQLite pool** so a writer waits for the lock\n   instead of failing immediately: `SqliteConnectOptions::busy_timeout(…)` (a\n   few seconds), plus `journal_mode(WAL)` if it is not already set — WAL lets\n   readers proceed during a write and is the standard fix for this class.\n2. **Retry `Transient` alongside the PK conflict** in the same bounded loop,\n   so the guarantee is \"a concurrent write is never lost\" rather than \"a\n   concurrent write is never lost unless SQLite was busy\".\n3. Keep the test unwrapping — with (1) and (2) it should pass deterministically.\n   If a residual race remains, assert on the *outcome* (six distinct versions)\n   rather than adding a retry to the test, which would hide the defect.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write` passes 50 consecutive\n  runs locally (`--test-threads` unchanged).\n- A `Transient` backend error during `template_register` / `template_launch` is\n  retried within the existing bound, and the existing \"no lost writes\"\n  assertions still hold.\n- The Postgres backend is unaffected (it does not take this path).\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The wider question of whether every `RunHistory` write should retry\n  `Transient` (this issue is scoped to the two template paths that already have\n  a retry loop to extend).\n\n## References\n\nSurfaced while landing #665. Test introduced in #650. Roadmap epic #38.\nBODY\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream \\\n  --title \"bug(serve): concurrent template_register on a SQLite history fails with \\`database is locked\\` (flakes a required CI check)\" \\\n  --label bug --label tier-2 --body-file /tmp/issue_flake.md 2>&1 | tail -2","description":"File the SQLite lock flake as an issue","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_read_input_tokens":635022,"output_tokens":1602,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1602,"cache_read_input_tokens":635022,"cache_creation_input_tokens":282,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":282},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01FWXkzQ5H9gFEMpMfoqruzs":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\ncat > /tmp/issue_flake.md <<'BODY'\n## Summary\n\n`template_register` against a **SQLite** run-history backend can fail with\n`database is locked` (SQLITE_BUSY) under concurrent callers. The backend\nalready classifies the error as `Transient`, but the register path does not\nretry that class — it retries only PK conflicts — so the error reaches the\ncaller. On `faucet serve` with `--history sqlite:…` that is a spurious 500 on\na concurrent template register; in CI it makes the **required** `Coverage` and\n`Test` jobs flaky.\n\nObserved on an unrelated PR's CI run (PR #665, run 35350804257, attempt 1 —\nthe same test passed on a later attempt, which is what makes it a flake rather\nthan a break):\n\n```\nthread 'templates::concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write'\npanicked at cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs:911:86:\ncalled `Result::unwrap()` on an `Err` value: BackendClassified {\n    message: \"error returned from database: (code: 5) database is locked\",\n    transience: Transient,\n}\n```\n\n## Why this matters\n\n[Primary Goal — reliability.] Two separate costs:\n\n1. **Product.** A concurrent register is a normal thing for a deploy pipeline\n   to do (several templates registered in parallel by CI). Today one of them\n   can fail with a lock error that the layer below already knows is retryable.\n2. **CI signal.** A flaky *required* check trains everyone to re-run rather\n   than read a red gate — the failure mode a reliability release should not\n   ship with.\n\n## Where it is\n\n- `cli/src/serve/history/sql.rs` — `impl_sql_history!`, the `template_register`\n  / `template_launch` read-max-then-insert transactions. They carry a bounded\n  **PK-conflict** retry (added so a concurrent write is never lost); a\n  `Transient` backend error takes a different path and is returned.\n- `cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs::concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write`\n  — spawns 6 concurrent registers and `unwrap()`s each.\n\n## Proposed design\n\nPrefer fixing the backend over relaxing the test — the test is asserting the\nright thing.\n\n1. **Set a busy timeout on the SQLite pool** so a writer waits for the lock\n   instead of failing immediately: `SqliteConnectOptions::busy_timeout(…)` (a\n   few seconds), plus `journal_mode(WAL)` if it is not already set — WAL lets\n   readers proceed during a write and is the standard fix for this class.\n2. **Retry `Transient` alongside the PK conflict** in the same bounded loop,\n   so the guarantee is \"a concurrent write is never lost\" rather than \"a\n   concurrent write is never lost unless SQLite was busy\".\n3. Keep the test unwrapping — with (1) and (2) it should pass deterministically.\n   If a residual race remains, assert on the *outcome* (six distinct versions)\n   rather than adding a retry to the test, which would hide the defect.\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- `concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write` passes 50 consecutive\n  runs locally (`--test-threads` unchanged).\n- A `Transient` backend error during `template_register` / `template_launch` is\n  retried within the existing bound, and the existing \"no lost writes\"\n  assertions still hold.\n- The Postgres backend is unaffected (it does not take this path).\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## Out of scope\n\n- The wider question of whether every `RunHistory` write should retry\n  `Transient` (this issue is scoped to the two template paths that already have\n  a retry loop to extend).\n\n## References\n\nSurfaced while landing #665. Test introduced in #650. Roadmap epic #38.\nBODY\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && \\\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue create --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream \\\n  --title \"bug(serve): concurrent template_register on a SQLite history fails with \\`database is locked\\` (flakes a required CI check)\" \\\n  --label bug --label tier-2 --body-file /tmp/issue_flake.md 2>&1 | tail -2","timeout":300000,"description":"File the SQLite lock flake as an issue"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCY8xerVofDVwqVpj5YC","type":"assistant","uuid":"7eda6799-e70c-45d8-8fc4-95c318a355c2","timestamp":"2026-09-19T09:10:40.969Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
