{"parentUuid":"87d7f3f5-0ec3-4eae-b76f-f17d36a0dad0","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14981448 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"9b14a7d4-9ed8-4cf0-8d01-697b1e1a49e1","timestamp":"2026-09-19T09:10:56.099Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14981448 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"9b14a7d4-9ed8-4cf0-8d01-697b1e1a49e1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCYBtFH8g1hp2a7k3qoz","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Both failures diagnosed and handled — and only one of them was mine.\n\n**Mine: the overlap test, not the code.** CI measured concurrency=15 at 71 ms against serial at 112 ms — a real 1.6× overlap — but I'd asserted ≥2×, which that runner can't reach because the per-request latency this fix hides is small next to its fixed decode cost. A wall-clock ratio was simply the wrong instrument: *how much* faster overlap makes a run is a property of the machine, while *that* the reads overlap is a property of the source.\n\nSo the test now measures the property directly. HTTP/1.1 can't multiplex, so N requests in flight need N sockets — the source is routed through a small counting TCP proxy and the test asserts the high-water mark of simultaneously open connections. Measured locally: **concurrency 15 peaks at 16 connections, concurrency 1 peaks at exactly 1.** The serial arm is the control, so a miscounting proxy or a stray SDK socket can't make the first assertion pass on a serial reader. No timing, nothing to tune, nothing to flake. (`net`/`io-util` went onto the s3 crate's *dev* tokio only — the shipped dependency is untouched.)\n\n**Not mine: `templates::concurrent_registers_and_launches_never_lose_a_write`.** Six concurrent `template_register` calls against one SQLite file, unwrapping an error the backend itself labels `Transient` — `database is locked`. It's from #650, in a file my PR doesn't touch, and it passed on a later attempt while mine failed consistently. Rather than absorb it silently or wave it off, I filed **#666** (bug/tier-2) with the CI evidence and a concrete fix — set a busy timeout + WAL on the SQLite pool and extend the existing bounded retry to cover `Transient`, keeping the test's assertion intact so the defect can't hide — and cross-linked it to epic #38. It matters twice over for a reliability release: a spurious 500 on a concurrent register, and a flaky *required* check that trains people to re-run instead of read a red gate.\n\nFix pushed; CI is recomputing. The quiet watch stays armed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_read_input_tokens":636959,"output_tokens":729,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":729,"cache_read_input_tokens":636959,"cache_creation_input_tokens":397,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":397},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCYBsQvgNp6LGqcKSsFy","type":"assistant","uuid":"55c5a0ab-921e-4adc-a302-0d3274e264c8","timestamp":"2026-09-19T09:11:07.371Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
