{"parentUuid":"3631d4c9-9371-4e3e-9e25-d14528736a74","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01Xh8xKcZzfhjw8Lw4SMAytg","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":10958},"type":"attachment","uuid":"1506fd33-4c03-416e-bd8d-7f93dbf9b75d","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:30:46.767Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"3631d4c9-9371-4e3e-9e25-d14528736a74","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Xh8xKcZzfhjw8Lw4SMAytg","type":"tool_result","content":"═══ #612 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A 60k-row load completes in seconds, not minutes.\n- Multi-million-row loads scale by data size, not page count.\n- Overwrite atomicity (staging→swap) and exactly-once/upsert semantics preserved.\n\n## Out of scope\n═══ #614 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A large overwrite (rows ≫ `batch_size`) completes as **one** BigQuery load job with peak RSS ≈ O(batch_size), not O(table) — demonstrably below the current ~346 MB for the 59k-row table when paged small.\n- Single-page behavior unchanged in result (one atomic WRITE_TRUNCATE load).\n- Append streams via WRITE_APPEND into one load job per run.\n- Atomicity preserved (mid-stream failure commits nothing / leaves prior data intact for overwrite).\n- Tests: streaming chunk assembly, session finalize/cancel, memory-bounded multi-page load, gzip/parquet round-trip.\n\n## Out of scope\n═══ #621 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Snowflake partition fetch and BigQuery Storage-Read streams run concurrently (bounded), measurably faster on multi-partition/multi-stream results.\n- BigQuery Storage Read API usable for arbitrary SQL (via a destination table).\n- No change to correctness or memory bounds; tests assert result parity.\n\n## References\n═══ #624 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Large CSV file mode yields multiple bounded `StreamPage`s; Excel no longer materializes the sheet twice.\n- `partition_concurrency > 1` demonstrably parallelizes partition reads under `stream_pages`; test asserts overlap.\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## References\n═══ #632 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `keys_case` with the disambiguation option renames colliding keys uniquely + deterministically; `Account`/`Contact` full-column sync succeeds (21/21).\n- Default stays fail-loud (back-compat).\n- ≥95% patch coverage (incl. a collision fixture).\n\n## References\n═══ #637 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Cancel/Discard/Deprecate/Purge render amber; Delete* render red; navigation/tabs stay grey — verified light + dark via rendered screenshots.\n- No behavior change, only affordance.\n\n## References\n═══ #646 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Dataset list columns align across all rows; URIs truncate at a consistent x; role/kind/search (and from/to if server-side) filter the list.\n- Preview shows \"N of M\", the toggle doesn't resize, and the table is aligned + horizontally contained.\n- Lineage nodes are visibly lighter and still readable; crossings remain minimal.\n- No behaviour change when preview is disabled or the catalog is empty.\n\n## Out of scope","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"c4194508-81a0-40ed-95d3-e89597450b39","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:30:53.403Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"═══ #612 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- A 60k-row load completes in seconds, not minutes.\n- Multi-million-row loads scale by data size, not page count.\n- Overwrite atomicity (staging→swap) and exactly-once/upsert semantics preserved.\n\n## Out of scope\n═══ #614 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n\n- A large overwrite (rows ≫ `batch_size`) completes as **one** BigQuery load job with peak RSS ≈ O(batch_size), not O(table) — demonstrably below the current ~346 MB for the 59k-row table when paged small.\n- Single-page behavior unchanged in result (one atomic WRITE_TRUNCATE load).\n- Append streams via WRITE_APPEND into one load job per run.\n- Atomicity preserved (mid-stream failure commits nothing / leaves prior data intact for overwrite).\n- Tests: streaming chunk assembly, session finalize/cancel, memory-bounded multi-page load, gzip/parquet round-trip.\n\n## Out of scope\n═══ #621 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Snowflake partition fetch and BigQuery Storage-Read streams run concurrently (bounded), measurably faster on multi-partition/multi-stream results.\n- BigQuery Storage Read API usable for arbitrary SQL (via a destination table).\n- No change to correctness or memory bounds; tests assert result parity.\n\n## References\n═══ #624 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Large CSV file mode yields multiple bounded `StreamPage`s; Excel no longer materializes the sheet twice.\n- `partition_concurrency > 1` demonstrably parallelizes partition reads under `stream_pages`; test asserts overlap.\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## References\n═══ #632 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- `keys_case` with the disambiguation option renames colliding keys uniquely + deterministically; `Account`/`Contact` full-column sync succeeds (21/21).\n- Default stays fail-loud (back-compat).\n- ≥95% patch coverage (incl. a collision fixture).\n\n## References\n═══ #637 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Cancel/Discard/Deprecate/Purge render amber; Delete* render red; navigation/tabs stay grey — verified light + dark via rendered screenshots.\n- No behavior change, only affordance.\n\n## References\n═══ #646 acceptance criteria\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Dataset list columns align across all rows; URIs truncate at a consistent x; role/kind/search (and from/to if server-side) filter the list.\n- Preview shows \"N of M\", the toggle doesn't resize, and the table is aligned + horizontally contained.\n- Lineage nodes are visibly lighter and still readable; crossings remain minimal.\n- No behaviour change when preview is disabled or the catalog is empty.\n\n## Out of scope","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"3631d4c9-9371-4e3e-9e25-d14528736a74","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
