{"parentUuid":"01fadf6a-a2a9-48ed-9868-78a5ee649cc1","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCek6L99KPYHTnhsDaDk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01RGw35nJRSJj8bi5wCPcs2p","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 614 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason completed --comment \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nVerified against the code — implemented, closing.\n\nThe resumable-session streaming load landed in `crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs`:\n\n- A BigQuery **resumable upload session** is held as sink state across pages; each page is serialized → gzipped → PUT as a 8 MiB-aligned chunk (`resumable_chunk` is the test hook), and the rows are dropped after the chunk is sent. Peak memory is O(chunk + page), not O(table).\n- **Overwrite**: the whole refresh is one `WRITE_TRUNCATE` session fed across every page and finalized in `flush()` — so a mid-run failure leaves the prior data intact and a table far larger than `batch_size` is still a single atomic load.\n- **Append**: `feed_session(table, \"WRITE_APPEND\", records)` — one load job per run, finalized the same way. (This is the criterion I checked most carefully, since the `media_load` doc comment still claims append is unaffected; the code contradicts it. I'm fixing that stale comment separately.)\n- Tests: `load_native_streaming_payload_feeds_session_chunk_by_chunk` (chunk assembly), `load_native_overwrite_first_batch_truncates_once_per_object` (truncate-once semantics), `load_native_ndjson_streams_session_with_explicit_string_schema`, `load_native_empty_payload_is_a_noop`, plus the `native_capabilities_*` guards.\n\n**Note for #612, which stays open:** this is the *streaming* half. The load path itself is still opt-in — `media_load` defaults to `false` — so a default-config user keeps the per-page `jobs.query` behaviour #612 reported. Detail on that issue.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 615 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason \"not planned\" --comment \"Duplicate of #626 (and of #625, filed the next day with a byte-identical title). Same defect, same evidence — 3.96 GB peak for one 838k-row Salesforce Bulk CSV result. Consolidating on **#626**, which carries the \\`tier-1\\` label; closing this one so the work is tracked in a single place.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 625 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason \"not planned\" --comment \"Duplicate of #626 (and of #615, filed a day earlier with a byte-identical title). Same defect, same evidence — 3.96 GB peak for one 838k-row Salesforce Bulk CSV result. Consolidating on **#626** (\\`tier-1\\`); closing this one so the work is tracked in a single place.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho done","description":"Close 614 as done and 615/625 as duplicates"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2154,"cache_read_input_tokens":682612,"output_tokens":1145,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2154,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1145,"cache_read_input_tokens":682612,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2154,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2154},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01RGw35nJRSJj8bi5wCPcs2p":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 614 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason completed --comment \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nVerified against the code — implemented, closing.\n\nThe resumable-session streaming load landed in `crates/sink/bigquery/src/sink.rs`:\n\n- A BigQuery **resumable upload session** is held as sink state across pages; each page is serialized → gzipped → PUT as a 8 MiB-aligned chunk (`resumable_chunk` is the test hook), and the rows are dropped after the chunk is sent. Peak memory is O(chunk + page), not O(table).\n- **Overwrite**: the whole refresh is one `WRITE_TRUNCATE` session fed across every page and finalized in `flush()` — so a mid-run failure leaves the prior data intact and a table far larger than `batch_size` is still a single atomic load.\n- **Append**: `feed_session(table, \"WRITE_APPEND\", records)` — one load job per run, finalized the same way. (This is the criterion I checked most carefully, since the `media_load` doc comment still claims append is unaffected; the code contradicts it. I'm fixing that stale comment separately.)\n- Tests: `load_native_streaming_payload_feeds_session_chunk_by_chunk` (chunk assembly), `load_native_overwrite_first_batch_truncates_once_per_object` (truncate-once semantics), `load_native_ndjson_streams_session_with_explicit_string_schema`, `load_native_empty_payload_is_a_noop`, plus the `native_capabilities_*` guards.\n\n**Note for #612, which stays open:** this is the *streaming* half. The load path itself is still opt-in — `media_load` defaults to `false` — so a default-config user keeps the per-page `jobs.query` behaviour #612 reported. Detail on that issue.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 615 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason \"not planned\" --comment \"Duplicate of #626 (and of #625, filed the next day with a byte-identical title). Same defect, same evidence — 3.96 GB peak for one 838k-row Salesforce Bulk CSV result. Consolidating on **#626**, which carries the \\`tier-1\\` label; closing this one so the work is tracked in a single place.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 625 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason \"not planned\" --comment \"Duplicate of #626 (and of #615, filed a day earlier with a byte-identical title). Same defect, same evidence — 3.96 GB peak for one 838k-row Salesforce Bulk CSV result. Consolidating on **#626** (\\`tier-1\\`); closing this one so the work is tracked in a single place.\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho done","description":"Close 614 as done and 615/625 as duplicates"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCek5NbjuXjuGD9kVHiv","type":"assistant","uuid":"4081637a-6e82-4213-8f8a-ec40d1842c40","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:37:09.749Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/inert-config-knobs","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
