{"parentUuid":"2aa35096-69d6-4193-9cd9-9924484da40d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCengEu47grvyzJhXYbK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01BSAPyZ8bQm8BGNEk2SYrHu","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue comment 612 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n**Audit: the capability landed, but the reported symptom still reproduces on a default config — keeping this open.**\n\nWhat exists now (`crates/sink/bigquery/src/{load,sink}.rs`):\n- A bucket-free **media load job** (`multipart/related` NDJSON, and `sourceFormat = PARQUET` via `build_load_job`), fed through a **resumable session** so a run is one load job rather than one `jobs.query` per page. The streaming half of that is #614, now closed.\n\nWhy this issue is not done:\n1. **It is opt-in.** `media_load` defaults to `false` (`crates/sink/bigquery/src/config.rs`). The exact scenario in the report — a `postgres → BigQuery` overwrite at the default `batch_size: 1000` — still takes the per-page `jobs.query` path and is still job-latency-bound. The acceptance criterion is outcome-shaped (\"a 60k-row load completes in seconds, not minutes\"), and out of the box it does not.\n2. **Append/upsert are only partly covered.** Append *does* use the session when `media_load` is on (`feed_session(.., \"WRITE_APPEND\", ..)`), but upsert/delete/exactly-once still run per-page query jobs.\n3. **The doc comment is stale and actively misleading.** `media_load`'s rustdoc says *\"Only consulted on the `write_mode: overwrite` path; append / upsert / delete / exactly-once are unaffected\"* — the append path reads it. That lands on docs.rs.\n\nRemaining work: decide whether `media_load` becomes the default (the issue's \"Primary — bulk load path\"), which is a real behaviour change — load jobs have different quota and latency characteristics from `insertAll` — and fix the stale rustdoc either way.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\n\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue comment 624 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --body \"$(cat <<'EOF'\n**Audit: one of the three parts is done; the other two are not — keeping this open.**\n\n- ✅ **`partition_concurrency` on the streaming path.** `crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:550` reads `self.config.partition_concurrency` inside the streaming path, so it is no longer ignored there.\n- ❌ **CSV file mode still buffers the whole file.** `format::parse_csv` returns `Vec<Value>` (`crates/source/rest/src/format.rs:15`). A streaming variant exists — `csv_reader_to_ndjson_stream` returns a real `Stream` — but it serves the byte-passthrough fast path (#633); the `Value` decode path still collects. This is the same defect as #626.\n- ❌ **Excel still double-materializes.** `parse_excel` also returns `Vec<Value>`.\n\nSo the remaining scope here overlaps #626 (the CSV half). Worth deciding whether to fold the CSV part into #626 and keep this issue for the Excel half only.\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1\necho done","description":"Post audit findings on 612 and 624"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_read_input_tokens":684766,"output_tokens":1423,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":195},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1423,"cache_read_input_tokens":684766,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1417,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1417},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01BSAPyZ8