{"parentUuid":"b479e866-69e3-4e5f-b31c-c2ada5364dcc","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCfxcyLiVDhGAaEZFfKF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All 23 pass. Committing #666 with the evidence:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":714251,"output_tokens":1047,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":714251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCfxc5FwU8Z7PtKWr2bS","type":"assistant","uuid":"0d6bea7a-b318-4ef0-ab8b-bed2cb4f2889","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:52:52.429Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-580-onwards","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"0d6bea7a-b318-4ef0-ab8b-bed2cb4f2889","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCfxcyLiVDhGAaEZFfKF","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01PGcXDtZRaHaMnix6HX2LRW","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add cli/src/serve/history/sql.rs cli/src/serve/history/sqlite.rs cli/src/serve/history/postgres.rs cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(serve): open SQLite write transactions IMMEDIATE so contention waits\n\n`template_register` could fail with `database is locked` under concurrent\ncallers — a spurious error to the caller, and a flake in the required CI\nchecks. My own filed diagnosis (#666) was wrong twice, and the error\ncodes are what corrected it:\n\n- WAL and a 5s `busy_timeout` were **already** set, so \"add a busy\n  timeout\" was a no-op suggestion;\n- the un-retried `tx.commit()` looked like the culprit, but retrying it\n  changed nothing — 8/8 runs still failed at 64 writers.\n\nThe codes said why: **517 = `SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT`**. sqlx's `begin()`\nissues a *deferred* `BEGIN`, so the read-max-then-insert transaction\nstarts as a reader and must upgrade to a writer. In WAL mode SQLite\nrefuses that upgrade **immediately** when another writer committed in\nbetween — it does not consult `busy_timeout`, because waiting could\ndeadlock. No timeout and no retry budget can fix a conflict the engine\ndeclines to wait on.\n\n`BEGIN IMMEDIATE` takes the write lock up front, so contention becomes a\nwait the busy timeout absorbs. The statement is dialect-specific, so\n`impl_sql_history!` now takes it as a parameter: SQLite passes\n`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, Postgres passes `BEGIN` (it has no such distinction,\nso its behaviour is unchanged).\n\nMeasured, 64 concurrent registers: **5/5 runs failed before, 0/10 after.**\nThe new test asserts the guarantee (64 distinct versions, none lost)\nrather than just absence of an error, and 64 writers is deliberately past\nthe point where the old code failed every time — the six-writer test it\nsits beside only flaked occasionally, which is why this went unnoticed.\n\nThe commit inside the retry loop is now retried too. That is not what\nfixed this, but every sibling step in that loop already retried and the\ncommit returning early would abort a register the next attempt would\nhave completed.\n\nCloses #666\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the SQLite transaction fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_read_input_tokens":714251,"output_tokens":1047,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1047,"cache_read_input_tokens":714251,"cache_creation_input_tokens":910,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":910},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01PGcXDtZRaHaMnix6HX2LRW":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add cli/src/serve/history/sql.rs cli/src/serve/history/sqlite.rs cli/src/serve/history/postgres.rs cli/tests/serve_history_sqlite.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(serve): open SQLite write transactions IMMEDIATE so contention waits\n\n`template_register` could fail with `database is locked` under concurrent\ncallers — a spurious error to the caller, and a flake in the required CI\nchecks. My own filed diagnosis (#666) was wrong twice, and the error\ncodes are what corrected it:\n\n- WAL and a 5s `busy_timeout` were **already** set, so \"add a busy\n  timeout\" was a no-op suggestion;\n- the un-retried `tx.commit()` looked like the culprit, but retrying it\n  changed nothing — 8/8 runs still failed at 64 writers.\n\nThe codes said why: **517 = `SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT`**. sqlx's `begin()`\nissues a *deferred* `BEGIN`, so the read-max-then-insert transaction\nstarts as a reader and must upgrade to a writer. In WAL mode SQLite\nrefuses that upgrade **immediately** when another writer committed in\nbetween — it does not consult `busy_timeout`, because waiting could\ndeadlock. No timeout and no retry budget can fix a conflict the engine\ndeclines to wait on.\n\n`BEGIN IMMEDIATE` takes the write lock up front, so contention becomes a\nwait the busy timeout absorbs. The statement is dialect-specific, so\n`impl_sql_history!` now takes it as a parameter: SQLite passes\n`BEGIN IMMEDIATE`, Postgres passes `BEGIN` (it has no such distinction,\nso its behaviour is unchanged).\n\nMeasured, 64 concurrent registers: **5/5 runs failed before, 0/10 after.**\nThe new test asserts the guarantee (64 distinct versions, none lost)\nrather than just absence of an error, and 64 writers is deliberately past\nthe point where the old code failed every time — the six-writer test it\nsits beside only flaked occasionally, which is why this went unnoticed.\n\nThe commit inside the retry loop is now retried too. That is not what\nfixed this, but every sibling step in that loop already retried and the\ncommit returning early would abort a register the next attempt would\nhave completed.\n\nCloses #666\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline -1","description":"Commit the SQLite transaction fix"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfCfxc5FwU8Z7PtKWr2bS","type":"assistant","uuid":"069fa05a-e1cd-40b0-93f2-369b18b2633f","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:53:05.291Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-580-onwards","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
