-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"5b425e89-e7a0-4368-8a97-177a9f9af796","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01P8KAQosjsYt5gFeNjSjzSH","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":81},"type":"attachment","uuid":"acd53992-65bc-4793-be0e-f400486b7e45","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:53:50.812Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-580-onwards","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"5b425e89-e7a0-4368-8a97-177a9f9af796","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01P8KAQosjsYt5gFeNjSjzSH","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\n\n`faucet_core::topology::NodeReport::error` is an `Option<String>` — the node's\nfailure is rendered to text before it leaves the executor. Everything\ndownstream that wants to react to a *kind* of failure therefore cannot, and the\nconcrete consequence today is that **a topology run whose node tripped the\nresilience circuit breaker does not get the scheduler's cooldown**, while the\nidentical failure in matrix mode does.\n\nMatrix mode was just fixed for exactly this (#654 M2): `InvocationOutcome` now\ncarries `executor::InvocationErrorKind`, and `schedule::classify` keys the\ncooldown off `InvocationErrorKind::CircuitOpen` instead of the `CircuitOpen`\ndisplay prefix. `cli/src/topology.rs::run_topology` has to set\n`error_kind: None` for every node outcome, with a comment saying why:\n\n```rust\nerror: n.error.clone(),\n// A topology node reports its failure as an already-rendered\n// string (`NodeReport.error`), so there is no typed error left to\n// classify here.\nerror_kind: None,\n```\n\nSo the fix stopped one layer short of the graph runtime.\n\n## Motivation\n\nPrimary Goal — reliability. The cooldown exists so a cron tick does not\nre-fire immediately at a destination that just tripped its own breaker; losing\nit in topology mode means the pipeline hammers a failing endpoint on every\ntick, which is the behaviour the breaker was added to prevent.\n\nIt is also the same PRINCIPLES §6 violation one level down: the typed\n`FaucetError::CircuitOpen` **is** available inside the node task, and is\ndiscarded at the reporting boundary. Fixing it removes the last place in the\nrun path where a failure class has to be recovered from prose (or, as now,\ncannot be recovered at all).\n\n## Proposed design\n\n`NodeReport` is already `#[non_exhaustive]`, so adding a field is a MINOR bump\nunder the declared semver contract — no major, no deprecation.\n\n1. **core** — add a typed kind alongside the rendered message:\n   ```rust","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"97e03eb9-835e-4764-aa92-d60c8a786204","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:53:53.928Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Summary\n\n`faucet_core::topology::NodeReport::error` is an `Option<String>` — the node's\nfailure is rendered to text before it leaves the executor. Everything\ndownstream that wants to react to a *kind* of failure therefore cannot, and the\nconcrete consequence today is that **a topology run whose node tripped the\nresilience circuit breaker does not get the scheduler's cooldown**, while the\nidentical failure in matrix mode does.\n\nMatrix mode was just fixed for exactly this (#654 M2): `InvocationOutcome` now\ncarries `executor::InvocationErrorKind`, and `schedule::classify` keys the\ncooldown off `InvocationErrorKind::CircuitOpen` instead of the `CircuitOpen`\ndisplay prefix. `cli/src/topology.rs::run_topology` has to set\n`error_kind: None` for every node outcome, with a comment saying why:\n\n```rust\nerror: n.error.clone(),\n// A topology node reports its failure as an already-rendered\n// string (`NodeReport.error`), so there is no typed error left to\n// classify here.\nerror_kind: None,\n```\n\nSo the fix stopped one layer short of the graph runtime.\n\n## Motivation\n\nPrimary Goal — reliability. The cooldown exists so a cron tick does not\nre-fire immediately at a destination that just tripped its own breaker; losing\nit in topology mode means the pipeline hammers a failing endpoint on every\ntick, which is the behaviour the breaker was added to prevent.\n\nIt is also the same PRINCIPLES §6 violation one level down: the typed\n`FaucetError::CircuitOpen` **is** available inside the node task, and is\ndiscarded at the reporting boundary. Fixing it removes the last place in the\nrun path where a failure class has to be recovered from prose (or, as now,\ncannot be recovered at all).\n\n## Proposed design\n\n`NodeReport` is already `#[non_exhaustive]`, so adding a field is a MINOR bump\nunder the declared semver contract — no major, no deprecation.\n\n1. **core** — add a typed kind alongside the rendered message:\n   ```rust","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"5b425e89-e7a0-4368-8a97-177a9f9af796","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-580-onwards","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
