{"parentUuid":"6679f414-6f26-4e9e-add2-7cf4828fa99c","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_017P8M4Ktx3nttgYB6oHNLq4","type":"tool_result","content":"   ```rust\n   /// Typed class of `error`, for callers that react to a kind of failure\n   /// rather than report it. `None` when the node succeeded.\n   pub error_kind: Option<NodeErrorKind>,\n   ```\n   with\n   ```rust\n   #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n   #[non_exhaustive]\n   pub enum NodeErrorKind { CircuitOpen, Other }\n   ```\n   Classify it where the node's `Result<_, FaucetError>` is still intact, in\n   the per-node task join in `run_reported`, via one pure\n   `fn classify(&FaucetError) -> NodeErrorKind`. Keep `error` exactly as it is\n   — this is additive, and the message is what users read.\n\n   Consider putting the classifier next to `FaucetError` instead and having\n   both `NodeErrorKind` and the CLI's `InvocationErrorKind` derive from it, so\n   there is one table rather than two that can drift. That is the better shape\n   if the two enums stay in step; if they diverge (the CLI's covers\n   `CliError`, not just `FaucetError`) keep them separate and cross-reference.\n\n2. **cli** — in `run_topology`, map `NodeErrorKind` → `InvocationErrorKind`\n   when building each node's `InvocationOutcome`, replacing the\n   `error_kind: None` and its comment. The scheduler then needs no change at\n   all: `classify` already reads the field.\n\n3. Extend `post_run_observability` if a per-node kind is worth a metric label\n   — but only if it does not raise cardinality (`kind` is a closed set, so it\n   is safe).\n\n### Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/core/src/topology.rs` — `NodeReport`, the new enum, the classifier,\n  and `run_reported`'s join arm.\n- `cli/src/topology.rs` — `run_topology`'s outcome construction.\n- `cli/src/executor.rs` — possibly a `From<NodeErrorKind>` for\n  `InvocationErrorKind`.\n- `.claude/rules/architecture.md` — the `topology.rs` \"Reporting (#459)\"\n  paragraph describing `NodeReport`.\n\n## Edge cases & failure modes\n\n- **A node cancelled by `TopologyOnError::Propagate`** must not be classified\n  `CircuitOpen` just because a *sibling* tripped — only the node that raised\n  it. Pin this with a test: one node trips, a sibling is cancelled, exactly\n  one report carries `CircuitOpen`.\n- **A panicked node task** has no typed error; `error_kind` stays `None`\n  (distinct from `Some(Other)`), matching the convention the CLI's\n  `InvocationErrorKind` doc already states.\n- **Multiple nodes trip** — the scheduler applies one cooldown; `classify`","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"4c5ee784-2f13-4149-b70c-c103429523a3","timestamp":"2026-09-19T10:54:00.907Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"   ```rust\n   /// Typed class of `error`, for callers that react to a kind of failure\n   /// rather than report it. `None` when the node succeeded.\n   pub error_kind: Option<NodeErrorKind>,\n   ```\n   with\n   ```rust\n   #[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, PartialEq, Eq)]\n   #[non_exhaustive]\n   pub enum NodeErrorKind { CircuitOpen, Other }\n   ```\n   Classify it where the node's `Result<_, FaucetError>` is still intact, in\n   the per-node task join in `run_reported`, via one pure\n   `fn classify(&FaucetError) -> NodeErrorKind`. Keep `error` exactly as it is\n   — this is additive, and the message is what users read.\n\n   Consider putting the classifier next to `FaucetError` instead and having\n   both `NodeErrorKind` and the CLI's `InvocationErrorKind` derive from it, so\n   there is one table rather than two that can drift. That is the better shape\n   if the two enums stay in step; if they diverge (the CLI's covers\n   `CliError`, not just `FaucetError`) keep them separate and cross-reference.\n\n2. **cli** — in `run_topology`, map `NodeErrorKind` → `InvocationErrorKind`\n   when building each node's `InvocationOutcome`, replacing the\n   `error_kind: None` and its comment. The scheduler then needs no change at\n   all: `classify` already reads the field.\n\n3. Extend `post_run_observability` if a per-node kind is worth a metric label\n   — but only if it does not raise cardinality (`kind` is a closed set, so it\n   is safe).\n\n### Affected crates / files\n\n- `crates/core/src/topology.rs` — `NodeReport`, the new enum, the classifier,\n  and `run_reported`'s join arm.\n- `cli/src/topology.rs` — `run_topology`'s outcome construction.\n- `cli/src/executor.rs` — possibly a `From<NodeErrorKind>` for\n  `InvocationErrorKind`.\n- `.claude/rules/architecture.md` — the `topology.rs` \"Reporting (#459)\"\n  paragraph describing `NodeReport`.\n\n## Edge cases & failure modes\n\n- **A node cancelled by `TopologyOnError::Propagate`** must not be classified\n  `CircuitOpen` just because a *sibling* tripped — only the node that raised\n  it. Pin this with a test: one node trips, a sibling is cancelled, exactly\n  one report carries `CircuitOpen`.\n- **A panicked node task** has no typed error; `error_kind` stays `None`\n  (distinct from `Some(Other)`), matching the convention the CLI's\n  `InvocationErrorKind` doc already states.\n- **Multiple nodes trip** — the scheduler applies one cooldown; `classify`","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"6679f414-6f26-4e9e-add2-7cf4828fa99c","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-580-onwards","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
