{"parentUuid":"e5c2b777-fd5d-4f32-975b-3efd22d7698a","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCgdaMv6pwhSVPbLU2Va","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"All green, including the sibling-isolation edge case. Committing #658:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_read_input_tokens":740821,"output_tokens":1024,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":740821,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCgdYHt8ZoPFmVC6SuSg","type":"assistant","uuid":"a6dcb7b2-93f8-4158-b14c-33ba27b78d7e","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:01:41.125Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"a6dcb7b2-93f8-4158-b14c-33ba27b78d7e","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCgdaMv6pwhSVPbLU2Va","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_017VHQuSUNAAKHzcfS862job","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\n# fold the WIP commit into a proper one\ngit add -u crates/core/src/topology.rs cli/src/topology.rs\ngit reset -q --soft HEAD~1\ngit add -u crates/core/src/topology.rs cli/src/topology.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(core/cli): carry a typed failure kind on NodeReport so topology runs cool down\n\n`NodeReport.error` was an already-rendered `String`, so the class of a\nnode's failure died at the reporting boundary. The concrete consequence:\na **topology** run whose node tripped the resilience circuit breaker got\nno scheduler cooldown, while the identical failure in **matrix** mode did\n(#654 M2 fixed that half). A cron tick therefore re-fired immediately at\na destination that had just tripped its own breaker — precisely what the\nbreaker exists to prevent.\n\n- `faucet_core::topology::NodeErrorKind` (`CircuitOpen` | `Other`,\n  `#[non_exhaustive]`) plus one pure `classify(&FaucetError)`, applied at\n  the two sites where a node's typed error is turned into text — so the\n  table lives once, where the error is still intact.\n- `NodeReport.error_kind: Option<NodeErrorKind>` alongside the unchanged\n  `error`. Additive on a `#[non_exhaustive]` struct: a minor bump under\n  the declared semver contract.\n- `cli::topology::build_summary` maps it to `InvocationErrorKind`, so the\n  scheduler needs no change — `schedule::classify` already reads the\n  field.\n\n`None` keeps meaning \"did not fail\", never \"failed, unclassified\".\n\nThe pre-existing test asserting the kind was *unset* said in its own\ncomment that it should be what changes when this lands, so it now asserts\nthe guarantee that actually matters and survives the fix: classification\ncomes from the typed kind, **never** from what the message happens to\nsay. A failure whose text reads \"Circuit open after 3 consecutive\nfailures\" but carries no kind is still not classified as one.\n\nThe edge case the issue calls out is pinned too: when one node trips and\nits siblings are cancelled so they can flush, exactly one report carries\n`CircuitOpen` — a cancelled sibling must not earn a breaker cooldown.\n\nCloses #658\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit the 658 fix properly"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_read_input_tokens":740821,"output_tokens":1024,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1024,"cache_read_input_tokens":740821,"cache_creation_input_tokens":979,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":979},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_017VHQuSUNAAKHzcfS862job":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\n# fold the WIP commit into a proper one\ngit add -u crates/core/src/topology.rs cli/src/topology.rs\ngit reset -q --soft HEAD~1\ngit add -u crates/core/src/topology.rs cli/src/topology.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfix(core/cli): carry a typed failure kind on NodeReport so topology runs cool down\n\n`NodeReport.error` was an already-rendered `String`, so the class of a\nnode's failure died at the reporting boundary. The concrete consequence:\na **topology** run whose node tripped the resilience circuit breaker got\nno scheduler cooldown, while the identical failure in **matrix** mode did\n(#654 M2 fixed that half). A cron tick therefore re-fired immediately at\na destination that had just tripped its own breaker — precisely what the\nbreaker exists to prevent.\n\n- `faucet_core::topology::NodeErrorKind` (`CircuitOpen` | `Other`,\n  `#[non_exhaustive]`) plus one pure `classify(&FaucetError)`, applied at\n  the two sites where a node's typed error is turned into text — so the\n  table lives once, where the error is still intact.\n- `NodeReport.error_kind: Option<NodeErrorKind>` alongside the unchanged\n  `error`. Additive on a `#[non_exhaustive]` struct: a minor bump under\n  the declared semver contract.\n- `cli::topology::build_summary` maps it to `InvocationErrorKind`, so the\n  scheduler needs no change — `schedule::classify` already reads the\n  field.\n\n`None` keeps meaning \"did not fail\", never \"failed, unclassified\".\n\nThe pre-existing test asserting the kind was *unset* said in its own\ncomment that it should be what changes when this lands, so it now asserts\nthe guarantee that actually matters and survives the fix: classification\ncomes from the typed kind, **never** from what the message happens to\nsay. A failure whose text reads \"Circuit open after 3 consecutive\nfailures\" but carries no kind is still not classified as one.\n\nThe edge case the issue calls out is pinned too: when one node trips and\nits siblings are cancelled so they can flush, exactly one report carries\n`CircuitOpen` — a cancelled sibling must not earn a breaker cooldown.\n\nCloses #658\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit the 658 fix properly"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfCgdYHt8ZoPFmVC6SuSg","type":"assistant","uuid":"00ac539f-aa08-41d1-bae7-3b9c5b7c987e","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:01:52.216Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
