{"parentUuid":"d443b071-d0b9-416f-aa26-5b394eb007f5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfChgYVFD5feoGmEoBj56","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Zero drift, schema gate green. Committing #644:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":774585,"output_tokens":1089,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1126,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":774585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1126},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfChgXJJmcB8HjaRja2BX","type":"assistant","uuid":"a8c88af4-597b-4654-a813-4645600d998d","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:15:28.122Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"a8c88af4-597b-4654-a813-4645600d998d","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfChgYVFD5feoGmEoBj56","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_019YY3u5eiDAr3J7LpsARdqT","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -A cli/src crates/core/src docs/book/src/reference/config.md schemas/faucet.schema.json cli/tests/partitioned_run.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(executor): cost-aware (LPT) dispatch order for matrix roots\n\nReady sibling rows queued for a concurrency permit in matrix-declaration\norder, so total wall-clock depended on the order the user happened to\nlist objects in. Measured on a 21-object Salesforce → BigQuery run at\n`max_concurrent: 8`: the two large objects sat late in the matrix and\nfinished ~9 minutes after the other 19 were done, with 6 of the 8 slots\nidle — a recoverable ~9 min of a 32.5 min run.\n\n`execution.schedule: lpt` dispatches the heaviest rows first. This is\n`P || Cmax`: longest-processing-time-first is provably within 4/3 of the\noptimal makespan, while largest-*last* — which declaration order can\nproduce by accident — is the worst case.\n\n- `DispatchOrder` (`declared` default | `lpt`) on `execution`, and an\n  optional per-row `weight`. The default path is byte-for-byte what it\n  was.\n- The policy is one pure function, `order_ready`, so it is tested without\n  standing up a pipeline. It sorts **stably**, so ties and unweighted\n  rows keep declaration order — dispatch must stay predictable from the\n  config alone — and unweighted rows sort last rather than displacing a\n  row somebody costed. A NaN weight (a config can carry one) is ordered\n  with `total_cmp`, since `partial_cmp` would leave the comparator\n  inconsistent and the sort unsound.\n- `faucet discover` fills `weight` in per generated row, estimated as\n  **rows × row width** from the descriptor's row estimate and column\n  types. Bytes, not rows, is the load-bearing choice: a 970k-row ×\n  3-column history table is *lighter* than a 122k-row × 100-column\n  object, so ranking on row count alone mis-orders exactly the wide\n  objects this is meant to front-load. Discovery is where both halves are\n  known, so the estimate lives there and the executor only ranks.\n\nOnly the enqueue order changes: same permit budget, same `JoinSet`, same\n`on_error` cancellation, and children / `depends_on` rows keep their\ncompletion-gated ordering. A discovery row publishes a value set rather\nthan moving data, so it carries no weight.\n\nCloses #644\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit the LPT dispatch work"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":774585,"output_tokens":1089,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1126,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1089,"cache_read_input_tokens":774585,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1126,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1126},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_019YY3u5eiDAr3J7LpsARdqT":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -A cli/src crates/core/src docs/book/src/reference/config.md schemas/faucet.schema.json cli/tests/partitioned_run.rs\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(executor): cost-aware (LPT) dispatch order for matrix roots\n\nReady sibling rows queued for a concurrency permit in matrix-declaration\norder, so total wall-clock depended on the order the user happened to\nlist objects in. Measured on a 21-object Salesforce → BigQuery run at\n`max_concurrent: 8`: the two large objects sat late in the matrix and\nfinished ~9 minutes after the other 19 were done, with 6 of the 8 slots\nidle — a recoverable ~9 min of a 32.5 min run.\n\n`execution.schedule: lpt` dispatches the heaviest rows first. This is\n`P || Cmax`: longest-processing-time-first is provably within 4/3 of the\noptimal makespan, while largest-*last* — which declaration order can\nproduce by accident — is the worst case.\n\n- `DispatchOrder` (`declared` default | `lpt`) on `execution`, and an\n  optional per-row `weight`. The default path is byte-for-byte what it\n  was.\n- The policy is one pure function, `order_ready`, so it is tested without\n  standing up a pipeline. It sorts **stably**, so ties and unweighted\n  rows keep declaration order — dispatch must stay predictable from the\n  config alone — and unweighted rows sort last rather than displacing a\n  row somebody costed. A NaN weight (a config can carry one) is ordered\n  with `total_cmp`, since `partial_cmp` would leave the comparator\n  inconsistent and the sort unsound.\n- `faucet discover` fills `weight` in per generated row, estimated as\n  **rows × row width** from the descriptor's row estimate and column\n  types. Bytes, not rows, is the load-bearing choice: a 970k-row ×\n  3-column history table is *lighter* than a 122k-row × 100-column\n  object, so ranking on row count alone mis-orders exactly the wide\n  objects this is meant to front-load. Discovery is where both halves are\n  known, so the estimate lives there and the executor only ranks.\n\nOnly the enqueue order changes: same permit budget, same `JoinSet`, same\n`on_error` cancellation, and children / `depends_on` rows keep their\ncompletion-gated ordering. A discovery row publishes a value set rather\nthan moving data, so it carries no weight.\n\nCloses #644\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit the LPT dispatch work"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfChgXJJmcB8HjaRja2BX","type":"assistant","uuid":"fde37720-3feb-4920-a6af-169cde9e4c1c","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:15:41.068Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
