{"parentUuid":"a5bfdadd-61e3-4813-94c9-7abc92160dee","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01NZebUT9QfMwLbecDjAQysY","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":71},"type":"attachment","uuid":"6ce79e9c-3f54-459c-af20-0ddceed80db5","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:16:30.367Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"a5bfdadd-61e3-4813-94c9-7abc92160dee","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NZebUT9QfMwLbecDjAQysY","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\nThe async-job (Salesforce Bulk) poll loop in `faucet-source-rest` sleeps a **fixed** `poll.interval_secs` between status checks, so a job that finishes shortly after submit still waits a full interval before it's noticed. Measured on a real Salesforce Bulk `User` job: **33s total at interval_secs=15, 22s at interval_secs=2** — i.e. ~11s of pure dead wait attributable to the fixed interval. A fixed *low* interval is not a fix (a 100-minute full sync would hammer the API for hours).\n\n## Motivation\n[Primary Goal — performance/reliability.] Quick jobs (small objects, validation runs) should be detected in seconds; long jobs should poll gently. Fixed interval can't do both.\n\n## Fix\nAdaptive **exponential backoff**, capped at `interval_secs`: poll immediately, then on each `Pending` result sleep `min(delay*2, interval_secs)` starting from ~1s. `interval_secs` becomes the cap (back-compatible: long jobs still poll ≤ interval_secs), quick jobs detected in ~1–3s.\n\n## Affected files\n`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs` (the `prepare_async_job` poll loop).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Quick job detected in ~1–3s even with a large `interval_secs`; wall-clock well under one interval (wiremock test).\n- Backoff never exceeds `interval_secs`; `timeout_secs` still fires.\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## References\nFound profiling the Salesforce Bulk `User` run (33s/701 rows). Companion to #623 (async_job streaming) and #627 (token form-encoding). Roadmap epic #38.","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1cc92864-c6ad-4ce9-8183-55fc4cf651ae","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:16:34.021Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Summary\nThe async-job (Salesforce Bulk) poll loop in `faucet-source-rest` sleeps a **fixed** `poll.interval_secs` between status checks, so a job that finishes shortly after submit still waits a full interval before it's noticed. Measured on a real Salesforce Bulk `User` job: **33s total at interval_secs=15, 22s at interval_secs=2** — i.e. ~11s of pure dead wait attributable to the fixed interval. A fixed *low* interval is not a fix (a 100-minute full sync would hammer the API for hours).\n\n## Motivation\n[Primary Goal — performance/reliability.] Quick jobs (small objects, validation runs) should be detected in seconds; long jobs should poll gently. Fixed interval can't do both.\n\n## Fix\nAdaptive **exponential backoff**, capped at `interval_secs`: poll immediately, then on each `Pending` result sleep `min(delay*2, interval_secs)` starting from ~1s. `interval_secs` becomes the cap (back-compatible: long jobs still poll ≤ interval_secs), quick jobs detected in ~1–3s.\n\n## Affected files\n`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs` (the `prepare_async_job` poll loop).\n\n## Acceptance criteria\n- Quick job detected in ~1–3s even with a large `interval_secs`; wall-clock well under one interval (wiremock test).\n- Backoff never exceeds `interval_secs`; `timeout_secs` still fires.\n- ≥95% patch coverage.\n\n## References\nFound profiling the Salesforce Bulk `User` run (33s/701 rows). Companion to #623 (async_job streaming) and #627 (token form-encoding). Roadmap epic #38.","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"a5bfdadd-61e3-4813-94c9-7abc92160dee","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
