{"parentUuid":"caac312f-9ad7-4a35-adad-264640b91252","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01GBGPyhhefFG3jzChnpYGz4","type":"tool_result","content":"/// [`DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES`].\nconst DEFAULT_RETRY_BACKOFF: Duration = Duration::from_secs(1);\n\n/// Starting delay for async-job poll backoff (doubles each Pending poll, up to\n/// the configured `poll.interval_secs` cap).\nconst POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_SECS: u64 = 1;\n\n/// Next async-job poll delay: exponential backoff (double the current delay),\n/// capped at `cap`. `interval_secs` is the ceiling, so a quick job is noticed in\n/// ~1s while a long job settles at the configured interval. Saturating so a\n/// large current delay never overflows.\nfn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\n    std::cmp::min(current.saturating_mul(2), cap)\n}\n\n/// Attach a mutual-TLS client identity (from [`TlsClientConfig`]) to the HTTP\n/// client builder. Only compiled with the `mtls` feature; the non-`mtls` stub\n/// errors so a `tls:` block on a build without the feature fails loudly rather\n/// than silently sending no client certificate.\n#[cfg(feature = \"mtls\")]\nfn apply_client_tls(\n═══ used in the loop?\n91:fn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\n1494:                    poll_delay = next_poll_delay(poll_delay, poll_cap);\n2765:    fn next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps() {\n2769:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(1), cap),\n2773:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(2), cap),\n2777:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(4), cap),\n2781:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(8), cap), cap);\n2782:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(cap, cap), cap);\n2785:            next_poll_delay(Duration::ZERO, Duration::ZERO),\n2789:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(u64::MAX), cap), cap);\n═══ tests\ncrates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:91:fn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\ncrates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:2765:    fn next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps() {\ncrates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs:358:/// and a 60s cap, exponential backoff starts at ~1s, so the run finishes in a\ncrates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs:406:        \"poll backoff should finish far under the 60s interval cap, took {elapsed:?}\"\ncrates/source/rest/tests/stream_test.rs:1358:            .retry_backoff(std::time::Duration::from_millis(1)),","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"1c437712-6028-4e03-b9d9-0ac27b162b20","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:16:50.027Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"/// [`DEFAULT_MAX_RETRIES`].\nconst DEFAULT_RETRY_BACKOFF: Duration = Duration::from_secs(1);\n\n/// Starting delay for async-job poll backoff (doubles each Pending poll, up to\n/// the configured `poll.interval_secs` cap).\nconst POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_SECS: u64 = 1;\n\n/// Next async-job poll delay: exponential backoff (double the current delay),\n/// capped at `cap`. `interval_secs` is the ceiling, so a quick job is noticed in\n/// ~1s while a long job settles at the configured interval. Saturating so a\n/// large current delay never overflows.\nfn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\n    std::cmp::min(current.saturating_mul(2), cap)\n}\n\n/// Attach a mutual-TLS client identity (from [`TlsClientConfig`]) to the HTTP\n/// client builder. Only compiled with the `mtls` feature; the non-`mtls` stub\n/// errors so a `tls:` block on a build without the feature fails loudly rather\n/// than silently sending no client certificate.\n#[cfg(feature = \"mtls\")]\nfn apply_client_tls(\n═══ used in the loop?\n91:fn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\n1494:                    poll_delay = next_poll_delay(poll_delay, poll_cap);\n2765:    fn next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps() {\n2769:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(1), cap),\n2773:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(2), cap),\n2777:            next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(4), cap),\n2781:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(8), cap), cap);\n2782:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(cap, cap), cap);\n2785:            next_poll_delay(Duration::ZERO, Duration::ZERO),\n2789:        assert_eq!(next_poll_delay(Duration::from_secs(u64::MAX), cap), cap);\n═══ tests\ncrates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:91:fn next_poll_delay(current: Duration, cap: Duration) -> Duration {\ncrates/source/rest/src/stream.rs:2765:    fn next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps() {\ncrates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs:358:/// and a 60s cap, exponential backoff starts at ~1s, so the run finishes in a\ncrates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs:406:        \"poll backoff should finish far under the 60s interval cap, took {elapsed:?}\"\ncrates/source/rest/tests/stream_test.rs:1358:            .retry_backoff(std::time::Duration::from_millis(1)),","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"caac312f-9ad7-4a35-adad-264640b91252","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
