{"parentUuid":"770306f3-eff2-456b-985f-4317ac8d7775","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfChnkTFQzDwWL7FLXCCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**#628 is already done** — `next_poll_delay` doubles with a cap, wired at `stream.rs:1494`, with unit tests *and* a wiremock test asserting the run finishes far under the interval. My earlier bulk check searched the wrong file, which means I should re-verify the other \"absent\" verdicts more carefully:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":778509,"output_tokens":1374,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":572},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1374,"cache_read_input_tokens":778509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfChnhwS8r4LUfyHGYxsP","type":"assistant","uuid":"27f4740c-0442-4773-8090-a0ac0b7f9db4","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:17:01.040Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"27f4740c-0442-4773-8090-a0ac0b7f9db4","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfChnkTFQzDwWL7FLXCCt","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01MQsRwmYEgdtdAWmqsmJhHh","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 628 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason completed --comment \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nVerified against the code — implemented, closing.\n\n`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs`:\n- `POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_SECS = 1` and `fn next_poll_delay(current, cap) = min(current*2, cap)` — exponential backoff whose ceiling is the configured `poll.interval_secs`, exactly the shape proposed (back-compatible: a long job still settles at the configured interval).\n- Wired into the async-job poll loop at `stream.rs:1494` (`poll_delay = next_poll_delay(poll_delay, poll_cap)`).\n\nTests:\n- `next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps` — doubling, the cap, a zero cap, and `Duration::from_secs(u64::MAX)` saturating instead of overflowing.\n- `crates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs` — a wiremock job with a 60s interval cap that asserts the run completes far under one interval (\"poll backoff should finish far under the 60s interval cap, took {elapsed:?}\").\n\nThat covers every acceptance criterion: quick detection despite a large `interval_secs`, backoff bounded by the cap, and `timeout_secs` unaffected.\n\n(Apologies for the noise if this was already known — my first automated sweep looked for this in a `async_job.rs` that does not exist and wrongly reported it missing; re-checked against `stream.rs`.)\nEOF\n)\" 2>&1 | tail -1","description":"Close 628 with evidence"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_read_input_tokens":778509,"output_tokens":1374,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":572},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1374,"cache_read_input_tokens":778509,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1415,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1415},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01MQsRwmYEgdtdAWmqsmJhHh":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh issue close 628 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --reason completed --comment \"$(cat <<'EOF'\nVerified against the code — implemented, closing.\n\n`crates/source/rest/src/stream.rs`:\n- `POLL_BACKOFF_BASE_SECS = 1` and `fn next_poll_delay(current, cap) = min(current*2, cap)` — exponential backoff whose ceiling is the configured `poll.interval_secs`, exactly the shape proposed (back-compatible: a long job still settles at the configured interval).\n- Wired into the async-job poll loop at `stream.rs:1494` (`poll_delay = next_poll_delay(poll_delay, poll_cap)`).\n\nTests:\n- `next_poll_delay_doubles_then_caps` — doubling, the cap, a zero cap, and `Duration::from_secs(u64::MAX)` saturating instead of overflowing.\n- `crates/source/rest/tests/async_job_test.rs` — a wiremock job with a 60s interval cap that asserts the run completes far under one interval (\"poll backoff should finish far under the 60s interval cap, took {elapsed:?}\").\n\nThat covers every acceptance criterion: quick detection despite a large `interval_secs`, backoff bounded by the cap, and `timeout_secs` unaffected.\n\n(Apologies for the noise if this was already known — my first automated sweep looked for this in a `async_job.rs` that