-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"05d976d5-e818-400b-a807-22e0052a9bec","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"hook_non_blocking_error","hookName":"PreToolUse:Bash","toolUseID":"toolu_01FNxrSnrdxxHr5v2o9VfYwC","hookEvent":"PreToolUse","stderr":"Failed with non-blocking status code: /bin/sh: rtk: command not found","stdout":"","exitCode":127,"command":"rtk hook claude","durationMs":73},"type":"attachment","uuid":"867c4a24-f2d8-4bf9-ba89-c53a4b2d8aec","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:17:44.679Z","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"05d976d5-e818-400b-a807-22e0052a9bec","isSidechain":false,"promptId":"23ad4779-0c1f-48fc-a10e-1c92c4154f79","type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01FNxrSnrdxxHr5v2o9VfYwC","type":"tool_result","content":"## Summary\n\nAdd an opt-in **JSON (structured) logging** format for all faucet log output. Today every subscriber install site uses `tracing_subscriber::fmt()` / `fmt::layer()` — the default **human-readable text** format. Introduce a `--log-format text|json` flag (default `text`) + `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` env that switches the formatter to line-delimited JSON, so logs can be ingested directly by Datadog / Elastic / Loki / CloudWatch / Splunk without regex parsing.\n\n## Motivation\n\nPrimary Goal + production-readiness. `faucet serve` / `faucet schedule` / `faucet run` are run as long-lived services and in orchestrators (k8s, ECS, Nomad) whose log pipelines expect **one JSON object per line** with structured fields. Text logs force brittle grok/regex parsing and lose the structured context faucet already produces. The code *already* records rich `tracing` spans and fields — `pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`, `connector`, `records_written`, error `kind`, etc. — so they're currently rendered to text and thrown away as structure. A JSON formatter surfaces them as first-class fields for free. This is the standard expectation for modern data tooling (Meltano, Airbyte, dbt, Fivetran connectors all emit structured logs).\n\n## Current state (verified)\n\nFour subscriber install sites, all text:\n- `cli/src/lib.rs::install_tracing` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt().with_env_filter(..).with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)` (the `run`/`validate`/`schedule`/one-shot path).\n- `cli/src/serve/observability.rs::install_subscriber` — `fmt::layer().with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)` (+ `RunLogLayer` for the SSE/persisted run-log capture).\n- `cli/src/mcp/mod.rs` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt()` (MCP stdio server; note: JSON must go to **stderr**, never stdout, which carries the MCP protocol).\n- `cli/src/tui/mod.rs` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt().with_ansi(false)` (TUI log pane).\n\nNo `--log-format` / `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` exists. `RedactingMakeWriter` (secret redaction at the I/O boundary) already wraps the writer and must keep wrapping it under JSON.\n\n## Proposed design\n\n- **`LogFormat { Text, Json }`** enum (default `Text`), parsed from a global `--log-format` clap arg (`cli/src/cli.rs`) and `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT`, flag winning. Thread it into all four install sites (alongside the existing `--log-level`).\n- **Text**: unchanged (`fmt()` / `fmt::layer()`), so default behavior is byte-identical.\n- **Json**: `tracing_subscriber::fmt().json().flatten_event(true).with_current_span(true).with_span_list(false)` (and the `fmt::layer().json()` equivalent for serve), keeping `EnvFilter` + `RedactingMakeWriter`. One JSON object per line: `{timestamp, level, target, message, <span+event fields>}`. Fields like `pipeline`/`row`/`run_id`/`connector` come through automatically from the existing spans.\n- **Serve run-log capture (`RunLogLayer`, `serve/logs.rs`)**: currently formats a text line `<ts> <LEVEL> <target>: <msg>` for the ephemeral ring / SSE / console. Under `json`, capture a JSON object per line (`{ts, level, target, message}`) so `GET /v1/runs/{id}/logs` (SSE + `?format=jsonl`) and the console are consistent with stderr. The persisted `RunLogLine{seq,ts,level,line}` already has structured columns; only the `line` rendering changes. (Alternatively: always keep the structured fields and let the *format* flag pick the rendering.)\n- **MCP caveat**: the MCP server speaks JSON-RPC on **stdout**; logs already go to stderr — keep it that way under `json` so the two JSON streams never mix.\n- Redaction: `RedactingMakeWriter` operates on the serialized bytes, so it works unchanged for JSON (a resolved secret that appears in a field value is still scrubbed).\n\n## Affected crates / files\n- `cli/src/cli.rs` (global `--log-format` arg + `LogFormat` enum), `cli/src/lib.rs` (`install_tracing` signature + dispatch), `cli/src/serve/observability.rs` (`install_subscriber`), `cli/src/mcp/mod.rs`, `cli/src/tui/mod.rs`, `cli/src/serve/logs.rs` (`RunLogLayer` JSON capture).\n- Docs: `docs/book/src/operations/observability.md`, `docs/book/src/reference/cli.md` (global flags), `cli/README.md`.\n═══ current tracing install\ncli/src/lib.rs:239:fn install_tracing(level: &str) {\ncli/src/lib.rs-240-    use crate::secrets::registry::RedactingMakeWriter;\ncli/src/lib.rs-241-    use tracing_subscriber::EnvFilter;\ncli/src/lib.rs-242-    let filter = EnvFilter::try_new(level).unwrap_or_else(|_| EnvFilter::new(\"info\"));\ncli/src/lib.rs-243-    let _ = tracing_subscriber::fmt()\ncli/src/lib.rs-244-        .with_env_filter(filter)\ncli/src/lib.rs-245-        .with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)\ncli/src/lib.rs-246-        .try_init();\ncli/src/lib.rs-247-}\ncli/src/lib.rs-248-\ncli/src/lib.rs-249-/// Stub used when the `observability` feature is disabled. Logging falls back to\ncli/src/lib.rs-250-/// whatever the host environment has wired (or nothing).\ncli/src/lib.rs-251-#[cfg(not(feature = \"observability\"))]\ncli/src/lib.rs:252:fn install_tracing(_level: &str) {}\ncli/src/lib.rs-253-\ncli/src/lib.rs-254-/// Convenience entry point for integration tests and custom hosts: parse a\ncli/src/lib.rs-255-/// YAML config string, expand the matrix, and run all rows.\ncli/src/lib.rs-256-///\ncli/src/lib.rs-257-/// This skips the `install_observability` call that [`commands::run::run`]\ncli/src/lib.rs-258-/// performs — callers can wire their own `metrics` recorder / tracing\ncli/src/lib.rs-259-/// subscriber before calling this function (or not at all).\ncli/src/lib.rs-260-pub async fn run_from_yaml_str(yaml: &str) -> CliResult<executor::RunSummary> {\ncli/src/lib.rs-261-    // Parse first, then resolve ${env}/${file}/${secret} INTO the parsed tree\ncli/src/lib.rs-262-    // (post-parse) so a resolved value can never alter the document's structure\ncli/src/lib.rs-263-    // (F43) — mirroring the binary's `from_path` path.\ncli/src/lib.rs-264-    let mut value: serde_json::Value =\ncli/src/lib.rs-265-        serde_yaml::from_str(yaml).map_err(|e| CliError::ParseConfig {\ncli/src/lib.rs-266-            path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\"<yaml-string>\"),\ncli/src/lib.rs-267-            message: e.to_string(),\ncli/src/lib.rs-268-        })?;\ncli/src/lib.rs-269-    interpolate::interpolate_value(&mut value)?;\ncli/src/lib.rs-270-    // Bind `${param.*}` from the config's own `params:` defaults (#444). No","is_error":false}]},"uuid":"df1d4e4c-5e7d-443b-bf0f-5d40a3383d23","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:17:47.845Z","toolUseResult":{"stdout":"## Summary\n\nAdd an opt-in **JSON (structured) logging** format for all faucet log output. Today every subscriber install site uses `tracing_subscriber::fmt()` / `fmt::layer()` — the default **human-readable text** format. Introduce a `--log-format text|json` flag (default `text`) + `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` env that switches the formatter to line-delimited JSON, so logs can be ingested directly by Datadog / Elastic / Loki / CloudWatch / Splunk without regex parsing.\n\n## Motivation\n\nPrimary Goal + production-readiness. `faucet serve` / `faucet schedule` / `faucet run` are run as long-lived services and in orchestrators (k8s, ECS, Nomad) whose log pipelines expect **one JSON object per line** with structured fields. Text logs force brittle grok/regex parsing and lose the structured context faucet already produces. The code *already* records rich `tracing` spans and fields — `pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`, `connector`, `records_written`, error `kind`, etc. — so they're currently rendered to text and thrown away as structure. A JSON formatter surfaces them as first-class fields for free. This is the standard expectation for modern data tooling (Meltano, Airbyte, dbt, Fivetran connectors all emit structured logs).\n\n## Current state (verified)\n\nFour subscriber install sites, all text:\n- `cli/src/lib.rs::install_tracing` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt().with_env_filter(..).with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)` (the `run`/`validate`/`schedule`/one-shot path).\n- `cli/src/serve/observability.rs::install_subscriber` — `fmt::layer().with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)` (+ `RunLogLayer` for the SSE/persisted run-log capture).\n- `cli/src/mcp/mod.rs` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt()` (MCP stdio server; note: JSON must go to **stderr**, never stdout, which carries the MCP protocol).\n- `cli/src/tui/mod.rs` — `tracing_subscriber::fmt().with_ansi(false)` (TUI log pane).\n\nNo `--log-format` / `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` exists. `RedactingMakeWriter` (secret redaction at the I/O boundary) already wraps the writer and must keep wrapping it under JSON.\n\n## Proposed design\n\n- **`LogFormat { Text, Json }`** enum (default `Text`), parsed from a global `--log-format` clap arg (`cli/src/cli.rs`) and `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT`, flag winning. Thread it into all four install sites (alongside the existing `--log-level`).\n- **Text**: unchanged (`fmt()` / `fmt::layer()`), so default behavior is byte-identical.\n- **Json**: `tracing_subscriber::fmt().json().flatten_event(true).with_current_span(true).with_span_list(false)` (and the `fmt::layer().json()` equivalent for serve), keeping `EnvFilter` + `RedactingMakeWriter`. One JSON object per line: `{timestamp, level, target, message, <span+event fields>}`. Fields like `pipeline`/`row`/`run_id`/`connector` come through automatically from the existing spans.\n- **Serve run-log capture (`RunLogLayer`, `serve/logs.rs`)**: currently formats a text line `<ts> <LEVEL> <target>: <msg>` for the ephemeral ring / SSE / console. Under `json`, capture a JSON object per line (`{ts, level, target, message}`) so `GET /v1/runs/{id}/logs` (SSE + `?format=jsonl`) and the console are consistent with stderr. The persisted `RunLogLine{seq,ts,level,line}` already has structured columns; only the `line` rendering changes. (Alternatively: always keep the structured fields and let the *format* flag pick the rendering.)\n- **MCP caveat**: the MCP server speaks JSON-RPC on **stdout**; logs already go to stderr — keep it that way under `json` so the two JSON streams never mix.\n- Redaction: `RedactingMakeWriter` operates on the serialized bytes, so it works unchanged for JSON (a resolved secret that appears in a field value is still scrubbed).\n\n## Affected crates / files\n- `cli/src/cli.rs` (global `--log-format` arg + `LogFormat` enum), `cli/src/lib.rs` (`install_tracing` signature + dispatch), `cli/src/serve/observability.rs` (`install_subscriber`), `cli/src/mcp/mod.rs`, `cli/src/tui/mod.rs`, `cli/src/serve/logs.rs` (`RunLogLayer` JSON capture).\n- Docs: `docs/book/src/operations/observability.md`, `docs/book/src/reference/cli.md` (global flags), `cli/README.md`.\n═══ current tracing install\ncli/src/lib.rs:239:fn install_tracing(level: &str) {\ncli/src/lib.rs-240-    use crate::secrets::registry::RedactingMakeWriter;\ncli/src/lib.rs-241-    use tracing_subscriber::EnvFilter;\ncli/src/lib.rs-242-    let filter = EnvFilter::try_new(level).unwrap_or_else(|_| EnvFilter::new(\"info\"));\ncli/src/lib.rs-243-    let _ = tracing_subscriber::fmt()\ncli/src/lib.rs-244-        .with_env_filter(filter)\ncli/src/lib.rs-245-        .with_writer(RedactingMakeWriter)\ncli/src/lib.rs-246-        .try_init();\ncli/src/lib.rs-247-}\ncli/src/lib.rs-248-\ncli/src/lib.rs-249-/// Stub used when the `observability` feature is disabled. Logging falls back to\ncli/src/lib.rs-250-/// whatever the host environment has wired (or nothing).\ncli/src/lib.rs-251-#[cfg(not(feature = \"observability\"))]\ncli/src/lib.rs:252:fn install_tracing(_level: &str) {}\ncli/src/lib.rs-253-\ncli/src/lib.rs-254-/// Convenience entry point for integration tests and custom hosts: parse a\ncli/src/lib.rs-255-/// YAML config string, expand the matrix, and run all rows.\ncli/src/lib.rs-256-///\ncli/src/lib.rs-257-/// This skips the `install_observability` call that [`commands::run::run`]\ncli/src/lib.rs-258-/// performs — callers can wire their own `metrics` recorder / tracing\ncli/src/lib.rs-259-/// subscriber before calling this function (or not at all).\ncli/src/lib.rs-260-pub async fn run_from_yaml_str(yaml: &str) -> CliResult<executor::RunSummary> {\ncli/src/lib.rs-261-    // Parse first, then resolve ${env}/${file}/${secret} INTO the parsed tree\ncli/src/lib.rs-262-    // (post-parse) so a resolved value can never alter the document's structure\ncli/src/lib.rs-263-    // (F43) — mirroring the binary's `from_path` path.\ncli/src/lib.rs-264-    let mut value: serde_json::Value =\ncli/src/lib.rs-265-        serde_yaml::from_str(yaml).map_err(|e| CliError::ParseConfig {\ncli/src/lib.rs-266-            path: std::path::PathBuf::from(\"<yaml-string>\"),\ncli/src/lib.rs-267-            message: e.to_string(),\ncli/src/lib.rs-268-        })?;\ncli/src/lib.rs-269-    interpolate::interpolate_value(&mut value)?;\ncli/src/lib.rs-270-    // Bind `${param.*}` from the config's own `params:` defaults (#444). No","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false,"noOutputExpected":false},"sourceToolAssistantUUID":"05d976d5-e818-400b-a807-22e0052a9bec","session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
