{"parentUuid":"d1641b5b-c7eb-4329-9ac4-a58995d38251","isSidechain":false,"attachment":{"type":"total_tokens_reminder","text":"<total_tokens>14791690 tokens left</total_tokens>"},"type":"attachment","uuid":"5badef50-b23b-4032-ae15-64733ce82e70","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:46:31.731Z","rendered":[{"content":"<system-reminder>\n<total_tokens>14791690 tokens left</total_tokens>\n</system-reminder>"}],"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"5badef50-b23b-4032-ae15-64733ce82e70","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCk44S8aBzV6NkgnA3nB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01F9BYTvhpLuwTAQhbRdXu39","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"docs/book/src/operations/observability.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"## Tracing\"\nnew = '''## Structured (JSON) logs\n\n`--log-format json` (or `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT=json`) renders every log record as\none JSON object per line on stderr, so a k8s / ECS / Nomad log pipeline can\ningest it without grok or regex:\n\n```console\n$ faucet run --log-format json pipeline.yaml\n{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-19T10:02:11.481Z\",\"level\":\"INFO\",\"target\":\"faucet_cli::executor\",\"pipeline\":\"orders\",\"row\":\"contact\",\"records_written\":4821,\"message\":\"row completed\"}\n```\n\nThe span fields faucet already records — `pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`,\n`connector`, error `kind` — arrive as fields rather than being rendered into\nthe message, so they are filterable at the collector.\n\nTwo things follow from \"every line is one object\":\n\n- Under `json` the end-of-run human status block, per-row timing table, and\n  peak-RSS line are not printed; the same numbers leave as structured events\n  (`pipeline completed`, `row completed`, `process peak rss`).\n- `faucet mcp` keeps logs on stderr under either format, because stdout carries\n  the JSON-RPC stream and two JSON streams on one pipe would corrupt it.\n\nSecret redaction is unaffected: it operates on the serialized bytes, so a\nresolved `${vault:…}` value appearing in a field is still scrubbed.\n\n`text` remains the default.\n\n## Tracing'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\np.write_text(s); print(\"observability.md updated\")\nPY\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\nCARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC=$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/rustc \\\ncargo clippy -p faucet-cli --features \"serve,serve-history-sqlite,templates,mcp,schedule\" --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error|^warning\" -A6 | head -20\necho CLIPPY_DONE","description":"Document in observability guide and run clippy","timeout":2400000,"run_in_background":true},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_read_input_tokens":849334,"output_tokens":966,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":966,"cache_read_input_tokens":849334,"cache_creation_input_tokens":227,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":227},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_01F9BYTvhpLuwTAQhbRdXu39":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream && python3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"docs/book/src/operations/observability.md\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"## Tracing\"\nnew = '''## Structured (JSON) logs\n\n`--log-format json` (or `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT=json`) renders every log record as\none JSON object per line on stderr, so a k8s / ECS / Nomad log pipeline can\ningest it without grok or regex:\n\n```console\n$ faucet run --log-format json pipeline.yaml\n{\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-19T10:02:11.481Z\",\"level\":\"INFO\",\"target\":\"faucet_cli::executor\",\"pipeline\":\"orders\",\"row\":\"contact\",\"records_written\":4821,\"message\":\"row completed\"}\n```\n\nThe span fields faucet already records — `pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`,\n`connector`, error `kind` — arrive as fields rather than being rendered into\nthe message, so they are filterable at the collector.\n\nTwo things follow from \"every line is one object\":\n\n- Under `json` the end-of-run human status block, per-row timing table, and\n  peak-RSS line are not printed; the same numbers leave as structured events\n  (`pipeline completed`, `row completed`, `process peak rss`).\n- `faucet mcp` keeps logs on stderr under either format, because stdout carries\n  the JSON-RPC stream and two JSON streams on one pipe would corrupt it.\n\nSecret redaction is unaffected: it operates on the serialized bytes, so a\nresolved `${vault:…}` value appearing in a field is still scrubbed.\n\n`text` remains the default.\n\n## Tracing'''\nassert old in s\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\np.write_text(s); print(\"observability.md updated\")\nPY\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\nCARGO_INCREMENTAL=0 RUSTC=$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin/rustc \\\ncargo clippy -p faucet-cli --features \"serve,serve-history-sqlite,templates,mcp,schedule\" --all-targets -- -D warnings 2>&1 | grep -E \"^error|^warning\" -A6 | head -20\necho CLIPPY_DONE","timeout":2400000,"run_in_background":true,"description":"Document in observability guide and run clippy"}},"wireIngestContext":{"toolu_01F9BYTvhpLuwTAQhbRdXu39":{"cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCk43Juk3mrsYsacdXxo","type":"assistant","uuid":"98a37df8-9307-423b-a525-ffc1a8bfb35b","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:46:43.727Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
