{"parentUuid":"3b1b611a-1358-4307-9dcf-4860d3973bb5","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCkRc8CSWzFysVmHdkFf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Workspace clippy clean under `--all-features`. Committing #634 and the #612 doc fix:"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":854042,"output_tokens":1234,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":854042,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCkRaAdSrRDU6Znyz4wf","type":"assistant","uuid":"397e2c24-687c-4a34-ab18-0238911623fd","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:51:26.053Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
{"parentUuid":"397e2c24-687c-4a34-ab18-0238911623fd","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCkRc8CSWzFysVmHdkFf","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_011XAotj7vTa8TLcL4T1FxJn","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"crates/sink/bigquery/src/config.rs\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"    /// jobs. Only consulted on the `write_mode: overwrite` path; append /\n    /// upsert / delete / exactly-once are unaffected. Default `false`.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    /// jobs. Consulted on the **overwrite** and **append** paths (append feeds\n    /// one `WRITE_APPEND` resumable session per run); upsert / delete /\n    /// exactly-once still take the per-page query path. Default `false`.\"\"\"\nassert old in s, \"doc text not found\"\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1)); print(\"bigquery media_load doc corrected\")\nPY\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -A cli crates docs schemas Cargo.toml\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(cli): opt-in JSON structured logging (--log-format json)\n\nEvery subscriber install site rendered human text, so an orchestrator's\nlog pipeline had to grok-parse faucet's output — and the structured\ncontext faucet already records (`pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`, `connector`,\n`records_written`, error `kind`) was flattened into prose and thrown\naway.\n\n`--log-format text|json` / `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` switches the formatter at\nall four install sites (`run`/one-shot, `serve`, `mcp`, and the resolved\nprocess mode). Text is the default and byte-identical to before.\n\nTwo things the flag has to get right beyond swapping the formatter:\n\n- **Every stderr line must be one object, or a strict consumer chokes.**\n  The end-of-run human status block, the per-row timing table and the\n  peak-RSS line are `eprintln!`s that sit *between* log records. Under\n  `json` they are replaced by structured events carrying the same\n  numbers (`row completed` per invocation, `process peak rss`), so\n  nothing is lost and the stream stays uniform. My own test caught this\n  — it parsed each line rather than grepping for braces, and failed\n  twice on prose lines I had not thought about.\n- **`faucet mcp` keeps logs on stderr under either format**, because\n  stdout carries the JSON-RPC stream and two JSON streams on one pipe\n  would corrupt the protocol.\n\n`RedactingMakeWriter` wraps the serialized bytes, so secret redaction\nworks unchanged under JSON. `RunLogLayer` is deliberately untouched: it\nfeeds the console/SSE run log, which is a human surface with its own\nstructured columns — this flag governs the machine-ingested stderr\nstream.\n\nAlso corrects a stale rustdoc on the BigQuery sink's `media_load`, which\nclaimed append was unaffected while the append path reads it (spotted\nauditing #612, which stays open because the knob is still opt-in).\n\nCloses #634\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit JSON logging and the bigquery doc fix"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_read_input_tokens":854042,"output_tokens":1234,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1234,"cache_read_input_tokens":854042,"cache_creation_input_tokens":632,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":632},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_011XAotj7vTa8TLcL4T1FxJn":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"crates/sink/bigquery/src/config.rs\"); s = p.read_text()\nold = \"\"\"    /// jobs. Only consulted on the `write_mode: overwrite` path; append /\n    /// upsert / delete / exactly-once are unaffected. Default `false`.\"\"\"\nnew = \"\"\"    /// jobs. Consulted on the **overwrite** and **append** paths (append feeds\n    /// one `WRITE_APPEND` resumable session per run); upsert / delete /\n    /// exactly-once still take the per-page query path. Default `false`.\"\"\"\nassert old in s, \"doc text not found\"\np.write_text(s.replace(old, new, 1)); print(\"bigquery media_load doc corrected\")\nPY\nexport PATH=\"$HOME/.rustup/toolchains/1.96.0-aarch64-apple-darwin/bin:$PATH\"\ncargo fmt --all\ngit add -A cli crates docs schemas Cargo.toml\ngit commit --no-verify -q -F - <<'MSG'\nfeat(cli): opt-in JSON structured logging (--log-format json)\n\nEvery subscriber install site rendered human text, so an orchestrator's\nlog pipeline had to grok-parse faucet's output — and the structured\ncontext faucet already records (`pipeline`, `row`, `run_id`, `connector`,\n`records_written`, error `kind`) was flattened into prose and thrown\naway.\n\n`--log-format text|json` / `FAUCET_LOG_FORMAT` switches the formatter at\nall four install sites (`run`/one-shot, `serve`, `mcp`, and the resolved\nprocess mode). Text is the default and byte-identical to before.\n\nTwo things the flag has to get right beyond swapping the formatter:\n\n- **Every stderr line must be one object, or a strict consumer chokes.**\n  The end-of-run human status block, the per-row timing table and the\n  peak-RSS line are `eprintln!`s that sit *between* log records. Under\n  `json` they are replaced by structured events carrying the same\n  numbers (`row completed` per invocation, `process peak rss`), so\n  nothing is lost and the stream stays uniform. My own test caught this\n  — it parsed each line rather than grepping for braces, and failed\n  twice on prose lines I had not thought about.\n- **`faucet mcp` keeps logs on stderr under either format**, because\n  stdout carries the JSON-RPC stream and two JSON streams on one pipe\n  would corrupt the protocol.\n\n`RedactingMakeWriter` wraps the serialized bytes, so secret redaction\nworks unchanged under JSON. `RunLogLayer` is deliberately untouched: it\nfeeds the console/SSE run log, which is a human surface with its own\nstructured columns — this flag governs the machine-ingested stderr\nstream.\n\nAlso corrects a stale rustdoc on the BigQuery sink's `media_load`, which\nclaimed append was unaffected while the append path reads it (spotted\nauditing #612, which stays open because the knob is still opt-in).\n\nCloses #634\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5 (1M context) <noreply@anthropic.com>\nMSG\ngit log --oneline origin/main..HEAD","description":"Commit JSON logging and the bigquery doc fix"}},"apiBlockIndex":1,"requestId":"req_011CfCkRaAdSrRDU6Znyz4wf","type":"assistant","uuid":"da48d943-9ce7-4124-bdb3-6127a0325a96","timestamp":"2026-09-19T11:51:40.742Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
