{"parentUuid":"5a41a43b-4e6a-4561-83c0-dfaf8b597234","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCmLFsnFV1yLuBUzyvEB","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_014mJbV6uWqijWy7BubweEWk","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && /opt/homebrew/bin/gh pr merge 667 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"fix: SQLite write-lock contention, topology cooldown, LPT dispatch, JSON logs (issue audit #580+) (#667)\" \\\n  --body \"$(printf '%s' \"An audit of every open issue from #580 onwards, plus fixes for the four that were real and tractable.\n\n#666 — concurrent template_register failed with 'database is locked'. WAL and a 5s busy_timeout were already set, and retrying the commit changed nothing; the error code (517, SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT) showed the cause: sqlx's deferred BEGIN makes the read-max-then-insert transaction upgrade its lock, and WAL refuses that immediately rather than waiting on busy_timeout. impl_sql_history! now takes the begin statement per dialect — SQLite BEGIN IMMEDIATE, Postgres unchanged. Measured at 64 concurrent registers: 5/5 runs failed before, 0/10 after.\n\n#658 — NodeReport.error was a rendered string, so a topology node that tripped the circuit breaker got no scheduler cooldown while the same matrix failure did. Adds a typed NodeErrorKind classified where the FaucetError is still intact; classification never comes from message text.\n\n#644 — execution.schedule: lpt dispatches the heaviest ready rows first (declared stays default), ranked by a weight faucet discover estimates as rows x row width. Ties and unweighted rows keep declaration order.\n\n#634 — --log-format json at all four subscriber sites, with the end-of-run human status block replaced by structured events so every stderr line is one object; faucet mcp keeps logs on stderr.\n\nClosed as already implemented after verification: #614, #632, #637, #628, and #615/#625 as duplicates of #626. Left open with findings: #612 (capability landed but media_load still defaults to false), #624 (one of three parts done).\n\nCloses #666\nCloses #658\nCloses #644\nCloses #634\")\" 2>&1 | tail -2\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh pr view 667 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest != null'","description":"Arm auto-merge on PR 667","timeout":300000},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2464,"cache_read_input_tokens":858870,"output_tokens":961,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2464,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":961,"cache_read_input_tokens":858870,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2464,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2464},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_014mJbV6uWqijWy7BubweEWk":{"command":"cd /Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh auth switch --user PawanSikawat >/dev/null 2>&1 && /opt/homebrew/bin/gh pr merge 667 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --auto --squash --delete-branch \\\n  --subject \"fix: SQLite write-lock contention, topology cooldown, LPT dispatch, JSON logs (issue audit #580+) (#667)\" \\\n  --body \"$(printf '%s' \"An audit of every open issue from #580 onwards, plus fixes for the four that were real and tractable.\n\n#666 — concurrent template_register failed with 'database is locked'. WAL and a 5s busy_timeout were already set, and retrying the commit changed nothing; the error code (517, SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT) showed the cause: sqlx's deferred BEGIN makes the read-max-then-insert transaction upgrade its lock, and WAL refuses that immediately rather than waiting on busy_timeout. impl_sql_history! now takes the begin statement per dialect — SQLite BEGIN IMMEDIATE, Postgres unchanged. Measured at 64 concurrent registers: 5/5 runs failed before, 0/10 after.\n\n#658 — NodeReport.error was a rendered string, so a topology node that tripped the circuit breaker got no scheduler cooldown while the same matrix failure did. Adds a typed NodeErrorKind classified where the FaucetError is still intact; classification never comes from message text.\n\n#644 — execution.schedule: lpt dispatches the heaviest ready rows first (declared stays default), ranked by a weight faucet discover estimates as rows x row width. Ties and unweighted rows keep declaration order.\n\n#634 — --log-format json at all four subscriber sites, with the end-of-run human status block replaced by structured events so every stderr line is one object; faucet mcp keeps logs on stderr.\n\nClosed as already implemented after verification: #614, #632, #637, #628, and #615/#625 as duplicates of #626. Left open with findings: #612 (capability landed but media_load still defaults to false), #624 (one of three parts done).\n\nCloses #666\nCloses #658\nCloses #644\nCloses #634\")\" 2>&1 | tail -2\n/opt/homebrew/bin/gh pr view 667 --repo faucet-hq/faucet-stream --json autoMergeRequest --jq '.autoMergeRequest != null'","timeout":300000,"description":"Arm auto-merge on PR 667"}},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCmLEMjgK2FDCiLXAE9B","type":"assistant","uuid":"7418b2bf-bb88-437f-8494-af2f8ff20282","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:03:32.027Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.2