{"type":"pr-link","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","prNumber":667,"prUrl":"https://github.com/faucet-hq/faucet-stream/pull/667","prRepository":"faucet-hq/faucet-stream","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:03:47.821Z"}
{"parentUuid":"ec2b7ff4-b4c9-41b7-b4a6-ba4bc794ebf8","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCmNSGeiozvqg9sXDKQH","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I audited all 33 issues from #580 onwards against the code. **PR #667** is up with the fixes; auto-merge is armed.\n\n## Already solved — closed with evidence\n\nYour instinct was right, five were done:\n\n| Issue | What I verified |\n|---|---|\n| **#614** BigQuery streaming load | Resumable session across pages, `WRITE_TRUNCATE`/`WRITE_APPEND`, finalized in `flush()` + 5 tests |\n| **#632** `keys_case` collisions | `KeyCollision::{Error,Suffix}`, default still fail-loud, 5 tests incl. order-stability |\n| **#637** button tiers | `btn-warn` on Purge/Cancel/Discard/Deprecate, `btn-danger` on every Delete — exactly the spec |\n| **#628** adaptive poll backoff | `next_poll_delay` doubling to the interval cap + unit and wiremock tests |\n| **#615, #625** | Duplicates of **#626** — byte-identical titles, same 3.96 GB evidence |\n\n**On surety:** my first automated sweep gave a false negative on #628 (it searched a file that doesn't exist), so I re-verified every \"absent\" verdict with multiple search terms and confirmed the rest by reading code and tests. Two more nuances the careful pass caught: **#612's** load path exists but `media_load` still defaults to `false`, so the reported symptom reproduces out of the box — I left it open with that finding rather than closing it on the capability alone; **#624** has one of three parts done. Both have detailed comments posted.\n\n## Fixed in #667\n\n- **#666** — my own filed diagnosis was wrong *twice*. WAL and a 5 s busy timeout were already set, and retrying the commit changed nothing. The error code told the truth: **517 = `SQLITE_BUSY_SNAPSHOT`** — sqlx's deferred `BEGIN` forces a read→write lock upgrade that WAL refuses instantly, never consulting `busy_timeout`. `BEGIN IMMEDIATE` fixes it: **5/5 runs failed before, 0/10 after** at 64 concurrent writers.\n- **#658** — topology nodes now carry a typed failure kind, so a tripped breaker earns the same scheduler cooldown a matrix row gets.\n- **#644** — `execution.schedule: lpt`, ranked by a weight `faucet discover` estimates as rows × row *width* (bytes, not rows — that's the mis-ordering that idled 6 of 8 slots).\n- **#634** — `--log-format json`; my test parses each line rather than grepping, which caught two prose `eprintln!`s that would have broken a strict consumer.\n\n## What I did not do, plainly\n\n\"Solve all of them in a single PR\" isn't achievable for what's left, and I'd rather say so than quietly ship something thin: **#583** is a white-paper *writing* programme, **#589**/**#591** are explicitly RFC-gated, **#604** is 4 formats × 8 connectors, **#580** is auto-create across ~10 sinks, **#635**/**#636** are Arrow re-architectures. Also untouched: #608, #610, #617, #618, #621, #626, #629, #638, #646, #648, #654. If you want the next batch, I'd take **#626** first — it's tier-1 and it's the 3.96 GB memory ceiling that blocks a real workload.\n\nOne housekeeping note: disk hit 100% again mid-run, and `cargo sweep --time 1` reclaimed **108 GB** without a full clean — worth remembering over `cargo clean`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"end_turn","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_read_input_tokens":862325,"output_tokens":1214,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":0},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1214,"cache_read_input_tokens":862325,"cache_creation_input_tokens":561,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":561},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"apiBlockIndex":0,"requestId":"req_011CfCmNQqaV6EsFVErMn4NQ","type":"assistant","uuid":"502def16-47cd-4fd2-97b4-f0ce5a9cc9df","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:04:05.897Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","version":"2.1.267","gitBranch":"fix/audit-batch-580","slug":"linear-noodling-leaf"}
