{"parentUuid":"a9e986af-20a8-4232-a366-c8f4031acb30","isSidechain":false,"message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011CfCp9ee38w7eHDKwMTNFi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_018bB7pu4YKtaejLKi7RW1oa","name":"Bash","input":{"command":"cat > \"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema.md\" <<'MD'\n---\nname: reference-rustdoc-edits-change-committed-schema\ndescription: \"Editing a connector config field's doc comment invalidates schemas/faucet.schema.json — descriptions come from rustdoc\"\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\n`schemas/faucet.schema.json` embeds every config field's **rustdoc** as its\n`description`, so editing a doc comment on any `#[derive(JsonSchema)]` config\nfield — even a pure typo/accuracy fix touching no code — makes the committed\nschema stale and fails the required `Test` **and** `Coverage` jobs via\n`committed_schema_covers_current_build`.\n\nBit twice in one session (2026-09-19): once when a kafka `headers_path` doc\nrewrite landed on a different branch than the schema update (PR #664), once\nwhen a one-line accuracy fix to BigQuery's `media_load` doc shipped without\nregenerating (PR #667).\n\n**How to apply:** after touching *any* config doc comment, regenerate and\ndiff before pushing:\n\n```\ncargo build -p faucet-cli --all-features\n./target/debug/faucet schema config > /tmp/regen.json\n# then splice the changed nodes into schemas/faucet.schema.json —\n# a wholesale copy reorders every key (serde_json's map type flips with\n# feature unification) and buries the real change in ~20k lines of churn\n```\n\nVerify with a recursive semantic diff showing zero drift, then run\n`cargo test -p faucet-cli --all-features --test schema_config`.\nSee [[reference_committed_config_json_schema]].\nMD\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/MEMORY.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nline = \"- [Rustdoc edits change the committed schema](reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema.md) — a config field's doc comment IS its schema `description`; edit one and regenerate schemas/faucet.schema.json or Test+Coverage go red.\\n\"\nif \"reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema\" not in s:\n    p.write_text(s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + line)\nprint(\"memory saved\")\nPY","description":"Save the rustdoc/schema lesson"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"container":null,"stop_reason":"tool_use","stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_read_input_tokens":867833,"output_tokens":1126,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":125},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":1126,"cache_read_input_tokens":867833,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1347,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":1347},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"wireToolInputs":{"toolu_018bB7pu4YKtaejLKi7RW1oa":{"command":"cat > \"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema.md\" <<'MD'\n---\nname: reference-rustdoc-edits-change-committed-schema\ndescription: \"Editing a connector config field's doc comment invalidates schemas/faucet.schema.json — descriptions come from rustdoc\"\nmetadata:\n  type: reference\n---\n\n`schemas/faucet.schema.json` embeds every config field's **rustdoc** as its\n`description`, so editing a doc comment on any `#[derive(JsonSchema)]` config\nfield — even a pure typo/accuracy fix touching no code — makes the committed\nschema stale and fails the required `Test` **and** `Coverage` jobs via\n`committed_schema_covers_current_build`.\n\nBit twice in one session (2026-09-19): once when a kafka `headers_path` doc\nrewrite landed on a different branch than the schema update (PR #664), once\nwhen a one-line accuracy fix to BigQuery's `media_load` doc shipped without\nregenerating (PR #667).\n\n**How to apply:** after touching *any* config doc comment, regenerate and\ndiff before pushing:\n\n```\ncargo build -p faucet-cli --all-features\n./target/debug/faucet schema config > /tmp/regen.json\n# then splice the changed nodes into schemas/faucet.schema.json —\n# a wholesale copy reorders every key (serde_json's map type flips with\n# feature unification) and buries the real change in ~20k lines of churn\n```\n\nVerify with a recursive semantic diff showing zero drift, then run\n`cargo test -p faucet-cli --all-features --test schema_config`.\nSee [[reference_committed_config_json_schema]].\nMD\npython3 - <<'PY'\nimport pathlib\np = pathlib.Path(\"/Users/c-sikawats/.claude/projects/-Users-c-sikawats-Documents-GitHub-Personal-faucet-stream/memory/MEMORY.md\")\ns = p.read_text()\nline = \"- [Rustdoc edits change the committed schema](reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema.md) — a config field's doc comment IS its schema `description`; edit one and regenerate schemas/faucet.schema.json or Test+Coverage go red.\\n\"\nif \"reference_rustdoc_edits_change_committed_schema\" not in s:\n    p.write_text(s.rstrip(\"\\n\") + \"\\n\" + line)\nprint(\"memory saved\")\nPY","description":"Save the rustdoc/schema lesson"}},"apiBlockIndex":2,"requestId":"req_011CfCp9cNra2FutHJufYQzc","type":"assistant","uuid":"db9ae49f-7b5a-4ad1-9ade-f530e6d830fb","timestamp":"2026-09-19T12:40:30.073Z","effort":"high","perTurnEffort":null,"session_id":"55398c64-7c65-40db-9b68-886111a86d7f","userType":"external","entrypoint":"cli","cwd":"/Users/c-sikawats/Documents/GitHub/Personal/faucet-stream","sessionId":"55398c64